phy_mech_001,Physics,Mechanics,Newton's Laws,A force of 10 N acts on a 2 kg body. What is the acceleration?,2 m/s²,4 m/s²,5 m/s²,10 m/s²,C,Using Newton’s 2nd law a=F/m=10/2=5 m/s².
phy_mech_002,Physics,Mechanics,Inertia,If the net force on a body is zero the body will?,Stop immediately,Remain at rest or move uniformly,Accelerate,Move in circles,B,Newton’s 1st law states that a body remains in rest or uniform motion if net force is zero.
phy_mech_003,Physics,Mechanics,Projectile Motion,Maximum range of a projectile occurs at angle?,30°,45°,60°,90°,B,Range is maximum at 45° when sin2θ=1.
phy_mech_004,Physics,Mechanics,Work & Energy,Work done against gravity in raising 5 kg mass to 2 m?,50 J,100 J,25 J,10 J,A,W=mgh=5×10×2=100 J (approx).
phy_mech_005,Physics,Mechanics,Momentum,Which quantity is conserved in an isolated system?,Energy only,Momentum only,Both energy and momentum,Mass only,C,In an isolated system both linear momentum and energy are conserved.
phy_mech_006,Physics,Mechanics,Circular Motion,If a car moves with constant speed around a circular track which quantity changes?,Speed,Velocity,Acceleration,Displacement,B,Velocity changes direction continuously in circular motion.
phy_mech_007,Physics,Mechanics,Friction,The coefficient of friction depends on?,Nature of surfaces,Area of contact,Mass,Acceleration,A,Friction coefficient depends only on the nature of contacting surfaces.
