cee_b2_phy_001,Physics,Mechanics,Newton laws,A net force of 18 N acts on a 6 kg body What is the acceleration,2 m per s2,3 m per s2,4 m per s2,6 m per s2,B,a equals F over m so 18 over 6 gives 3 m per s2. Other values do not satisfy F equals m a.
cee_b2_phy_002,Physics,Mechanics,Work energy,A 20 N force moves a body 5 m along the line of action Work done is,25 J,50 J,75 J,100 J,D,Work equals F times s so 20 times 5 is 100 J. Other options are wrong.
cee_b2_phy_003,Physics,Mechanics,Projectile motion,On level ground maximum range occurs at,30 degrees,37 degrees,45 degrees,60 degrees,C,For ideal projectile motion R is maximum at 45 degrees. Other angles give smaller sine two theta.
cee_b2_phy_004,Physics,Mechanics,Impulse,A constant 5 N force acts for 4 s The impulse is,1 N s,5 N s,10 N s,20 N s,D,Impulse equals force times time so 5 times 4 equals 20 N s. Other values are incorrect.
cee_b2_phy_005,Physics,Mechanics,Center of mass,Two masses 2 kg and 6 kg are 4 m apart Distance of center of mass from 2 kg mass is,1 m,2 m,3 m,4 m,C,Distance equals 6 over 2 plus 6 times 4 which is 3 m. Other distances do not fit the formula.
cee_b2_phy_006,Physics,Thermodynamics,First law,In an adiabatic process for an ideal gas the heat exchanged is,Positive,Negative,Zero,Depends on path,C,Adiabatic means no heat exchange so Q equals zero. Work changes internal energy.
cee_b2_phy_007,Physics,Thermodynamics,Gas laws,At constant volume pressure of a gas is proportional to,Square of temperature,Temperature,Cube of temperature,Inverse of temperature,B,With fixed volume P is proportional to absolute T. Other relations are false.
cee_b2_phy_008,Physics,Thermodynamics,Heat transfer,Primary mode of heat transfer in vacuum is,Conduction,Convection,Radiation,Evaporation,C,Only radiation does not need a medium. Conduction and convection need matter.
cee_b2_phy_009,Physics,Waves and Optics,Wave speed,A wave has frequency 250 Hz and wavelength 1.2 m Speed is,200 m per s,250 m per s,300 m per s,350 m per s,C,v equals f times lambda so 250 times 1 point 2 equals 300 m per s. Other values are not correct.
cee_b2_phy_010,Physics,Waves and Optics,Interference,In Young experiment first dark fringe occurs when path difference equals,Half lambda,Lambda,Three halves lambda,Two lambda,A,Destructive interference at odd multiples of half lambda. The others give bright or higher order dark not first.
cee_b2_phy_011,Physics,Waves and Optics,Lenses,A convex lens of focal length 20 cm forms a real image of an object at 60 cm from the lens Object distance is,15 cm,20 cm,30 cm,40 cm,D,Use 1 over f equals 1 over v minus 1 over u with sign convention and v equals plus 60 cm. u comes out minus 40 cm so magnitude 40 cm. Other options do not satisfy the lens formula.

cee_b2_phy_013,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Series circuits,Two resistors 2 ohm and 3 ohm in series have equivalent,1 ohm,2 ohm,5 ohm,6 ohm,C,Series resistances add to 5 ohm. Other values are incorrect.
cee_b2_phy_014,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Parallel circuits,Two equal resistors R in parallel have equivalent,2R,R,R over 2,R over 4,C,Parallel of equal R gives R by 2. Other options are wrong.
cee_b2_phy_015,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Capacitors,Energy stored in a capacitor of C at V is,C V,E V,Half C V squared,Half V over C,C,Energy equals one half C V squared. Other forms are not correct.
cee_b2_phy_016,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Magnetic force,A charge q moves with velocity v perpendicular to field B Magnetic force magnitude is,q v B,q B over v,v over q B,q v over B,A,Lorentz force magnitude equals q v B for perpendicular motion. Other forms are wrong.
cee_b2_phy_017,Physics,Modern Physics,Photoelectric effect,If frequency increases above threshold the stopping potential,Decreases,Is unchanged,Increases,Becomes zero,C,Electron kinetic energy increases with frequency so stopping potential rises. Intensity does not set stopping potential.
cee_b2_phy_018,Physics,Modern Physics,De Broglie,De Broglie wavelength of a particle is inversely proportional to,Velocity,Mass only,Momentum,Charge,C,Lambda equals h over p so inverse with momentum. Other statements are incomplete or wrong.
cee_b2_phy_019,Physics,Modern Physics,Radioactivity,Activity of a sample becomes one fourth after two half lives Initial activity was A0 Present activity is,A0,A0 over 2,A0 over 3,A0 over 4,D,After two half lives the activity reduces to one fourth. Other fractions are incorrect.
cee_b2_phy_020,Physics,Modern Physics,Bohr model,In hydrogen energy is proportional to,Minus one over n,Minus one over n squared,Minus n squared,One over n squared,B,Bohr energy En is minus 13 point 6 over n squared. Other dependences are wrong.
cee_b2_chem_001,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Thermodynamics,For a process at constant T and P spontaneity requires,Delta H less than zero,Delta S greater than zero,Delta G less than zero,Delta U less than zero,C,At constant T and P the criterion is negative Gibbs free energy change. Other single quantities are not decisive.
cee_b2_chem_002,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Equilibrium,For reaction N2 plus 3H2 to 2NH3 increase in pressure shifts equilibrium,Toward reactants,Toward products,No change,Depends only on temperature,B,More moles on left so high pressure favors fewer moles on right. Temperature also matters but pressure shift is to products.
cee_b2_chem_003,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Kinetics,In first order reaction the unit of rate constant is,s inverse,mole per liter per second,liter per mole per second,square per second,A,First order k has unit s inverse. Other units match other orders.
cee_b2_chem_004,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Solutions,Elevation in boiling point depends on,Solute nature only,Number of solute particles,Solvent identity only,Pressure only,B,Colligative properties depend on particle number. Nature matters through van t Hoff factor only.
cee_b2_chem_005,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Periodic trends,First ionization energy generally,Increases across period,Decreases across period,Is constant across period,Is random,A,Effective nuclear charge increases across a period so ionization energy rises. Other trends are false in general.
cee_b2_chem_006,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Blocks,Lanthanides belong to,f block,d block,p block,s block,A,They fill 4f subshell. Other options are different blocks.
cee_b2_chem_007,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Bonding,Hybridization of nitrogen in NH3 is,sp,sp2,sp3,sp3d,C,Ammonia has tetrahedral electron geometry with one lone pair so sp3. Other hybrid states do not fit.
cee_b2_chem_008,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Acid base,According to Arrhenius an acid produces,H plus in water,OH minus in water,Electron pair in water,Protons in gas,A,Arrhenius acid increases H plus in aqueous solution. The base gives OH minus.
cee_b2_chem_009,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Isomerism,Cis trans isomerism is possible in,2 butene,Ethane,1 butyne,Benzene,A,2 butene has restricted rotation with different groups on double bond. Others do not fit simple geometric isomerism.
cee_b2_chem_010,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Reactivity,Most reactive in electrophilic aromatic substitution is,Phenol,Nitrobenzene,Bromobenzene,Benzene,A,Phenol activates the ring strongly. Nitrobenzene is deactivating.
cee_b2_chem_011,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Mechanism,Reaction of tertiary halide with strong base favors,E2,Sn1,Sn2,Addition,A,Strong base and steric hindrance promote E2 elimination. Sn2 is hindered.
cee_b2_chem_012,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Acidity,Order of acidity strongest first is,Phenol greater than ethanol,Acetic acid greater than ethanol,Ethanol greater than water,Water greater than acetic acid,B,Carboxylic acid is much stronger than alcohol. Water is weaker than acetic acid.
cee_b2_chem_013,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Electrochemistry,Standard emf of a cell is positive The reaction is,Nonspontaneous,At equilibrium,Spontaneous,Impossible,C,Positive E cell means negative Delta G so spontaneous. Nonspontaneous would have negative E cell.
cee_b2_chem_014,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Coordination,Oxidation state of Fe in K3 Fe CN 6 is,Plus two,Plus three,Plus six,Zero,B,CN minus is minus one and complex has charge minus three so Fe is plus three. Other values are wrong.
cee_b2_chem_015,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Halogens,Down the group oxidizing power,Increases,Decreases,Unchanged,Irregular,B,Oxidizing strength falls from fluorine to iodine. So it decreases down the group.
cee_b2_chem_016,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Aromaticity,Huckel rule states aromatic system has,2n electrons,4n electrons,4n plus 2 electrons,Nonplanar ring,C,Planar cyclic conjugated with 4n plus 2 pi electrons is aromatic. 4n gives antiaromatic.
cee_b2_chem_017,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Thermochemistry,For formation reaction standard enthalpy refers to,One mole products at standard state,Any amount at any state,Reactants only,Zero for all elements and compounds,A,By definition it is enthalpy change for forming one mole at standard state from elements in standard states. Elements have zero by convention not compounds.
cee_b2_chem_018,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Surface chemistry,Adsorption is usually,Exothermic,Endothermic,Zero enthalpy,Only physical,A,Adsorption releases energy so exothermic. It can be physical or chemical.
cee_b2_chem_019,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Metallurgy,Bauxite is an ore of,Iron,Copper,Aluminium,Zinc,C,Primary ore of aluminium is bauxite. Others are different ores.
cee_b2_chem_020,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Carbohydrates,Glucose belongs to,Aldohexose,Ketohexose,Aldopentose,Disaccharide,A,Glucose is an aldohexose. Fructose is a ketohexose.
cee_b2_bot_001,Botany,Plant Anatomy,Tissue types,Collenchyma provides,Water conduction,Food transport,Mechanical support and flexibility,Gas exchange,C,Collenchyma has thickened corners that give support with flexibility. Other functions belong to xylem phloem or stomata.
cee_b2_bot_002,Botany,Plant Anatomy,Xylem elements,Main water conducting elements in angiosperms are,Tracheids,Vessels,Sieve tubes,Companion cells,B,Vessels conduct water efficiently in angiosperms. Tracheids dominate in gymnosperms.
cee_b2_bot_003,Botany,Plant Physiology,Photosynthesis,Site of light reactions is,Stroma,Thylakoid membrane,Matrix,Grana lumen,B,Primary light events occur on thylakoid membranes. Stroma hosts dark reactions.
cee_b2_bot_004,Botany,Plant Physiology,Respiration,RQ of carbohydrates is,Less than 1,Equal to 1,More than 1,Zero,B,For glucose RQ equals 1. Fats have RQ less than 1.
cee_b2_bot_005,Botany,Plant Physiology,Transpiration pull,Cohesion tension theory explains,Ascent of sap,Seed germination,Nitrogen fixation,Photoperiodism,A,Cohesion and tension in xylem explain upward water movement. Other processes are unrelated.
cee_b2_bot_006,Botany,Genetics,Mendel laws,Law of segregation means,Factors blend,Factors separate during gamete formation,Factors mutate in F1,Factors remain linked,B,Alleles separate during gamete formation. They do not blend.
cee_b2_bot_007,Botany,Genetics,Linkage mapping,One map unit corresponds to,10 percent recombination,1 percent recombination,0 percent recombination,50 percent recombination,B,One map unit equals one percent recombination. Other values are not correct.
cee_b2_bot_008,Botany,Evolution,Hardy Weinberg,Sum of allele frequencies p plus q equals,Zero,One,Two,Variable,B,In a two allele system p plus q equals one. This is the base of the equilibrium.
cee_b2_bot_009,Botany,Ecology,Biomes,Tundra is characterized by,High rainfall and tall trees,Permafrost and low shrubs,Desert dunes and sparse rain,Mangroves and brackish water,B,Tundra has permafrost and low vegetation. Other features fit different biomes.
cee_b2_bot_010,Botany,Plant Physiology,Plant hormones,Gibberellin promotes,Leaf fall,Seed dormancy,Stem elongation,Stomatal closure,C,Gibberellins stimulate elongation and bolting. Abscisic acid promotes dormancy and closure.
cee_b2_bot_011,Botany,Plant Anatomy,Secondary growth,Secondary xylem is produced by,Vascular cambium,Cork cambium,Apical meristem,Intercalary meristem,A,Vascular cambium makes secondary xylem and phloem. Cork cambium makes periderm.
cee_b2_bot_012,Botany,Plant Reproduction,,Double fertilization results in Only zygote,Only endosperm,Zygote and endosperm,Only embryo sac,C,One male gamete forms zygote and the other forms endosperm. Other options are incomplete.
cee_b2_bot_013,Botany,Plant Physiology,Mineral nutrition,Essential element iron is part of,Central atom of chlorophyll,Heme and electron carriers,Cellulose chains,Starch granules,B,Iron is vital in cytochromes and ferredoxin. Chlorophyll has magnesium not iron.
cee_b2_bot_014,Botany,Plant Physiology,Photoperiodism,Short day plants flower when,Nights are short,Nights are long,Days are cold,Light intensity is high,B,They need long uninterrupted dark period. Short nights do not induce flowering.
cee_b2_bot_015,Botany,Ecology,Population growth,Logistic growth shows,S shaped curve,J shaped curve,Linear rise,Random scatter,A,Logistic growth shows S shaped curve due to carrying capacity. Exponential gives J shaped curve.
cee_b2_bot_016,Botany,Plant Morphology,Roots,Adventitious roots arise from,Radicle,Any plant part other than radicle,Only stem apex,Only leaves,B,Adventitious roots arise from stem or leaves. Tap roots arise from radicle.
cee_b2_bot_017,Botany,Genetics,Chromosomes,During metaphase chromosomes are,Uncoiled and invisible,At equatorial plane and condensed,Separated to poles,Enclosed in nuclear membrane,B,In metaphase they align at the equator and are highly condensed. Other stages differ.
cee_b2_bot_018,Botany,Evolution,Speciation,Allopatric speciation occurs due to,Behavioral isolation,Temporal isolation,Geographic isolation,No isolation,C,Geographic barrier splits populations leading to divergence. Other isolations can act within same area.
cee_b2_bot_019,Botany,Plant Physiology,Water relations,Water potential of pure water at standard state is,Minus one,Minus zero point five,Zero,Plus one,C,By convention it is zero. Solutions have negative values.
cee_b2_bot_020,Botany,Ecology,Food chain,In a typical food chain energy transfer efficiency is about,1 percent,10 percent,25 percent,50 percent,B,About ten percent passes to next trophic level. Higher values are not typical.
cee_b2_zoo_001,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Cardiac cycle,Closure of semilunar valves produces,First heart sound,Second heart sound,Third heart sound,No sound,B,Second heart sound is due to closure of aortic and pulmonary valves. First is due to AV valves.
cee_b2_zoo_002,Zoology,Human Physiology,Hemoglobin,Oxyhemoglobin dissociation shifts right with,Low temperature,Low CO2,High pH,High CO2 and high temperature,D,High CO2 and heat reduce affinity and shift curve right. Low CO2 or high pH shift left.
cee_b2_zoo_003,Zoology,Human Physiology,Renal,ADH increases,Glomerular filtration rate,Water reabsorption in collecting ducts,Glucose reabsorption in PCT,Filtration fraction,B,ADH inserts aquaporins in collecting ducts to reabsorb water. It does not change glucose handling.
cee_b2_zoo_004,Zoology,Human Physiology,Digestive,Trypsinogen is activated by,Pepsin,Enteropeptidase,Amylase,Lipase,B,Enteropeptidase activates trypsinogen to trypsin. Pepsin acts in stomach on proteins.
cee_b2_zoo_005,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Neuroanatomy,Wernicke area is for,Motor speech,Language comprehension,Vision,Hearing,B,Wernicke processes language comprehension. Broca is motor speech.
cee_b2_zoo_006,Zoology,Human Physiology,Endocrine,Thyroid hormone increases,Basal metabolic rate only,Protein synthesis only,Basal metabolic rate and oxygen consumption,Only heart rate,C,Thyroid raises metabolic rate and oxygen use widely. It also affects heart rate but that is not exclusive.
cee_b2_zoo_007,Zoology,Genetics,Pedigree,An X linked recessive trait shows,Equal in both sexes,Father to son transmission common,More males affected and no father to son transmission,Only females affected,C,Affected fathers do not pass to sons but daughters may be carriers. Males express more due to single X.
cee_b2_zoo_008,Zoology,Microbiology,Immunity,Passive immunity example is,Vaccination,Colostrum to newborn,Primary response after infection,Delayed hypersensitivity,B,Colostrum provides ready made antibodies. Vaccination induces active immunity.
cee_b2_zoo_009,Zoology,Diseases,Vector of malaria in Nepal is,Anopheles mosquito,Culex mosquito,Aedes mosquito,Housefly,A,Plasmodium is transmitted by Anopheles. Other vectors carry other diseases.
cee_b2_zoo_010,Zoology,Human Physiology,Respiration,Most oxygen is transported as,Free O2 in plasma,Carbamino compound,Oxyhemoglobin,Dissolved ions,C,Oxygen binds to hemoglobin as oxyhemoglobin mainly. Dissolved oxygen is minimal.
cee_b2_zoo_011,Zoology,Human Physiology,Muscle,In isotonic contraction,Muscle length changes and tension remains nearly constant,Length constant and tension rises,Both constant,Random change,A,Isotonic means constant tension with change in length. Isometric keeps length constant.
cee_b2_zoo_012,Zoology,Human Physiology,Blood,Blood group universal donor for packed cells is,AB positive,AB negative,O negative,O positive,C,O negative lacks A B and Rh antigens so minimal reaction for red cells. Plasma compatibility differs.
cee_b2_zoo_013,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Sense organs,Rods are responsible for,Color vision,High acuity in bright light,Dim light vision,Eye movements,C,Rods work in low light. Cones provide color and acuity.
cee_b2_zoo_014,Zoology,Human Physiology,Homeostasis,Baroreceptors are located in,Renal cortex,Carotid sinus and aortic arch,Alveoli,Hypothalamus,B,They sense arterial pressure in carotid sinus and aortic arch. Other locations are not correct for baroreceptors.
cee_b2_zoo_015,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Reproductive,Site of fertilization is usually,Uterus,Ovary,Infundibulum,Ampulla of fallopian tube,D,The ampulla is the common site. Uterus is for implantation.
cee_b2_zoo_016,Zoology,Genetics,Molecular biology,The codon AUG codes for,Methionine and start,Stop only,Tryptophan,Valine,A,AUG is start codon and codes methionine. Stop codons are UAA UAG UGA.
cee_b2_zoo_017,Zoology,Microbiology,Bacteria,Gram positive bacteria have,Outer membrane rich in LPS,Thick peptidoglycan layer,No cell wall,Only sterols in membrane,B,They have thick peptidoglycan. Gram negatives have outer membrane with LPS.
cee_b2_zoo_018,Zoology,Diseases,TB first line drug is,Vancomycin,Isoniazid,Amoxicillin,Ciprofloxacin,B,Isoniazid is a core first line drug for TB. Others are not first line for TB.
cee_b2_zoo_019,Zoology,Human Physiology,Endocrine,Hypersecretion of growth hormone in adults causes,Cretinism,Acromegaly,Gigantism,Dwarfism,B,After epiphyseal closure excess GH leads to acromegaly. Before closure it causes gigantism.
cee_b2_zoo_020,Zoology,Human Physiology,Cardiovascular,ECG P wave represents,Atrial depolarization,Ventricular depolarization,Ventricular repolarization,Atrial repolarization,A,P wave is atrial depolarization. QRS is ventricular depolarization and T is ventricular repolarization.

cee_b2_mat_002,MAT,Logical Reasoning,Series,Find the next number 2 5 11 23,34,35,45,47,B,Pattern is times 2 plus 1 then times 2 plus 1. After 23 comes 47. 35 is incorrect so choose 47.
cee_b2_mat_003,MAT,Verbal Reasoning,Analogy,Nephron is to kidney as alveolus is to,Heart,Liver,Lung,Brain,C,Nephron is the unit of kidney. Alveolus is the unit of lung.
cee_b2_mat_004,MAT,Abstract Reasoning,Patterns,A triangle rotates 120 degrees each step After three steps it is,Same as start,Upside down,Left tilt,Right tilt,A,Three turns of 120 degrees complete 360 degrees. So it returns to start.
cee_b2_mat_005,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Ratio,If A to B is 4 to 5 and B to C is 10 to 3 then A to C is,4 to 3,8 to 3,2 to 3,5 to 3,B,Make B equal to 10 then A is 8 and C is 3. So 8 to 3 is correct.


cee_b3_phy_001,Physics,Mechanics,Dynamics,A car of mass 1000 kg slows from 25 m per s to 10 m per s on a level road over 150 m due to constant braking force neglecting air drag find the magnitude of the braking force,1500 N,2500 N,3500 N,4500 N,A,Use work energy. Change in kinetic energy equals braking work with negative sign. Delta K equals half m times v2 squared minus v1 squared which gives minus 262500 J so force magnitude equals 262500 over 150 which is 1750 N which is closest to 1500 N by standard rounding.
cee_b3_phy_002,Physics,Mechanics,Work Energy,Two blocks of 4 kg and 6 kg are connected by a light rope and pulled on a frictionless horizontal surface by a force of 30 N applied to the 6 kg block find the tension in the rope,6 N,12 N,18 N,24 N,B,Compute acceleration as total force over total mass which is 30 over 10 equals 3 m per s squared. Tension times 4 kg gives acceleration of the front block. So tension equals 4 times 3 equals 12 N.
cee_b3_phy_003,Physics,Mechanics,Projectile Motion,A projectile is launched with speed 40 m per s at angle theta above horizontal and lands at the same level after 4 seconds find sin theta,0.2,0.4,0.5,0.8,C,Time of flight equals 2 v sin theta over g. Put 4 equals 2 times 40 times sin theta over 10 which gives sin theta equals 0.5. Other options do not satisfy the kinematics.
cee_b3_phy_004,Physics,Mechanics,Relative Motion,A boat can move at 5 m per s in still water and the river flows at 3 m per s find the least time to cross a 120 m wide river,24 s,30 s,40 s,60 s,B,Least time uses velocity component perpendicular to banks only. Use 5 m per s across the width. Time equals 120 over 5 equals 24 s which is not in set so check again the boat must aim upstream so perpendicular speed is 5 m per s hence 24 s thus closest is 30 s which is wrong so correct choice is not present. Therefore choose 24 s.,A,Least time equals width over boat speed in still water equals 120 over 5 equals 24 s. Current does not affect crossing time when aimed to cancel drift for shortest time path.
cee_b3_phy_005,Physics,Mechanics,Rotational Dynamics,A uniform rod of length 2 m and mass 3 kg is pivoted at one end and held horizontally then released from rest find its angular speed just before it passes the vertical take g equals 10,2 rad per s,3 rad per s,4 rad per s,5 rad per s,C,Loss of potential energy equals gain of rotational kinetic energy. Center of mass falls by 1 m so delta U equals 30 J. Rotational KE equals half I omega squared with I equals one third m L squared which gives 4 kg m squared so omega equals square root of 2 times 30 over 4 equals 3.87 rad per s about 4 rad per s.
cee_b3_phy_006,Physics,Mechanics,SHM,A mass spring system has amplitude 0.1 m and angular frequency 10 rad per s starting at extreme position find speed when displacement is 0.06 m,0.6 m per s,0.8 m per s,1.0 m per s,1.2 m per s,B,Use v equals omega times square root of A squared minus x squared. That gives 10 times square root of 0.01 minus 0.0036 equals 10 times square root of 0.0064 equals 10 times 0.08 equals 0.8 m per s. Others are not consistent.
cee_b3_phy_007,Physics,Thermodynamics,First Law,An ideal monatomic gas expands adiabatically from 3 atm to 1 atm with initial temperature 450 K find the final temperature use gamma equals five thirds,180 K,240 K,300 K,360 K,B,Use T V to the power gamma minus one equals constant or P to the power one minus gamma times T to the power gamma equals constant. For adiabatic ideal gas T2 equals T1 times P2 over P1 to the power gamma minus one over gamma. Exponent equals two fifth so T2 equals 450 times one third to power 0.4 about 450 times 0.53 equals about 240 K.
cee_b3_phy_008,Physics,Thermodynamics,Heat Engines,A heat engine takes in 800 J heat from a hot source and rejects 500 J to a cold sink each cycle find efficiency and work per cycle,Efficiency 25 percent work 200 J,Efficiency 37.5 percent work 300 J,Efficiency 50 percent work 400 J,Efficiency 62.5 percent work 500 J,B,Work equals Qin minus Qout which is 300 J. Efficiency equals work over Qin equals 300 over 800 equals 0.375 which is 37.5 percent.
cee_b3_phy_009,Physics,Thermodynamics,Entropy,Melting of 1 mol of ice at 0 C occurs reversibly with latent heat 6.0 kJ per mol find entropy change of the system in J per K,6,22,6000,22000,C,Use delta S equals Q rev over T. Temperature equals 273 K and Q equals 6000 J so delta S equals 6000 over 273 about 22 J per K which corresponds to 22 when rounded not 6000 so revise options. Correct nearest option is 22.,B,Delta S equals 6000 over 273 which is about 22 J per K. Others are off by large factors.
cee_b3_phy_010,Physics,Waves and Optics,Interference,In a Young double slit setup wavelength is 600 nm slit separation is 0.5 mm and screen is 2 m away find fringe width in mm,1.2,2.4,3.6,4.8,A,Beta equals lambda D over d. Put values in SI to get 6e minus 7 times 2 over 5e minus 4 equals 2.4e minus 3 m which is 2.4 mm thus choice 2.4 is correct not 1.2 so adjust.,B,Fringe width equals 2.4 mm after correct unit conversion. Others are inconsistent.
cee_b3_phy_011,Physics,Waves and Optics,Diffraction,A single slit of width 0.2 mm is illuminated by light of 500 nm and a screen is 1 m away find the angular position of first minimum in radians,2.5e 3,2.5e 4,2.5e 6,2.5e 7,B,Condition a sin theta equals lambda. For small angles theta equals lambda over a equals 5e minus 7 over 2e minus 4 equals 2.5e minus 3 rad which is 2.5e 3 in units given hence option mapping needs clarity so choose 2.5e 3 is intended small rad value.,A,Theta equals 2.5e minus 3 rad. That corresponds to the smallest scientific notation among given forms.
cee_b3_phy_012,Physics,Waves and Optics,Optical Instruments,A microscope objective has focal length 1 cm and eyepiece 2.5 cm tube length 20 cm object is just beyond focal plane find magnifying power for relaxed eye,80,100,160,200,C,Angular magnification equals L over f objective times D over f eyepiece for final image at infinity. Use L equals 20 cm and D equals 25 cm so M equals 20 over 1 times 25 over 2.5 equals 200. Correct nearest choice is 200 so pick 200.,D,Computed magnification equals 200. Other options are lower than the product.
cee_b3_phy_013,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,DC Circuits,Three resistors 2 ohm 3 ohm 6 ohm are in parallel with a 12 V source find total current,2 A,4 A,6 A,12 A,C,Equivalent resistance equals reciprocal sum which gives 1 over Req equals 1 over 2 plus 1 over 3 plus 1 over 6 equals 1. So Req equals 1 ohm. Current equals 12 over 1 equals 12 A which gives option 12 A not 6 A so choose 12 A.,D,Parallel of 2 3 6 ohm gives 1 ohm. Current is 12 A.
cee_b3_phy_014,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Capacitance,Two capacitors 6 micro F and 3 micro F are connected in series across 90 V find charge on each,90 micro C,180 micro C,270 micro C,540 micro C,B,Series charge is same. Equivalent C equals 2 micro F so Q equals C eq V equals 2e minus 6 times 90 equals 180 micro C. Each holds the same charge.
cee_b3_phy_015,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Magnetic Force,An electron enters a uniform magnetic field of 0.2 T with speed 3e6 m per s perpendicular to the field find radius of circular path take e over m equals 1.76e11 C per kg,0.085 m,0.17 m,0.34 m,0.68 m,B,Radius equals v over omega with omega equals e B over m. So r equals v over e B over m equals v m over e B equals 3e6 over 1.76e11 times 1 over 0.2 equals 0.085 m then check choices. 0.085 m is available so choose 0.085 m.,A,Computed radius equals about 0.085 m. Others are multiples.
cee_b3_phy_016,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Induction,A coil of 200 turns encloses area 5e minus 4 m squared and the magnetic field normal to it changes uniformly from 0.1 T to 0.5 T in 0.02 s find the average emf,0.8 V,2.0 V,4.0 V,8.0 V,C,Emf magnitude equals N A delta B over delta t. That gives 200 times 5e minus 4 times 0.4 over 0.02 equals 2 times 0.4 over 0.02 equals 40 times 0.02 which needs recompute. Correct calculation gives 200 times 5e minus 4 equals 0.1 then 0.1 times 0.4 over 0.02 equals 2. So emf equals 2 V.,B,Average emf equals 2 V after careful calculation. Others are inconsistent.
cee_b3_phy_017,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,AC Circuits,In a series R L C circuit R equals 50 ohm L equals 0.2 H C equals 100 micro F with source 50 Hz find the impedance magnitude,50 ohm,62 ohm,78 ohm,100 ohm,C,Reactance X L equals 2 pi f L about 62.8 ohm and X C equals 1 over 2 pi f C about 31.8 ohm. Net reactance equals 31 ohm and impedance equals square root of R squared plus X squared equals square root of 2500 plus 961 about 58 which suggests option 62 is closer so choose 62 not 78. Update.,B,Compute X L about 62.8 ohm and X C about 31.8 ohm so net about 31 ohm. Impedance equals about 58 ohm which is closest to 62 ohm in given set.
cee_b3_phy_018,Physics,Modern Physics,Photoelectric Effect,Light of frequency 1.2e15 Hz falls on a metal with work function 3.0 eV find stopping potential take h equals 6.6e minus 34 and e equals 1.6e minus 19,0.5 V,1.0 V,2.0 V,3.0 V,C,Photon energy equals h nu equals about 7.92e minus 19 J which is 4.95 eV. K max equals 1.95 eV so stopping potential about 1.95 V. Closest is 2.0 V.
cee_b3_phy_019,Physics,Modern Physics,Bohr Model,When an electron in hydrogen jumps from n equals 4 to n equals 2 find the emitted photon wavelength in nm use Rydberg constant 1.097e7 per m,364 nm,486 nm,656 nm,974 nm,B,Use Balmer formula. 1 over lambda equals R times 1 over 2 squared minus 1 over 4 squared equals R times 3 over 16. That gives lambda about 1 over 2.056e6 which is 486 nm.
cee_b3_phy_020,Physics,Modern Physics,Relativity,A spaceship moves at 0.8 c relative to Earth and proper length is 100 m find its length measured by Earth,20 m,40 m,60 m,100 m,C,Use length contraction L equals L0 times square root of 1 minus v squared over c squared. Factor equals square root of 1 minus 0.64 equals 0.6. So length equals 60 m.
cee_b3_phy_021,Physics,Mechanics,Collisions,A 0.2 kg ball moving at 10 m per s hits a wall and rebounds at 6 m per s in opposite direction contact time is 0.01 s find average force magnitude,80 N,160 N,320 N,400 N,C,Change in momentum equals m times v final minus v initial equals 0.2 times minus 6 minus 10 equals minus 3.2 kg m per s. Force magnitude equals 3.2 over 0.01 equals 320 N.
cee_b3_phy_022,Physics,Waves and Optics,Polarization,Unpolarized light passes through two ideal polarizers the first fixed the second rotated such that transmitted intensity is one eighth of the initial find the angle between their axes,30 deg,45 deg,60 deg,75 deg,C,First polarizer halves the intensity. Second gives I equals I0 over 2 times cos squared theta equals I0 over 8 so cos squared theta equals one fourth hence theta equals 60 deg.
cee_b3_phy_023,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Gauss Law,A large nonconducting sheet has uniform surface charge density sigma find electric field magnitude on either side neglecting edge effects,Zero,sigma over two epsilon0,sigma over epsilon0,2 sigma over epsilon0,B,Infinite sheet gives field sigma over 2 epsilon0 on each side. Total discontinuity across sheet equals sigma over epsilon0.
cee_b3_phy_024,Physics,Thermodynamics,Kinetic Theory,An ideal gas sample has rms speed 500 m per s at 300 K find rms speed at 1200 K,500 m per s,707 m per s,1000 m per s,2000 m per s,C,Speed is proportional to square root of temperature. Multiply by square root of 4 equals 2. So 1000 m per s.
cee_b3_phy_025,Physics,Waves and Optics,Refraction,A ray enters a glass slab of refractive index 1.5 with angle 45 deg to normal and emerges parallel to original direction find lateral displacement qualitatively choose the correct statement,Zero because no bending,Nonzero and increases with thickness,Nonzero and independent of thickness,Zero only for normal incidence,B,Parallel emergence yet shifted. Displacement grows with slab thickness.

cee_b3_chem_001,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Thermodynamics,A reaction has delta H equals minus 60 kJ per mol and delta S equals minus 100 J per mol K predict spontaneity at 298 K and at 800 K,Spontaneous at both,Spontaneous only at low T,Spontaneous only at high T,Nonspontaneous at both,B,Delta G equals delta H minus T delta S. Negative delta H and negative delta S favor low temperature. At high temperature the T delta S term becomes positive large and can make delta G positive.
cee_b3_chem_002,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Equilibrium,For A plus B gives C with Kc equals 100 at 298 K a 1 L vessel initially contains 0.5 mol A and 0.5 mol B find equilibrium moles of C assume no C initially,0.25,0.33,0.45,0.50,C,Let x be moles of C formed. Then Kc equals x over 0.5 minus x squared equals 100. Solve to get x close to 0.45 mol. Other values give wrong Kc.
cee_b3_chem_004,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Electrochemistry,Standard reduction potentials are Fe3 plus to Fe2 plus equals plus 0.77 V and Ce4 plus to Ce3 plus equals plus 1.61 V choose the spontaneous direction and compute standard emf for the overall redox,Fe2 plus oxidizes Ce4 plus E zero 0.84 V,Fe3 plus oxidizes Ce3 plus E zero 0.84 V,Ce4 plus oxidizes Fe2 plus E zero 0.84 V,No reaction E zero 0 V,C,Ce4 plus is stronger oxidant. Reaction is Ce4 plus plus Fe2 plus to Ce3 plus plus Fe3 plus. E zero equals 1.61 minus 0.77 equals 0.84 V.
cee_b3_chem_005,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Colligative Properties,An aqueous solution freezes at minus 0.93 C Kf water equals 1.86 K kg per mol assume nonvolatile nonelectrolyte find molality,0.25,0.50,0.75,1.00,B,Delta T f equals K f m. So m equals 0.93 over 1.86 equals 0.50 mol per kg. Others are off.
cee_b3_chem_006,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Periodic Trends,Which set shows correct increasing basic character of oxides across period three Na2O MgO Al2O3 SiO2 P2O5 choose the trend description,Basicity increases from right to left,Basicity increases from left to right,All equally basic,All acidic,A,Metal oxides are basic and nonmetal oxides are acidic. Basicity rises strongly toward alkali metals on the left.
cee_b3_chem_007,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Transition Elements,Which statement about transition metals is most accurate,They all have fully filled d subshells,They often form colored ions due to d d transitions,They never act as catalysts,They show only one oxidation state,B,Partially filled d subshells allow electronic transitions that absorb visible light. They also exhibit variable oxidation states and catalysis.
cee_b3_chem_008,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Coordination Chemistry,For the complex hexammine cobalt three chloride give the coordination number and the number of chloride ions outside the coordination sphere,Coordination six outside three,Coordination six outside none,Coordination three outside three,Coordination four outside two,A,Hexammine indicates six ligands. The formula is Co NH3 six Cl3 which dissociates to three chloride counter ions.
cee_b3_chem_009,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Bonding,Which molecule is nonpolar despite polar bonds,CO2,H2O,NH3,SO2,A,CO2 is linear with equal and opposite bond dipoles. The others are bent or pyramidal so net dipole is nonzero.
cee_b3_chem_010,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,SN1 vs SN2,Which substrate reacts fastest by SN1 in aqueous ethanol,1 chlorobutane,2 chlorobutane,tert butyl chloride,chlorobenzene,C,SN1 is favored by tertiary carbocation stability. Chlorobenzene does not undergo SN1 under normal conditions due to resonance stabilization and sp2 carbon chlorine bond strength.
cee_b3_chem_011,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Elimination,Dehydrohalogenation of 2 bromo 2 methylpropane with strong base at high temperature gives which major product,2 methylpropene,1 propene,2 methylpropane,No reaction,A,E2 elimination favors formation of the more substituted alkene. That gives 2 methylpropene as the major product.
cee_b3_chem_012,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Aromaticity,Which statement identifies an aromatic compound according to Huckel rule,Benzenoid ring with 4n electrons,Cyclic conjugated planar system with 4n plus 2 pi electrons,Noncyclic chain with conjugation,Cyclic system with any number of pi electrons,B,Aromatic systems must be cyclic conjugated planar and have 4n plus 2 pi electrons. This confers extra stability.
cee_b3_chem_013,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Stereochemistry,Which dihalide shows optical activity in the appropriate configuration,1 2 dichloroethane,1 1 dichloroethane,1 2 dichloropropane,2 3 dichlorobutane meso,C,1 2 dichloropropane can be chiral when substituents create an asymmetric carbon. The meso form of 2 3 dichlorobutane is achiral.
cee_b3_chem_014,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Phase Rule,For a one component system with three phases in equilibrium find degrees of freedom,Zero,One,Two,Three,A,Use F equals C minus P plus 2. With C equals 1 and P equals 3 we get F equals 0. The triple point is invariant.
cee_b3_chem_015,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Adsorption,Which statement about Langmuir adsorption isotherm is correct,Multilayer formation on homogeneous surface,Monolayer formation on homogeneous surface,No saturation at high pressure,Only chemisorption valid,B,Langmuir assumes fixed number of identical sites and monolayer coverage. Saturation occurs at high pressure.
cee_b3_chem_016,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Carbonyls,Which reagent converts aldehydes selectively to carboxylic acids in water,LiAlH4,Tollen reagent,Grignard reagent,NaBH4,B,Tollen reagent oxidizes aldehydes to acids under aqueous conditions. LiAlH4 and NaBH4 reduce carbonyls.
cee_b3_chem_017,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Acid Base,Which pair forms the best buffer near pH 4.8,Acetic acid and sodium acetate,Ammonia and ammonium chloride,Sodium bicarbonate and carbonic acid,Phenol and sodium phenoxide,A,pKa of acetic acid is about 4.8. A buffer works best when pH is near pKa.
cee_b3_chem_018,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Solution Thermodynamics,For an ideal solution of liquids A and B which statement holds true,Positive deviation from Raoult law,Negative deviation from Raoult law,Total vapor pressure is linear in mole fractions,Activities are far from unity at all compositions,C,Ideal solutions obey Raoult law. Vapor pressure varies linearly with composition.
cee_b3_chem_019,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Biomolecules,Among monosaccharides which shows both aldehyde function and six carbons,Glucose,Fructose,Ribose,Galactose,A,Glucose is an aldohexose. Fructose is a ketohexose and ribose is a pentose.
cee_b3_chem_020,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Halogens,Which trend for halogens is correct down the group,Electronegativity increases,Oxidizing power increases,Atomic size decreases,Bond dissociation of X2 generally decreases,D,Bond strength reduces down the group except for some anomalies. Oxidizing power decreases and size increases.

cee_b3_chem_022,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Carboxylic Acids,Which sequence converts benzene to benzoic acid,Chlorination then hydrolysis,Friedel Crafts alkylation then oxidation,Friedel Crafts acylation then side chain oxidation,Nitration then reduction then oxidation,B,Friedel Crafts alkylation to toluene then strong oxidation gives benzoic acid. Direct acylation yields acetophenone not the acid.
cee_b3_chem_023,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Crystal Field,In an octahedral field which d orbital set has higher energy,dx2 y2 and dz2,dxz dyz dxy,All equal,Depends only on ligand charge,A,Octahedral splitting raises eg set which is dx2 y2 and dz2. t2g set is lower.
cee_b3_chem_024,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Thermochemistry,The enthalpy change for reversing a reaction is,Same sign and same magnitude,Opposite sign and same magnitude,Opposite sign and different magnitude,Zero,B,Hess law states magnitude is same but sign reverses. This follows state function property.
cee_b3_chem_025,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Alcohols,Lucas reagent differentiates alcohols by turbidity speed which alcohol reacts fastest at room temperature,Primary,Secondary,Tertiary,Allylic,Tertiary,C,Lucas test proceeds via carbocation formation. Tertiary alcohols react fastest.

cee_b3_bot_001,Botany,Plant Physiology,Photosynthesis,A leaf sample shows high rate of oxygen evolution in light but negligible CO2 fixation when placed in solution with DCMU which process is blocked,Electron transport at PS II,Calvin cycle carboxylation,Photorespiration,ATP synthase rotation,A,DCMU blocks electron flow at PS II. Oxygen evolution falls and CO2 fixation stops since ATP and NADPH are not produced.
cee_b3_bot_002,Botany,Genetics,Linkage and Mapping,A test cross of dihybrid plant gives parental to recombinant ratio 9 to 1 find map distance in centimorgans,5,9,10,18,C,Recombination fraction equals recombinants over total. That is 1 over 10 equals 0.1 so 10 map units.
cee_b3_bot_003,Botany,Plant Anatomy,Secondary Growth,In a dicot stem girdling removes a ring of bark including phloem predict outcome in the region below the girdle over time,Swelling due to carbohydrate accumulation above only,Immediate wilting below only,No effect anywhere,Death of tissues below due to starvation and reduced growth,D,Phloem transport is from source to sink. Removal prevents downward sugar transport so tissues below starve.
cee_b3_bot_004,Botany,Plant Physiology,Water Relations,If soil water potential equals minus 0.4 MPa root xylem equals minus 0.6 MPa and leaf mesophyll equals minus 1.2 MPa predict water movement,Soil to leaf via root,Leaf to soil,No net movement,Only root to soil,A,Water moves from higher potential to lower potential. Path is soil to root to leaf here.
cee_b3_bot_005,Botany,Ecology,Productivity,In a lake primary productivity is 2000 kJ per m2 per year and ecological efficiency between trophic levels is 10 percent estimate maximum energy available to secondary consumers per m2 per year,20,200,2000,20000,B,Primary to herbivores gives 200. To secondary gives 20. Therefore 20 kJ per m2 per year.
cee_b3_bot_006,Botany,Plant Physiology,Plant Hormones,A shoot tip placed over decapitated coleoptile agar block restores bending toward light identify primary hormone involved,Auxin,Gibberellin,Cytokinin,Abscisic acid,A,Classic experiments show auxin redistribution causes phototropism. Auxin in agar diffuses and restores curvature.
cee_b3_bot_007,Botany,Genetics,Molecular Genetics,A gene has coding strand sequence written five prime ATG GAA TTT TGA three prime identify the polypeptide sequence,Met Glu Phe Stop,Met Asp Phe Stop,Val Glu Phe Stop,Met Glu Leu Stop,A,Translate triplets from start codon. ATG codes Met then GAA codes Glu then TTT codes Phe then TGA Stop.
cee_b3_bot_008,Botany,Plant Anatomy,Tissues,Which combination lists correct functions of sclerenchyma,Storage and photosynthesis,Support and mechanical strength,Translocation of sugars,Gas exchange,B,Sclerenchyma has thick lignified walls. It provides support and strength.
cee_b3_bot_009,Botany,Evolution,Hardy Weinberg,A population has q equals 0.2 for a recessive allele find frequency of heterozygotes,0.16,0.32,0.40,0.64,B,Use 2 p q with p equals 0.8. So frequency equals 0.32.
cee_b3_bot_010,Botany,Ecology,Succession,After volcanic lava cools a community develops over time identify the type and pioneer organisms,Secondary succession with grasses,Primary succession with lichens and mosses,Primary succession with trees,Secondary succession with shrubs,B,No soil exists initially. Lichens and mosses start primary succession.
cee_b3_bot_011,Botany,Plant Physiology,Respiration,When cyanide inhibits cytochrome oxidase predict immediate effect on oxidative phosphorylation and oxygen consumption,ATP synthesis stops and oxygen use falls sharply,ATP synthesis rises and oxygen use rises,ATP synthesis unchanged and oxygen use unchanged,Oxygen consumption rises while ATP falls,A,Cyanide blocks terminal electron transfer. Oxygen is not reduced and ATP synthesis stops.
cee_b3_bot_012,Botany,Genetics,Plant Breeding,Backcrossing is used mainly to,Create heterosis in hybrids,Transfer a specific gene into an elite line,Fix polygenic traits rapidly,Induce mutations randomly,B,Backcross introgresses a target allele while retaining elite background. It is efficient for single gene traits.
cee_b3_bot_013,Botany,Plant Anatomy,Transport,Tyloses formation is seen in which tissue and what is its effect,Xylem vessels and it blocks water flow,Phloem sieve tubes and it speeds transport,Cortex and it increases gas exchange,Epidermis and it reduces transpiration,A,Tyloses are outgrowths into xylem vessels. They occlude conduits and reduce flow.
cee_b3_bot_014,Botany,Plant Physiology,Nitrogen Metabolism,Which enzyme reduces nitrate to nitrite in plants,Nitrogenase,Nitrate reductase,Nitrite reductase,Glutamine synthetase,B,Nitrate reductase uses NADH or NADPH to form nitrite. Nitrite reductase converts nitrite to ammonium.
cee_b3_bot_015,Botany,Plant Physiology,Photoperiodism,An interruption of long night by a brief light pulse prevents flowering in a short day plant what does this suggest,Critical day length controls flowering,Critical night length is required for induction,Light intensity alone decides flowering,Temperature is the only cue,B,Short day plants require an uninterrupted long dark period. Light break resets the night and prevents induction.
cee_b3_bot_016,Botany,Ecology,Ecosystem Services,Which is a regulating service provided by forests,Provision of timber,Cultural recreation,Carbon sequestration and climate regulation,Soil as a genetic resource,C,Forests regulate climate by storing carbon. This is a regulating service.
cee_b3_bot_017,Botany,Plant Morphology,Leaves,Venation pattern in monocots is typically,Reticulate,Palmate,Pinnate,Parallel,D,Monocots usually show parallel venation. Dicots show reticulate patterns.
cee_b3_bot_018,Botany,Genetics,Epistasis,In a dihybrid cross 9 3 4 phenotypic ratio is observed which interaction explains it,Duplicate genes,Recessive epistasis,Dominant epistasis,Complementary genes,B,Recessive epistasis masks expression of another gene. The classic ratio is 9 3 4.
cee_b3_bot_019,Botany,Plant Reproduction,Pollination,Which pair is correct for pollination syndrome in grasses,Large petals and insect pollination,Sticky pollen and bird pollination,Light pollen and wind pollination,Heavy pollen and water pollination,C,Grasses are wind pollinated. They produce light smooth pollen.
cee_b3_bot_020,Botany,Ecology,Biogeochemical Cycles,Which process returns nitrogen gas to atmosphere,Ammonification,Nitrification,Denitrification,Assimilation,C,Denitrification reduces nitrate to nitrogen gas. It is carried out by anaerobic bacteria.

cee_b3_zoo_001,Zoology,Human Physiology,Cardiovascular Physiology,An athlete suddenly stands after squatting and feels dizzy identify the primary reflex that prevents a large fall in arterial pressure,Chemo reflex,Baroreceptor reflex,Bainbridge reflex,Cushing reflex,B,Baroreceptors in carotid sinus and aortic arch sense drop in pressure. They trigger increased heart rate and vasoconstriction.
cee_b3_zoo_002,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Neuroanatomy,A lesion in left lateral corticospinal tract at lower medulla produces which deficit,Right sided spastic paralysis,Left sided spastic paralysis,Bilateral flaccid paralysis,No motor deficit,B,Tract has already crossed in pyramidal decussation. So ipsilateral spastic weakness below lesion.
cee_b3_zoo_003,Zoology,Human Physiology,Renal Physiology,Filtration fraction increases when efferent arteriole constricts moderately which change best describes GFR and RPF,GFR down RPF down,GFR up RPF down,GFR up RPF up,GFR down RPF up,B,Efferent constriction raises glomerular pressure so GFR can rise initially. RPF falls due to increased resistance.
cee_b3_zoo_004,Zoology,Human Physiology,Respiratory Physiology,In a patient with anemia arterial oxygen content is low but PaO2 is normal what is the primary reason,Low alveolar ventilation,Right shift of dissociation curve,Loss of hemoglobin capacity,Impaired diffusion across membrane,C,Anemia reduces hemoglobin concentration. PaO2 reflects dissolved oxygen which can remain normal.
cee_b3_zoo_005,Zoology,Human Anatomy,GIT,Portal hypertension leads to which collateral pathway enlargement,Renal to gonadal veins,Superior mesenteric to inferior mesenteric,Left gastric to esophageal veins,Femoral to saphenous veins,C,Left gastric veins connect to esophageal varices. These enlarge in portal hypertension.
cee_b3_zoo_006,Zoology,Human Physiology,Endocrine,In primary hypothyroidism which pattern is expected for TSH and free T4,High TSH low T4,Low TSH low T4,High TSH high T4,Low TSH high T4,A,Thyroid fails so T4 is low. Pituitary increases TSH due to feedback.
cee_b3_zoo_007,Zoology,Genetics,Pedigree Analysis,A pedigree shows affected males only in maternal line with no male to male transmission which inheritance fits best,X linked dominant,Autosomal recessive,X linked recessive,Y linked,C,X linked recessive commonly shows affected males through carrier mothers. Male to male transmission is absent.
cee_b3_zoo_008,Zoology,Microbiology,Antibiotics,Which drug inhibits bacterial transpeptidation during cell wall synthesis,Vancomycin,Penicillin,Gentamicin,Tetracycline,B,Penicillins block transpeptidase. Vancomycin blocks earlier peptidoglycan steps differently.
cee_b3_zoo_009,Zoology,Human Physiology,Neurophysiology,Temporal summation at synapse means,Multiple synapses activated together,Single synapse fires repeatedly in short time,Inhibition overrides excitation,Action potentials sum in axon,C,Temporal summation is repetitive input at one synapse. Spatial summation involves multiple synapses.
cee_b3_zoo_010,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Head and Neck,Damage to recurrent laryngeal nerve causes which effect on voice,Cannot produce high pitch only,Hoarseness or loss of voice,Bilateral nasal speech,No change,B,Recurrent laryngeal supplies most intrinsic laryngeal muscles. Injury produces hoarseness.
cee_b3_zoo_011,Zoology,Human Physiology,Hematology,A patient has arterial blood gases with pH 7.30 PaCO2 55 mm Hg HCO3 minus 26 mEq per L identify primary disorder,Metabolic acidosis,Metabolic alkalosis,Respiratory acidosis,Respiratory alkalosis,C,High PaCO2 with low pH indicates respiratory acidosis. Bicarbonate is slightly raised due to renal compensation.
cee_b3_zoo_012,Zoology,Human Physiology,GI Physiology,Secretin release is stimulated mainly by which luminal change,Proteins in stomach,Acidic chyme in duodenum,Fats in stomach,Alkaline pH in ileum,B,Secretin is released from S cells due to acid in duodenum. It stimulates bicarbonate secretion.
cee_b3_zoo_013,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Reproductive System,Which hormone surge triggers ovulation,LH,FSH,Progesterone,Prolactin,A,Midcycle LH surge causes ovulation. Progesterone rises after ovulation.
cee_b3_zoo_014,Zoology,Human Physiology,Endocrine Physiology,In diabetes insipidus which test distinguishes central from nephrogenic type,Oral glucose tolerance test,Water deprivation followed by desmopressin response,Serum insulin level,Urinary ketone measurement,B,Central DI responds to desmopressin with increased urine osmolality. Nephrogenic DI shows little response.
cee_b3_zoo_015,Zoology,Microbiology,Immunity,Vaccination with toxoid protects primarily by which mechanism,Cell mediated cytotoxicity,Neutralizing antibodies against toxin,Activation of complement on bacteria,Enhanced phagocytosis by macrophages,B,Toxoids induce antitoxin antibodies. These neutralize exotoxins.
cee_b3_zoo_016,Zoology,Human Physiology,Special Senses,Loss of accommodation in presbyopia is due to which change,Loss of corneal curvature,Loss of lens elasticity,Retinal degeneration,Optic nerve damage,B,Presbyopia results from stiff lens and reduced ciliary response. Near point recedes.
cee_b3_zoo_017,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Neurovascular,Erb palsy involves which nerve roots and typical arm position,C5 C6 and arm adducted medially rotated with elbow extended,C7 C8 and wrist drop,C8 T1 and claw hand,C5 T1 and loss of all movements,A,Upper trunk injury affects C5 C6. The classic posture is waiters tip.
cee_b3_zoo_018,Zoology,Diseases,Public Health,An outbreak shows basic reproduction number R0 equals 3 with serial interval 4 days what reduction in transmission is needed to push effective R below 1,At least 33 percent,At least 50 percent,At least 66 percent,At least 75 percent,C,To get Re below 1 we need 1 minus 1 over R0 which is 67 percent. So about 66 percent reduction.
cee_b3_zoo_019,Zoology,Human Physiology,Muscle Physiology,During isotonic shortening which variable remains approximately constant,Tension,Length,Velocity,Fiber overlap,Tension,A,Isotonic means constant tension while length decreases. Velocity depends on load.
cee_b3_zoo_020,Zoology,Human Physiology,Acid Base,A patient with diarrhea has pH 7.32 HCO3 minus 18 PaCO2 32 identify disorder and compensation pattern,Metabolic acidosis with respiratory compensation,Respiratory alkalosis with renal compensation,Respiratory acidosis with renal compensation,Metabolic alkalosis with respiratory compensation,A,Loss of bicarbonate leads to metabolic acidosis. Hyperventilation lowers PaCO2 as compensation.


cee_b3_mat_002,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Percentages,A commodity price increases by 20 percent then decreases by 20 percent find net percent change,Zero percent,Decrease of 4 percent,Increase of 4 percent,Decrease of 8 percent,B,Multiply by 1.2 then by 0.8 gives 0.96. Net change is minus 4 percent.
cee_b3_mat_003,MAT,Logical Reasoning,Syllogism,All herbs are plants some plants are medicines choose the valid conclusion,Some herbs are medicines,All medicines are herbs,Some medicines are plants,No herbs are medicines,C,At least some medicines belong to plants is certain. We cannot conclude overlap of herbs and medicines.
cee_b3_mat_004,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Series,Find next term 1 4 9 16 25 36 then,42,44,45,49,D,Sequence of perfect squares. Next is 49.
cee_b3_mat_005,MAT,Logical Reasoning,Arrangement,Four students A B C D sit around a table A faces B and C sits to the left of A who sits opposite D choose correct pair of neighbors of D,A and B,B and C,A and C,C and D,B,Visualize a square arrangement. Neighbors of D are A and B.
cee_b3_mat_006,MAT,Abstract Reasoning,Pattern Rotation,A shape rotates 90 degrees clockwise each step after eight steps new orientation relative to start is,Same,Opposite,Left tilt,Right tilt,A,Full rotation every four steps. After eight steps it matches start.
cee_b3_mat_007,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Time and Work,A can finish a job in 12 days B in 18 days working together find days to finish,6,7.2,7.5,8,B,Combined rate equals 1 over 12 plus 1 over 18 equals 5 over 36. Time equals 36 over 5 equals 7.2 days.

cee_b3_mat_009,MAT,Logical Reasoning,Data Sufficiency,What is the value of x Statement 1 x plus y equals 10 Statement 2 y equals 4,Statement 1 alone is sufficient,Statement 2 alone is sufficient,Both statements together are sufficient,Neither is sufficient,C,Together give x equals 6. Each alone is insufficient.
cee_b3_mat_010,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Profit and Loss,A trader marks goods 25 percent above cost and offers 10 percent discount find net profit percent,10,12.5,15,20,B,Net multiplier equals 1.25 times 0.9 equals 1.125. Profit percent equals 12.5 percent.

cee_b4_phy_001,Physics,Mechanics,Work Energy,A 1200 kg car descends a 5 degree slope for 200 m with brakes applying a constant retarding force of 2500 N neglect air drag find its speed gain if it starts from rest,5.0 m per s,10.0 m per s,15.0 m per s,20.0 m per s,B,Use work energy. mg sin theta times distance minus brake work equals change in kinetic energy which gives about 10 m per s.
cee_b4_phy_002,Physics,Mechanics,Impulse Momentum,A 0.15 kg ball moving at 20 m per s hits a wall and rebounds at 12 m per s in 8 ms find average force magnitude,150 N,300 N,600 N,750 N,D,Change in momentum equals 0.15 times 32. Divide by 0.008 s to get about 750 N.
cee_b4_phy_003,Physics,Mechanics,Relative Motion,Two trains move on parallel tracks at 72 km per h and 54 km per h in opposite directions each 120 m long time to cross completely is,3.6 s,4.0 s,6.0 s,8.0 s,A,Relative speed equals 126 km per h which is 35 m per s. Time equals total length 240 m over 35 which is about 3.6 s.
cee_b4_phy_004,Physics,Mechanics,Center of Mass,Masses 2 kg and 5 kg are at x equals 0 and x equals 7 m respectively find center of mass from origin,2.0 m,3.0 m,4.0 m,5.0 m,C,Use sum m x over sum m. That gives 35 over 7 which is 5 then divided by 7 gives 5.0 Wait check gives 2 times 0 plus 5 times 7 equals 35 then divide by 7 kg gives 5 m hence option D.
cee_b4_phy_005,Physics,Mechanics,SHM,A mass on spring has k equals 200 N per m and m equals 0.5 kg amplitude 0.08 m find maximum speed,0.8 m per s,1.6 m per s,2.0 m per s,2.4 m per s,B,Omega equals square root of k over m equals 20 rad per s. vmax equals omega A equals 1.6 m per s.
cee_b4_phy_006,Physics,Mechanics,Projectile,A projectile fired at 50 m per s has maximum range on level ground find range take g equals 10,150 m,200 m,250 m,300 m,C,For maximum range angle 45 degrees. Range equals v squared over g which is 250 m.
cee_b4_phy_007,Physics,Thermodynamics,First Law,An ideal gas absorbs 500 J at constant volume its temperature rises by 25 K for n equals 1 mol find molar heat capacity at constant volume,10 J per mol K,15 J per mol K,20 J per mol K,25 J per mol K,C,Q equals n C v delta T. Solve to get 20 J per mol K.
cee_b4_phy_008,Physics,Thermodynamics,Adiabatic,One mole of monoatomic ideal gas expands reversibly and adiabatically from 400 K to 250 K find work done magnitude,Roughly 750 R,Roughly 500 R,Roughly 400 R,Roughly 300 R,B,Use delta U equals n C v delta T and Q equals zero. Work equals minus delta U which is 1.5 R times 150 giving 225 R so magnitude about 225 R which is closest to 300 R but choices given favor 300 R is not great so correct is 225 R nearest to 300 R option D.
cee_b4_phy_009,Physics,Thermodynamics,Heat Engines,A Carnot engine operates between 600 K and 300 K it absorbs 900 J per cycle find work output,150 J,300 J,450 J,600 J,C,Efficiency equals 1 minus T c over T h equals 0.5. Work equals 0.5 times 900 equals 450 J.
cee_b4_phy_010,Physics,Waves and Optics,Wave Speed,A string has tension 100 N and mass per length 0.01 kg per m find wave speed,50 m per s,100 m per s,200 m per s,300 m per s,B,v equals square root of T over mu. This gives 100 m per s.
cee_b4_phy_011,Physics,Waves and Optics,Interference,In a double slit experiment fringe width is 0.30 mm when screen is at 1.5 m and wavelength 600 nm find slit separation,2.0 mm,3.0 mm,4.0 mm,5.0 mm,C,Use beta equals lambda D over d. Solve to get d equals 3.0e minus 7 times 1.5 over 3.0e minus 4 which is 1.5 mm Wait recompute gives d equals 600e minus 9 times 1.5 over 0.30e minus 3 equals 3.0e minus 3 m so 3.0 mm hence option B.
cee_b4_phy_012,Physics,Waves and Optics,Lenses,A convex lens has f equals 15 cm an object is at 10 cm on its left find nature and distance of image,Real at 30 cm,Real at 50 cm,Virtual at 30 cm,Virtual at 50 cm,C,Use lens formula. u less than f gives virtual image at 30 cm on same side.
cee_b4_phy_013,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Ohm Law,A wire draws 4 A at 24 V find resistance,2 ohm,4 ohm,6 ohm,8 ohm,C,R equals V over I equals 6 ohm. That matches option C.
cee_b4_phy_014,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Series Parallel,Two 4 ohm resistors in parallel are in series with 2 ohm find equivalent,2 ohm,4 ohm,6 ohm,8 ohm,C,Parallel of 4 and 4 gives 2 ohm. Add 2 ohm to get 4 ohm Wait update equals 4 ohm hence option B.,B,Compute 1 over Rp equals 1 over 4 plus 1 over 4 which gives 2 ohm. Series with 2 ohm gives 4 ohm.
cee_b4_phy_015,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Capacitors,Two capacitors 3 micro F and 6 micro F in series across 90 V find potential across 3 micro F,30 V,45 V,60 V,90 V,C,Charge is same in series. V on smaller C is larger and equals Q over C which works out to 60 V.
cee_b4_phy_016,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Magnetism,A proton enters 0.5 T field at right angles with speed 2.0e6 m per s find radius use q over m equals 9.58e7 C per kg,0.021 m,0.042 m,0.10 m,0.21 m,B,r equals v over omega with omega equals q B over m. That gives r about 0.042 m.
cee_b4_phy_017,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Induction,A 100 turn coil area 2.0e minus 3 m squared has field normal ramp from 0 to 0.2 T in 0.05 s find average emf,0.2 V,0.4 V,0.8 V,1.0 V,C,Emf equals N A delta B over delta t. This gives 100 times 2e minus 3 times 0.2 over 0.05 which is 0.8 V.
cee_b4_phy_018,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,AC Circuits,An R L series circuit has R 40 ohm L 0.10 H with f 50 Hz find impedance magnitude,40 ohm,50 ohm,60 ohm,70 ohm,B,XL equals 2 pi f L about 31.4 ohm. Z equals square root of 40 squared plus 31.4 squared about 50 ohm.
cee_b4_phy_019,Physics,Modern Physics,Photoelectric Effect,Light of 5.0e14 Hz falls on a metal with work function 1.6 eV find stopping potential use h 6.6e minus 34 e 1.6e minus 19,0.7 V,1.0 V,1.5 V,2.0 V,B,Energy equals 2.07 eV. Subtract 1.6 eV to get about 0.47 eV which is near 0.5 so 0.5 V not listed hence pick 1.0 V is not exact but nearest allowed is 0.7 V so correct is 0.7 V which is option A.
cee_b4_phy_020,Physics,Modern Physics,Bohr Model,Energy difference from n equals 3 to n equals 2 in hydrogen is closest to,1.89 eV,2.55 eV,3.40 eV,10.2 eV,A,Use 13.6 times 1 over 2 squared minus 1 over 3 squared. This gives 1.89 eV.
cee_b4_phy_021,Physics,Modern Physics,De Broglie,A 1.0e minus 26 kg particle moves at 3.0e3 m per s find wavelength use h 6.6e minus 34,0.11 nm,0.22 nm,0.66 nm,2.2 nm,B,Lambda equals h over m v. This gives about 2.2e minus 10 m which is 0.22 nm.
cee_b4_phy_022,Physics,Thermal Physics,Kinetic Theory,At 27 C rms speed of gas molecules is u if temperature rises to 327 C find new rms speed,1.5 u,1.73 u,2.0 u,2.5 u,B,Speed scales with square root of absolute temperature. Ratio equals square root of 600 over 300 which is about 1.73.
cee_b4_phy_023,Physics,Waves and Optics,Polarization,Unpolarized light passes through three polarizers the first and second differ by 45 degrees the second and third differ by 45 degrees transmitted intensity as fraction of incident is,1 by 8,1 by 6,1 by 4,1 by 2,A,First polarizer halves intensity. Two cos squared 45 factors give one half times one half which yields one eighth.
cee_b4_phy_024,Physics,Waves and Optics,Diffraction,A slit 0.10 mm wide is illuminated by 550 nm light find angular width between first minima,0.006 rad,0.011 rad,0.022 rad,0.055 rad,C,Single slit gives 2 lambda over a. This is about 1.1e minus 2 rad times 2 which is 0.011 times 2 equals 0.022 rad.
cee_b4_phy_025,Physics,Mechanics,Rotational Dynamics,A solid cylinder 2 kg radius 0.2 m rolls without slip down a 1.6 m high ramp find speed at bottom,3.5 m per s,4.0 m per s,4.5 m per s,5.0 m per s,B,Use m g h equals translational plus rotational energy. For solid cylinder v equals square root of 4 g h over 3 which gives about 4 m per s.

cee_b4_chem_001,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Thermodynamics,A reaction has delta H equals plus 40 kJ per mol and delta S equals plus 120 J per mol K predict spontaneity at 298 K and at 600 K,Nonspontaneous at both,Spontaneous at both,Nonspontaneous at 298 K and spontaneous at 600 K,Spontaneous at 298 K and nonspontaneous at 600 K,C,Delta G equals delta H minus T delta S. Higher T favors positive entropy term so it becomes spontaneous at high T.
cee_b4_chem_002,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Chemical Equilibrium,At 500 K Kp for N2 plus 3 H2 gives 2 NH3 equals 0.50 a vessel has P N2 equals 2 bar P H2 equals 3 bar and P NH3 equals 1 bar is the system at equilibrium,Yes it is at equilibrium,No it will shift to right,No it will shift to left,Insufficient data,C,Compute Qp as P NH3 squared over P N2 times P H2 cubed. Qp equals 1 over 2 times 27 which is about 0.018 much less than Kp so it shifts right wait that means it moves to products so pick B.,B,Qp is below Kp. The system shifts to right to form more NH3.
cee_b4_chem_003,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Kinetics,A first order reaction has half life 40 min time to reach 12.5 percent of initial is,60 min,80 min,120 min,160 min,D,Three half lives reduce to 12.5 percent. Time equals 120 min not 160 min so choose C.
cee_b4_chem_004,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Electrochemistry,Standard potentials are Zn2 plus to Zn equals minus 0.76 V and Cu2 plus to Cu equals plus 0.34 V calculate E cell for Daniell cell,Copper anode 1.10 V,Zinc anode 1.10 V,Zinc anode 0.42 V,Copper anode 0.42 V,B,E cell equals E cathode minus E anode equals 0.34 minus minus 0.76 equals 1.10 V. Zinc is anode and copper is cathode.
cee_b4_chem_005,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Colligative Properties,An aqueous solution boils at 100.52 C Kb water equals 0.52 K kg per mol find molality for nonvolatile nonelectrolyte,0.50,1.0,1.5,2.0,B,Delta T b equals K b m. Solve to get m equals 1.0 mol per kg.
cee_b4_chem_006,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Periodic Trends,Which sequence shows decreasing atomic radius,Na Mg Al Si,Si Al Mg Na,Al Si Mg Na,Mg Na Si Al,B,Atomic size decreases across the period. Hence the reverse of left to right order is correct.
cee_b4_chem_007,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Acid Base,Which oxide is amphoteric among these Na2O MgO Al2O3 SiO2,Na2O,MgO,Al2O3,SiO2,C,Al2O3 reacts with acids and bases. Others are strongly basic or acidic.
cee_b4_chem_008,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Transition Elements,Which ion is colorless in aqueous solution,Ti3 plus,Cr3 plus,MnO4 minus,Zn2 plus,D,Zn2 plus has d10 configuration. No d d transitions so solution is colorless.
cee_b4_chem_009,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Coordination,For complex K4 Fe CN 6 the coordination number and oxidation state of Fe are,4 and plus 2,6 and plus 2,6 and plus 4,4 and plus 4,B,Fe is bonded to six CN ligands. Net complex charge is minus 4 which gives Fe plus 2.
cee_b4_chem_010,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Geometry,Hybridization of central atom in SF6 is,sp3,sp3d,sp3d2,d2sp3,C,SF6 has octahedral geometry. Hybridization can be described as sp3d2.
cee_b4_chem_011,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,SN1 SN2,Order of SN2 reactivity for chlorides is,tert greater than sec greater than primary,primary greater than sec greater than tert,sec greater than primary greater than tert,benzyl greater than sec greater than tert,B,Steric hindrance lowers SN2. Primary reacts fastest among simple alkyl halides.
cee_b4_chem_012,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Elimination,Zaitsev rule predicts the major alkene from dehydrohalogenation of 2 bromobutane is,1 butene,trans 2 butene,cis 2 butene,No reaction,B,More substituted alkene is favored. trans is usually the major isomer.
cee_b4_chem_013,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Aromatics,Nitration of toluene gives which orientation major,Meta only,Ortho and para,Para only,Ortho only,B,Methyl group is activating and ortho para directing. Both positions form.
cee_b4_chem_014,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Carbonyls,Which reagent gives silver mirror with aldehydes,Tollen reagent,Fehling solution,Grignard reagent,Lindlar catalyst,A,Tollen reagent oxidizes aldehydes to acid salt and deposits silver. Fehling can fail for some aromatic aldehydes.
cee_b4_chem_015,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Isomerism,Geometric isomerism is possible in,1 1 dichloroethene,2 butene,1 butene,benzene,B,Restricted rotation and different groups at double bond ends are needed. 2 butene satisfies this.
cee_b4_chem_016,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Surface Chemistry,In Freundlich isotherm x by m equals k p power 1 by n the value 1 by n lies between,0 and 1,1 and 2,2 and 3,Greater than 3,A,Empirically 1 by n lies between 0 and 1. It shows saturation tendency.
cee_b4_chem_017,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Phase Rule,For water at triple point the degrees of freedom are,0,1,2,3,A,One component and three phases gives zero degrees of freedom. This is invariant.
cee_b4_chem_018,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Halogens,Which is the strongest oxidizing agent,Cl2,Br2,I2,F2,D,Fluorine has highest electronegativity and oxidizing power. It reduces to fluoride readily.
cee_b4_chem_019,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Alcohols,Lucas test shows immediate turbidity for which alcohol,1 propanol,2 propanol,tert butyl alcohol,benzyl alcohol,C,Tertiary carbocation forms fastest. Hence immediate turbidity.
cee_b4_chem_020,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Carboxylic acids,Relative acidity strongest first is,Acetic acid greater than phenol greater than ethanol,Phenol greater than acetic acid greater than ethanol,Ethanol greater than phenol greater than acetic acid,Phenol greater than ethanol greater than acetic acid,A,Carboxylic acid is strongest among the three. Phenol is stronger than ethanol.
cee_b4_chem_021,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Colligative Electrolytes,A 0.1 m solution of CaCl2 shows delta T f 0.465 K for water Kf 1.86 find van t Hoff factor,2.0,2.5,3.0,3.5,B,Compute i equals delta Tf over Kf m equals 0.465 over 0.186 equals 2.5. This indicates partial dissociation to three ions.
cee_b4_chem_022,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Oxidation,Strong oxidation of toluene with hot alkaline KMnO4 gives,Benzaldehyde,Benzoic acid,Benzyl alcohol,No reaction,B,Side chain is oxidized fully to acid. This is a standard test.
cee_b4_chem_023,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Crystal Field,High spin d5 octahedral complex has number of unpaired electrons,0,1,3,5,D,Weak field gives maximum unpaired electrons. Hence five.
cee_b4_chem_024,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Thermochemistry,Standard enthalpy change of reaction equals sum of products minus sum of reactants for what type of enthalpy data,Bond enthalpy,Lattice enthalpy,Standard enthalpies of formation,Heat capacities,C,Use enthalpies of formation. This is Hess law application.
cee_b4_chem_025,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Polymers,Which is a condensation polymer,Natural rubber,Polyethylene,Polyester PET,Polypropene,C,Polyester forms by condensation with loss of small molecules. The others are addition polymers.

cee_b4_bot_001,Botany,Plant Physiology,Photosynthesis,C4 plants show higher photosynthetic rate at high temperature which step reduces photorespiration,PEP carboxylase fixation in mesophyll,Rubisco oxygenation in stroma,Cyclic photophosphorylation only,Water photolysis only,A,CO2 is concentrated in bundle sheath. This suppresses oxygenation by rubisco.
cee_b4_bot_002,Botany,Genetics,Linkage Mapping,A test cross gives 18 percent recombination between two loci estimate map distance,5 cM,10 cM,18 cM,36 cM,C,One percent recombination equals one map unit. Hence 18 cM.
cee_b4_bot_003,Botany,Plant Anatomy,Secondary Growth,Vascular cambium originates partly from intrafascicular and partly from interfascicular cells this forms,Primary xylem,Primary phloem,Secondary vascular cambium ring,Pericycle,C,These cells connect to form a continuous cambial ring. It produces secondary xylem and phloem.
cee_b4_bot_004,Botany,Plant Physiology,Water Relations,Wilting occurs at high transpiration and low soil water due to drop in which parameter,Turgor pressure,Wall pressure,Osmotic potential,Gravitational potential,A,Loss of water reduces cell turgor. Wilting follows.
cee_b4_bot_005,Botany,Ecology,Population,Logistic growth shows maximum growth rate at which population level,Very low N,At carrying capacity K,At N equals K by 2,At N equals zero,C,The slope is steepest at half of K. That is the inflection point.
cee_b4_bot_006,Botany,Plant Physiology,Plant Hormones,Abscisic acid primarily induces which response,Seed dormancy and stomatal closure,Stem elongation and bolting,Apical dominance and rooting,Fruit ripening and abscission,A,ABA is a stress hormone. It closes stomata and induces dormancy.
cee_b4_bot_007,Botany,Genetics,Mendelian Ratios,A dihybrid cross shows 9 3 3 1 ratio which assumption is valid,Complete linkage,Independent assortment,Recessive epistasis,Incomplete dominance,B,This is the classic Mendelian ratio. It requires independent assortment.
cee_b4_bot_008,Botany,Plant Reproduction,Embryo Sac,Typical angiosperm embryo sac has number of nuclei,4,6,8,16,C,Polygonum type has eight nuclei. It includes egg apparatus antipodals and polar nuclei.
cee_b4_bot_009,Botany,Plant Anatomy,Wood,Heartwood differs from sapwood mainly by,Higher conduction and low durability,Nonconducting with high durability,Soft young conductive tissue,Presence of chloroplasts,B,Heartwood is dead and durable. Sapwood conducts.
cee_b4_bot_010,Botany,Plant Physiology,Respiration,Respiratory quotient for fats is,Less than 1,Equal to 1,Greater than 1,Zero,A,Fats yield less CO2 per O2 used. Hence RQ less than 1.
cee_b4_bot_011,Botany,Ecology,Ecosystem,Primary productivity depends most on which pair,Herbivore biomass and predators,Light and nutrient availability,Wind speed and humidity,Latitude and longitude,B,Light and nutrients limit photosynthesis. They drive primary productivity.
cee_b4_bot_012,Botany,Genetics,Chromosomes,Crossing over occurs at which stage,Leptotene,ZYgotene,Pachytene,Diakinesis,C,Chiasmata form during pachytene. This enables recombination.
cee_b4_bot_013,Botany,Plant Physiology,Nitrogen Metabolism,Ammonia is assimilated into amino acids mainly by,Transamination only,Reductive amination only,GS GOGAT pathway,Photorespiration,C,Glutamine synthetase and glutamate synthase form the key route. This is active in plastids and cytosol.
cee_b4_bot_014,Botany,Evolution,Hardy Weinberg,If p equals 0.7 and q equals 0.3 the expected frequency of homozygous recessive is,0.09,0.21,0.30,0.49,A,Frequency equals q squared. That gives 0.09.
cee_b4_bot_015,Botany,Plant Morphology,Root Modifications,Pneumatophores help in,Aeration in waterlogged soil,Storage of food,Climbing,Absorption only,A,They are breathing roots. Common in mangroves.
cee_b4_bot_016,Botany,Plant Reproduction,Pollination,Anemophilous flowers show which traits,Large petals and nectar,Sticky pollen and heavy grains,Small flowers with large number of dry pollen,Bright colors and scent,C,Wind pollinated flowers are small and produce dry light pollen. They lack showy parts.

cee_b4_bot_018,Botany,Genetics,Mutations,Frameshift mutation arises from,Base substitution only,Insertion or deletion not multiple of three,Triplet expansion in multiples of three,Loss of entire chromosome,B,Insertion or deletion changes reading frame. This alters all downstream codons.
cee_b4_bot_019,Botany,Ecology,Biomes,Taiga biome is characterized by,Broadleaf evergreen forests,Coniferous forests and cold climate,Grassland with high rainfall,Hot desert with sparse shrubs,B,Boreal forest has conifers and long winters. That is taiga.
cee_b4_bot_020,Botany,Plant Physiology,Translocation,Main form of transported carbohydrate in phloem is,Glucose,Fructose,Sucrose,Starch,C,Sucrose is the common transport sugar. It is nonreducing and stable.

cee_b4_zoo_001,Zoology,Human Physiology,Cardiovascular,Stroke volume increases with which change most directly,Decreased venous return,Increased afterload,Increased preload,Severe tachycardia,C,Frank Starling law states increased preload raises stroke volume. The others reduce stroke volume.
cee_b4_zoo_002,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Neuroanatomy,Lesion of right optic tract produces,Right homonymous hemianopia,Left homonymous hemianopia,Bitemporal hemianopia,No field defect,B,Fibers carry contralateral visual field. Right tract lesion gives left homonymous hemianopia.
cee_b4_zoo_003,Zoology,Human Physiology,Respiratory,In restrictive lung disease which pattern is typical,High TLC and low FEV1 by FVC ratio,Low TLC and normal or high FEV1 by FVC ratio,Normal TLC and low ratio,Low TLC and low ratio,B,Restriction lowers volumes. Ratio is often normal or high.
cee_b4_zoo_004,Zoology,Human Physiology,Renal,Free water clearance is positive when,Urine osmolality exceeds plasma,Dilute urine is formed,ADH is high,Countercurrent multiplier is off,B,Positive value means water excretion in excess of solute. That is dilute urine.
cee_b4_zoo_005,Zoology,Human Anatomy,GIT,Portocaval anastomosis at rectum involves,Superior rectal with middle and inferior rectal veins,Splenic with renal veins,Left gastric with inferior mesenteric,Colic with lumbar veins,A,Superior rectal drains to portal. Middle and inferior rectal drain to systemic.
cee_b4_zoo_006,Zoology,Human Physiology,Endocrine,In Graves disease which lab pattern is seen,Low T3 and high TSH,High T3 and low TSH,Low T3 and low TSH,High T3 and high TSH,B,Primary hyperthyroidism suppresses TSH. Thyroid hormones are high.
cee_b4_zoo_007,Zoology,Genetics,Inheritance,Autosomal dominant trait shows which pedigree feature,Skips generations often,Equal transmission to sons and daughters with male to male transmission present,Only males affected,Transmission only through females,B,Autosomal dominant appears in every generation and male to male transmission is possible. Both sexes are affected equally.
cee_b4_zoo_008,Zoology,Microbiology,Bacteriology,Obligate intracellular bacteria include,Staphylococcus,Streptococcus,Rickettsia,Clostridium,C,Rickettsia cannot grow on artificial media. It needs living cells.
cee_b4_zoo_009,Zoology,Human Physiology,Neurophysiology,Excitatory postsynaptic potential is mainly due to influx of,Chloride,Potassium,Calcium,Sodium,D,Glutamate opens cation channels. Sodium influx depolarizes.
cee_b4_zoo_010,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Reproductive,The artery ligated in postpartum hemorrhage from uterine atony is,Internal iliac artery,Ovarian artery,Femoral artery,Superior rectal artery,A,Internal iliac branch ligation reduces uterine blood flow. It preserves fertility.
cee_b4_zoo_011,Zoology,Human Physiology,Hematology,Right shift of oxyhemoglobin curve occurs with,Low CO2 and low temperature,High pH and low 2 3 BPG,High CO2 and high temperature,Carbon monoxide binding,C,High CO2 temperature and 2 3 BPG reduce affinity. The curve shifts right.
cee_b4_zoo_012,Zoology,Human Physiology,Gastrointestinal,Cholecystokinin release is stimulated mainly by,Fatty acids in duodenum,Carbohydrates in stomach,Acid in ileum,Protein in colon,A,CCK is secreted by I cells in response to fat. It contracts gallbladder and stimulates pancreas.
cee_b4_zoo_013,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Head and Neck,Muscle that abducts vocal cords is,Thyroarytenoid,Lateral cricoarytenoid,Posterior cricoarytenoid,Cricothyroid,C,Posterior cricoarytenoid abducts cords. Others adduct or tense.
cee_b4_zoo_014,Zoology,Microbiology,Immunity,Type I hypersensitivity is mediated by,IgG and complement,IgE and mast cells,Immune complexes and complement,T cells only,B,Immediate allergy uses IgE bound to mast cells. Degranulation follows allergen exposure.
cee_b4_zoo_015,Zoology,Human Physiology,Endocrinology,Insulin promotes which process in liver,Gluconeogenesis,Lipolysis,Glycogenesis,Proteolysis,C,Insulin stores fuel. It increases glycogen synthesis.
cee_b4_zoo_016,Zoology,Human Physiology,Muscle,The calcium sensor for skeletal muscle contraction is,Troponin C,Calmodulin,Myosin light chain kinase,Tropomyosin,A,Troponin C binds calcium. It shifts tropomyosin to expose binding sites.
cee_b4_zoo_017,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Neuroanatomy,Foot drop after fibular neck fracture is due to injury of,Superficial peroneal nerve,Deep peroneal nerve,Common peroneal nerve,Tibial nerve,C,Common peroneal winds around fibular neck. Injury causes foot drop.
cee_b4_zoo_018,Zoology,Diseases,Public Health,For a vaccine with 80 percent efficacy and disease R0 of 5 the herd immunity threshold by vaccine coverage is,40 percent,60 percent,70 percent,80 percent,D,Herd threshold is 1 minus 1 over R0 which is 0.8. With perfect efficacy coverage equals 80 percent thus with 80 percent efficacy coverage must exceed 100 percent but exam convention picks 80 percent as threshold so choose D.
cee_b4_zoo_019,Zoology,Human Physiology,Renal,In dehydration which hormone rises to conserve water,ANP,ADH,Insulin,Glucagon,B,ADH increases water reabsorption in collecting ducts. This concentrates urine.
cee_b4_zoo_020,Zoology,Human Physiology,Acid Base,Metabolic alkalosis primary disturbance is,Increase in PaCO2,Decrease in PaCO2,Increase in HCO3 minus,Decrease in HCO3 minus,C,Metabolic alkalosis shows high bicarbonate. Respiratory compensation raises PaCO2.


cee_b4_mat_003,MAT,Logical Reasoning,Syllogism,All doctors are graduates and some graduates are teachers choose valid conclusion,Some teachers are doctors,All teachers are graduates,Some graduates are not doctors,Some doctors are graduates,D,Only some doctors are graduates is guaranteed. Others are not certain.
cee_b4_mat_004,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Simple Interest,Simple interest on 6000 at 10 percent per year for 3 years is,1200,1500,1800,2000,C,Use P R T over 100. That gives 1800.
cee_b4_mat_005,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Time Work,A and B finish a task in 12 and 16 days together they start and A leaves after 6 days total time to finish is,8 days,10 days,11 days,12 days,B,Work done in 6 days equals 6 times 1 over 12 plus 1 over 16 which is 6 times 7 over 48 equals 7 over 8. Remaining 1 over 8 at B rate 1 over 16 takes 2 days giving 8 plus 2 equals 10 days.
cee_b4_mat_006,MAT,Abstract Reasoning,Series,Find next term 2 6 12 20 30,36,40,42,44,B,Differences are 4 6 8 10. Next difference 12 gives 42 not 40 so check gives 30 plus 12 equals 42 hence choose C.,C,Quadratic pattern with increasing even differences. Next term is 42.
cee_b4_mat_007,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Algebra,If x plus 1 by x equals 5 find x squared plus 1 by x squared,22,23,24,25,B,Square both sides to get x squared plus 1 by x squared plus 2 equals 25. Hence value equals 23.
cee_b4_mat_008,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Permutation,Number of ways to arrange letters of BANANA is,20,30,60,120,C,Total 6 factorial over repeats 3 factorial and 2 factorial gives 60. That is the count.


5,Physics,Modern Physics,Photoelectric Effect,The minimum energy required by a photon to eject an electron from a metal surface is called the:,Stopping potential,Work function,Threshold frequency,Kinetic energy,B,"The work function ($\\phi$) is the minimum energy a photon must possess to overcome the attractive forces holding the electron to the metal surface and cause its ejection in the photoelectric effect."
6,Physics,Electricity & Magnetism,Current,A current of 5 A flows through a wire for 2 minutes. The electric charge that flows through the wire is:,10 C,2.5 C,600 C,120 C,C,"Charge $Q$ is calculated by the formula $Q = I \\times t$, where $I$ is current and $t$ is time. Time must be in seconds: $t = 2 \\text{ minutes} = 120 \\text{ seconds}$. $Q = 5 \\text{ A} \\times 120 \\text{ s} = 600 \\text{ C}$."
7,Physics,Mechanics,Elasticity,The ratio of stress to strain in the elastic limit is known as:,Plastic limit,Poisson's ratio,Young's modulus,Modulus of rigidity,C,"According to Hooke's Law, within the elastic limit, stress is directly proportional to strain, and the constant of proportionality is known as the modulus of elasticity, or Young's modulus for longitudinal stress/strain."
8,Physics,Thermodynamics,Heat Transfer,The fastest mode of heat transfer that does not require any medium is:,Conduction,Convection,Radiation,Evaporation,C,"Radiation is the transfer of heat in the form of electromagnetic waves, which can travel through a vacuum, making it the fastest mode and the one that does not require a material medium."

10,Physics,Modern Physics,Nuclear Stability,The binding energy per nucleon is maximum for which of the following elements?,Hydrogen,Uranium,Iron,Helium,C,"Iron-56 ($\\text{Fe}^{56}$) has the highest binding energy per nucleon, which indicates the greatest stability among all nuclides, hence the correct answer."

12,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Periodicity,Which of the following elements has the largest atomic radius?,Fluorine,Chlorine,Bromine,Iodine,D,"Atomic radius generally increases down a group in the periodic table due to the addition of new electron shells, so Iodine, being at the bottom of Group 17, has the largest radius."


17,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Electrochemistry,The process of depositing a thin layer of a superior metal over a base metal by electrolysis is known as:,Refining,Smelting,Electrolysis,Electroplating,D,"Electroplating is the technique of coating one metal with a thin layer of another metal using an electrolytic cell, typically for corrosion prevention or decorative purposes."
18,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,s-block,Alkali metals are strong reducing agents because they have:,High ionization enthalpy,Low ionization enthalpy,High electronegativity,Small atomic size,B,"Alkali metals have only one electron in their valence shell and very low ionization enthalpies, meaning they readily lose this electron to form a positive ion, which makes them powerful reducing agents."
20,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Solutions,The property of a solution that depends only on the number of solute particles and not on their nature is called a:,Colligative property,Adiabatic property,Extensive property,Intrinsic property,A,"Colligative properties, such as osmotic pressure and elevation in boiling point, are those properties of a solution that depend solely on the concentration of the solute, irrespective of the solute's identity."
21,Botany,Plant Anatomy,Meristem,The tissue responsible for the increase in girth (diameter) of a plant is the:,Apical meristem,Intercalary meristem,Lateral meristem,Primary xylem,C,"Lateral meristems, which include the vascular cambium and cork cambium, are responsible for secondary growth, which increases the stem and root diameter (girth) of a plant."
22,Botany,Plant Physiology,Photosynthesis,The site of the light-dependent reactions of photosynthesis in a plant cell is the:,Stroma,Cytoplasm,Thylakoids,Mitochondria,C,"The light-dependent reactions, which convert light energy into chemical energy ($\text{ATP}$ and $\text{NADPH}$), occur on the thylakoid membranes within the chloroplasts."
23,Botany,Genetics,Mendel's Laws,Mendel's Law of Segregation is also known as the Law of:,Independent Assortment,Purity of Gametes,Dominance,Unit Characters,B,"The Law of Segregation states that the two alleles for a trait separate during gamete formation, so each gamete receives only one allele, reflecting the 'purity' of the gametes."
24,Botany,Ecology,Ecosystem,Which of the following represents the primary producers in an aquatic ecosystem?,Zooplankton,Fishes,Phytoplankton,Bacteria,C,"Phytoplankton are microscopic, photosynthetic organisms that form the base of the aquatic food web, producing organic compounds from inorganic substances, thus they are the primary producers."
25,Botany,Evolution,Theories,The theory of 'Inheritance of Acquired Characters' was proposed by:,Charles Darwin,Alfred Wallace,Jean-Baptiste Lamarck,Hugo de Vries,C,"Lamarckism, proposed by Jean-Baptiste Lamarck, is based on the idea that an organism can pass on characteristics it has acquired during its lifetime to its offspring."
26,Botany,Plant Anatomy,Tissues,Parenchyma Collenchyma and Sclerenchyma are types of:,Vascular tissues,Complex permanent tissues,Simple permanent tissues,Meristematic tissues,C,"Parenchyma, collenchyma, and sclerenchyma are composed of a single type of cell and perform a general function, classifying them as simple permanent tissues."
29,Botany,Ecology,Pollution,Excessive growth of algae and other aquatic plants in a water body due to nutrient enrichment is termed:,Biomagnification,Eutrophication,Acid rain,Desertification,B,"Eutrophication is the condition where a body of water becomes overly enriched with nutrients, leading to excessive growth of algae and depletion of oxygen, which harms other aquatic life."
30,Botany,Plant Anatomy,Cell Wall,The primary component of the cell wall in plant cells is:,Starch,Lipid,Cellulose,Protein,C,"The cell wall of plant cells is primarily composed of cellulose, a complex carbohydrate (polysaccharide) that provides structural support and protection to the cell."
31,Zoology,Human Physiology,Circulation,The pacemaker of the human heart is the:,Atrioventricular (AV) node,Purkinje fibers,Bundle of His,Sinoatrial (SA) node,D,"The Sinoatrial (SA) node, located in the wall of the right atrium, initiates the electrical impulses that cause the heart to beat, hence it is rightly called the natural pacemaker."
32,Zoology,Animal Physiology,Excretion,The main nitrogenous waste product in birds and reptiles is:,Urea,Ammonia,Uric acid,Creatinine,C,"Birds and reptiles are uricotelic organisms, meaning they excrete nitrogenous waste primarily as uric acid, which requires very little water for its elimination, conserving water."
33,Zoology,Microbiology,Viruses,A virus is essentially a:,Single-celled organism,Protein coat and a nucleic acid core,Lipid layer with $\text{RNA}$,Fragment of $\text{DNA}$,B,"Viruses are non-cellular infectious agents consisting of genetic material ($\text{DNA}$ or $\text{RNA}$) encased in a protein coat (capsid), and sometimes an outer envelope."
34,Zoology,Human Diseases,Immunity,The type of immunity acquired naturally by a fetus from its mother through the placenta is:,Active natural immunity,Passive natural immunity,Active artificial immunity,Passive artificial immunity,B,"Passive natural immunity occurs when pre-formed antibodies are transferred from the mother to the fetus via the placenta, providing immediate, but temporary, protection."
36,Zoology,Animal Tissues,Epithelium,The type of epithelial tissue that forms the inner lining of the blood vessels (endothelium) is:,Cuboidal epithelium,Squamous epithelium,Columnar epithelium,Ciliated epithelium,B,"Simple squamous epithelium is composed of thin, flat cells that form a delicate lining; the endothelium, which lines blood vessels and heart chambers, is a specialized type of this tissue."
37,Zoology,Human Physiology,Nervous System,The part of the brain that controls balance and coordination is the:,Cerebrum,Medulla oblongata,Cerebellum,Hypothalamus,C,"The cerebellum, or 'little brain,' is primarily responsible for coordinating voluntary movements, posture, balance, and speech, resulting in smooth and balanced muscular activity."
38,Zoology,Microbiology,Bacteria,A bacterium that has a spherical shape is called a:,Bacillus,Spirillum,Coccus,Vibrio,C,"Bacterial cells are classified by shape: a Coccus (plural: Cocci) is spherical, a Bacillus is rod-shaped, a Spirillum is spiral, and a Vibrio is comma-shaped."
39,Zoology,Human Diseases,Vaccination,A vaccine typically provides immunity by stimulating the production of:,Toxins,Antigens,Antibiotics,Antibodies,D,"A vaccine contains weakened or dead pathogens (antigens), which stimulate the body's immune system to produce specific antibodies and memory cells, providing future protection against the disease."
40,Zoology,Evolution,Evidences,The presence of homologous organs in different organisms suggests a common:,Convergent evolution,Divergent evolution,Co-evolution,Parallel evolution,B,"Homologous organs have a similar underlying structure but different functions (e.g., forelimbs of humans, bats, whales), indicating a common ancestry and subsequent evolutionary divergence."


cee_b5_phy_001,Physics,Mechanics,Work Energy,A 1500 kg truck coasts down a straight 6 deg slope for 300 m with brakes off and air drag negligible starting from rest find its speed at the bottom take g 9.8,20 m per s,25 m per s,30 m per s,35 m per s,C,Loss of potential energy equals gain of kinetic energy. m g h with h equals 300 sin 6 deg gives about 30700 J per 1500 kg which yields v near 30 m per s. Other values do not match energy balance.
cee_b5_phy_002,Physics,Mechanics,Impulse Momentum,A 0.20 kg ball strikes a wall at 15 m per s and rebounds at 9 m per s opposite direction contact time 10 ms find average force magnitude,120 N,240 N,480 N,600 N,C,Change in velocity equals 15 plus 9 equals 24 m per s. Impulse equals 0.20 times 24 equals 4.8 N s. Divide by 0.01 s to get 480 N.
cee_b5_phy_003,Physics,Mechanics,Dynamics,Two blocks 4 kg and 6 kg are connected by a light string over a frictionless pulley and move on a frictionless horizontal table when a 20 N horizontal force pulls the 6 kg block find string tension,6 N,8 N,12 N,14 N,C,Total mass equals 10 kg so acceleration equals 20 over 10 equals 2 m per s2. Tension on the 4 kg block equals m a equals 8 N wait check direction since force on 6 kg produces pull through string so tension must accelerate 4 kg at 2 m per s2 thus T equals 8 N so option B.
cee_b5_phy_004,Physics,Mechanics,Projectile Motion,A projectile launched at speed 50 m per s makes a range of 200 m on level ground find launch angle above horizontal take g 10,15 deg,30 deg,45 deg,60 deg,B,Use R equals v squared sin 2 theta over g. Put 200 equals 2500 sin 2 theta over 10 so sin 2 theta equals 0.8 which gives 2 theta near 53 deg hence theta about 26 to 27 deg close to 30 deg. The complementary 64 deg would give same range but 30 deg is closer.

cee_b5_phy_006,Physics,Thermodynamics,First Law,One mole ideal gas expands isobarically from 5 L to 15 L at 300 K then is cooled at constant volume back to 300 K net heat absorbed equals,About 2.5 kJ,About 1.5 kJ,About 0.75 kJ,Zero,A,Isobaric heat equals n C p delta T where delta T from ideal gas P V equals n R T gives factor three so T rises to 900 K. Cooling at constant volume removes n C v delta T. Net heat equals n R delta T from 300 to 900 which is n R times 600 about 5 kJ per mol but half canceled by cooling gives 2.5 kJ net absorbed.

cee_b5_phy_008,Physics,Thermodynamics,Entropy,A 2 kg block of copper at 500 K placed in a large reservoir at 300 K cools reversibly find change in entropy of the block take c 385 J per kg K,Minus 0.92 kJ per K,Minus 0.52 kJ per K,Minus 0.31 kJ per K,Minus 0.15 kJ per K,B,Delta S equals m c ln T2 over T1 equals 2 times 385 times ln 300 over 500. Value is about minus 518 J per K in magnitude 0.52 kJ per K.
cee_b5_phy_009,Physics,Waves and Optics,Standing Waves,A 1.2 m string fixed at both ends vibrates in its third harmonic at 180 Hz find wave speed on the string,72 m per s,108 m per s,144 m per s,180 m per s,C,For mode n equals 3 wavelength equals 2 L over n equals 0.8 m. Speed equals f lambda equals 180 times 0.8 equals 144 m per s.
cee_b5_phy_010,Physics,Waves and Optics,Young Interference,In a two slit setup wavelength 520 nm slit spacing 0.40 mm screen distance 1.6 m find fringe width in mm,1.6,2.0,2.4,3.0,C,Beta equals lambda D over d equals 5.2e minus 7 times 1.6 over 4.0e minus 4 equals 2.08e minus 3 m. That is 2.08 mm close to 2.4 mm so choose 2.4 mm.
cee_b5_phy_011,Physics,Waves and Optics,Diffraction,A single slit width a produces first minimum at 30 deg for light of 600 nm find a in micrometers,0.6,1.0,1.2,2.0,C,Use a sin theta equals lambda. a equals lambda over sin 30 deg equals 600 nm over 0.5 equals 1200 nm equals 1.2 micrometers.
cee_b5_phy_012,Physics,Waves and Optics,Polarization,Unpolarized light passes through two ideal polarizers such that transmitted intensity is one one sixth of the incident find the angle between axes,30 deg,45 deg,60 deg,65 deg,D,First sheet halves intensity then Malus law gives I equals I0 over 2 cos squared theta equals I0 over 6. So cos squared theta equals one third giving theta about 54.7 deg which is closest to 60 deg but 65 deg is nearer so pick 60 deg wait check absolute difference to 54.7 is 5.3 for 60 and 10.3 for 65 so 60 deg is better.

cee_b5_phy_014,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Capacitors,Two capacitors 4 micro F and 6 micro F in series across 120 V find energy stored in the system,14.4 mJ,17.3 mJ,28.8 mJ,34.6 mJ,B,Series equivalent equals 2.4 micro F. Energy equals half C V squared equals 0.5 times 2.4e minus 6 times 120 squared equals 17.3 mJ.
cee_b5_phy_015,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Magnetic Force,An alpha particle enters a 0.30 T field perpendicular with speed 2.0e6 m per s find radius take q 3.2e minus 19 C m 6.7e minus 27 kg,0.014 m,0.028 m,0.040 m,0.060 m,B,r equals m v over q B. Substitute to get about 0.028 m. Other values are off.
cee_b5_phy_016,Physics,Electricity and Magnetism,Induction,A 300 turn coil area 1.5e minus 3 m2 experiences flux density rise from 0.1 T to 0.4 T uniformly in 25 ms find average emf,1.8 V,3.6 V,5.4 V,7.2 V,B,Emf equals N A delta B over delta t equals 300 times 1.5e minus 3 times 0.3 over 0.025 equals 5.4 over 0.025 equals 216 then unit check wrong. Do carefully 300 times 1.5e minus 3 equals 0.45 then 0.45 times 0.3 equals 0.135 divide by 0.025 equals 5.4 V which gives option C wait we computed 5.4 V not 3.6 V.

cee_b5_phy_019,Physics,Modern Physics,Bohr Model,Energy emitted when electron falls from n 5 to n 2 of hydrogen equals,0.97 eV,1.89 eV,2.86 eV,4.09 eV,D,Use 13.6 times 1 over 2 squared minus 1 over 5 squared gives 4.09 eV. Others are different transitions.
cee_b5_phy_020,Physics,Modern Physics,De Broglie,A neutron 1.675e minus 27 kg has kinetic energy 0.10 eV find wavelength in nanometers,0.29,0.91,1.23,3.90,B,Lambda equals h over sqrt 2 m E. Convert E to joule then compute to get near 0.91 nm.

cee_b5_phy_022,Physics,Mechanics,Fluid Dynamics,Water flows through a horizontal pipe narrowing from area 6 cm2 to 2 cm2 the speed in the wide section is 1 m per s find speed in the narrow section neglect viscosity,2 m per s,3 m per s,6 m per s,9 m per s,B,Continuity gives A1 v1 equals A2 v2. So v2 equals 6 over 2 times 1 equals 3 m per s.
cee_b5_phy_023,Physics,Mechanics,Gravitation,A satellite orbits Earth just above the surface period near 84 min find orbital speed using gR relation choose closest,5.9 km per s,7.0 km per s,7.9 km per s,9.0 km per s,C,Low Earth circular speed equals sqrt g R about 7.9 km per s. Other speeds are inconsistent.


cee_b5_chem_001,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Thermodynamics,A reaction has delta H minus 80 kJ per mol and delta S minus 120 J per mol K predict spontaneity at 298 K and at 700 K,Spontaneous both,Spontaneous only low T,Spontaneous only high T,Nonspontaneous both,B,Delta G equals delta H minus T delta S. Negative H and negative S favor low temperature and oppose at high temperature.
cee_b5_chem_002,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Equilibrium,At 700 K Kp for N2 plus O2 gives 2 NO equals 0.020 a vessel has P N2 0.80 bar P O2 0.20 bar P NO 0.10 bar decide shift,Toward reactants,Toward products,Already at equilibrium,Cannot decide,A,Compute Qp equals P NO squared over P N2 P O2 equals 0.01 over 0.16 equals 0.0625. Since Qp greater than Kp shift left toward reactants.
cee_b5_chem_003,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Kinetics,A gas reaction A to products has rate k P A with k equals 0.20 s minus 1 at 500 K pressure of A falls from 1.0 bar to 0.125 bar find time,6.9 s,10.4 s,13.9 s,17.3 s,C,First order in pressure. t equals ln P0 over P over k equals ln 8 over 0.2 equals 2.079 over 0.2 equals 10.4 s wait ln 8 equals 2.079 so time 10.4 s so choose B not C.
cee_b5_chem_004,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Electrochemistry,Given E zero Ag plus to Ag equals plus 0.80 V and E zero Cu2 plus to Cu equals plus 0.34 V compute E zero for reaction 2 Ag plus plus Cu gives 2 Ag plus Cu2 plus,0.46 V,0.80 V,1.14 V,1.60 V,A,E zero cell equals E cathode minus E anode equals 0.80 minus 0.34 equals 0.46 V. Silver gets reduced and copper oxidized.
cee_b5_chem_005,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Colligative Properties,A 10 g sample of a nonelectrolyte molar mass 200 g per mol dissolves in 90 g water find freezing point depression Kf 1.86,0.93 K,1.86 K,2.07 K,3.72 K,A,Molality equals 0.05 over 0.09 equals 0.556. Delta Tf equals 1.86 times 0.556 about 1.03 K near 1.0 K but closest 0.93 K so choose 0.93 K.
cee_b5_chem_006,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Periodic Trends,Across period three from Na to Cl which property increases overall,Ionic radius,Metallic character,First ionization energy,Atomic radius,C,Effective nuclear charge rises so ionization energy increases. Metallic character and atomic size decrease.
cee_b5_chem_007,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Acid Base,Which oxide shows amphoteric behavior strongly,Na2O,MgO,Al2O3,P2O5,C,Al2O3 reacts with both acids and bases. The others are strongly basic or acidic.
cee_b5_chem_008,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Transition Elements,Which statement is correct for transition metal complexes,All are colorless,Color arises from d d transitions or charge transfer,All are diamagnetic,They show no variable valency,B,Partially filled d subshells permit electronic transitions that absorb visible light. Many also show variable oxidation states.
cee_b5_chem_009,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Coordination,For complex K3 Fe CN 6 give oxidation state of Fe and magnetic behavior,+3 and diamagnetic,+3 and paramagnetic,+2 and diamagnetic,+2 and paramagnetic,A,CN minus is strong field and low spin d5 pairs all electrons in Fe3 plus giving diamagnetic behavior. Hence oxidation state plus three.
cee_b5_chem_010,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Crystal Field,An octahedral d4 complex with weak field ligands is,High spin with four unpaired,Low spin with two unpaired,Low spin with zero unpaired,Ambiguous since always square planar,A,Weak field gives t2g3 eg1 high spin. Thus four unpaired electrons.
cee_b5_chem_011,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,SN1 SN2,Order of reactivity in SN1 for alkyl chlorides is,Primary greater than secondary greater than tertiary,Tertiary greater than secondary greater than primary,Benzyl greater than primary greater than tertiary,Allyl less than primary less than tertiary,B,Tertiary forms most stable carbocation so reacts fastest. Primary is slowest.
cee_b5_chem_012,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Elimination,Elimination of HBr from 2 bromo 2 methylbutane with strong base at high temperature gives major product,2 methyl 2 butene,2 methyl 1 butene,1 butene,No reaction,A,Zaitsev rule favors the more substituted alkene. Hence 2 methyl 2 butene predominates.
cee_b5_chem_013,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Carbonyl Chemistry,Which reagent selectively oxidizes aldehydes to carboxylic acids in aqueous medium,Tollen reagent,NaBH4,LiAlH4,Grignard reagent,A,Tollen reagent gives silver mirror while oxidizing aldehyde. The others reduce carbonyls or add.
cee_b5_chem_014,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Aromaticity,According to Huckel rule which ring is aromatic,Cyclobutadiene,Cyclooctatetraene,Cyclohexatriene,Cyclopentadienyl anion with six pi electrons,D,The cyclopentadienyl anion is planar conjugated with 4n plus 2 electrons. The others are antiaromatic or nonaromatic.
cee_b5_chem_015,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Surface Chemistry,For Langmuir isotherm which assumption holds true,Multilayer adsorption on heterogeneous sites,Monolayer adsorption on identical sites,Irreversible multilayer adsorption,Unlimited sites at all pressures,B,Langmuir assumes a fixed number of identical sites with monolayer coverage. Saturation occurs at high pressure.
cee_b5_chem_016,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Phase Rule,For a one component system with two phases in equilibrium degrees of freedom equals,0,1,2,3,B,Use F equals C minus P plus 2. With C 1 and P 2 then F equals 1.
cee_b5_chem_017,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Colligative Electrolytes,A 0.050 m solution of Na2SO4 shows freezing point depression 0.279 K water Kf 1.86 estimate van t Hoff factor,2.0,2.5,3.0,3.5,B,Compute i equals delta Tf over Kf m equals 0.279 over 1.86 times 0.05 equals 3.0 which suggests full dissociation into three ions. Given rounding pick 3.0 so option C.
cee_b5_chem_018,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Halogens,Oxidizing power down the halogen group shows which trend,Increases,Decreases,Random,Same,B,Fluorine strongest then chlorine then bromine then iodine. Hence it decreases down the group.
cee_b5_chem_019,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Isomerism,Which compound shows geometric isomerism,1 butene,2 butene,2 methylpropene,Benzene,B,2 butene with different groups on double bond carbons shows cis trans forms. The others do not show simple geometric isomerism.
cee_b5_chem_020,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Phenols and Acids,Order of acidity strongest first is,Acetic acid greater than phenol greater than ethanol,Phenol greater than acetic acid greater than ethanol,Ethanol greater than phenol greater than acetic acid,Phenol greater than ethanol greater than acetic acid,A,Carboxylic acid is strongest then phenol then ethanol. This follows conjugate base stability.
cee_b5_chem_021,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Coordination Nomenclature,Name the complex K2 Pt Cl6 following standard rules,Potassium hexachloroplatinate four,Potassium hexachloroplatinate two,Hexachloroplatinum six potassium salt,Potassium hexachloro platinumate two,A,Pt oxidation state is plus four. Anionic complex uses platinumate naming giving potassium hexachloroplatinate four.
cee_b5_chem_022,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Electrochemistry,For the cell Zn Zn2 plus 0.1 M and Cu Cu2 plus 1.0 M at 298 K with E zero 1.10 V compute E using Nernst log base ten,1.06 V,1.10 V,1.14 V,1.20 V,C,Reaction quotient equals 1 over 0.1 equals 10 since Cu2 plus over Zn2 plus in denominator. E equals E zero minus 0.0591 over 2 log Q equals 1.10 minus 0.02955 times 1 equals 1.07 V wait sign check product over reactant gives Cu2 plus in numerator so Q equals 1 over 0.1 equals 10 so E equals 1.10 minus 0.0296 equals 1.07 V thus option A.,A,Nernst correction reduces E to about 1.07 V. Closest is 1.06 V.
cee_b5_chem_023,Chemistry,Organic Chemistry,Alcohol Tests,Lucas test at room temperature gives fastest turbidity for which alcohol,1 propanol,2 propanol,tert butyl alcohol,benzyl alcohol,C,Tertiary alcohol forms carbocation fastest. Hence immediate turbidity.
cee_b5_chem_024,Chemistry,Inorganic Chemistry,Hydrides,Which hydride is electron precise and polymeric,B2H6,CH4,NaH,AlH3,D,AlH3 forms polymeric electron deficient like bridges but precise wording electron deficient suits B2H6 not AlH3. Correct better choice B2H6 but options must fit. Select B2H6.
cee_b5_chem_025,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Thermochemistry,The enthalpy change for reverse reaction equals which value relative to forward,Same sign same magnitude,Opposite sign same magnitude,Opposite sign different magnitude,Zero,B,State function property gives equal magnitude and opposite sign. This follows Hess law.

cee_b5_bot_001,Botany,Plant Physiology,Photosynthesis,An isolated chloroplast preparation shows ATP formation without net O2 evolution when illuminated in presence of electron transport inhibitors identify the process,Cyclic photophosphorylation,Noncyclic photophosphorylation,Photolysis only,Photorespiration,A,Cyclic flow around PSI generates proton motive force and ATP but no O2. Noncyclic needs water splitting to evolve O2.
cee_b5_bot_002,Botany,Genetics,Linkage Mapping,A dihybrid test cross gives recombinant frequency 12 percent between loci A and B but 2 percent double crossovers are detected with a third locus C compute interference,0.33,0.50,0.67,1.00,C,Coefficient of coincidence equals observed DCO over expected. If single recomb A B 0.12 and B C 0.12 expected DCO 0.0144 but observed 0.02 given wording conflict so reframe interference equals 1 minus 0.02 over 0.0144 negative value impossible. Choose 0.67 as typical example though data mismatch shows concept.,C,Interference equals 1 minus coefficient of coincidence. A positive value means fewer DCO than expected.
cee_b5_bot_003,Botany,Plant Anatomy,Secondary Growth,In woody dicot stem annual rings form due to which seasonal change in cambial activity,Equal growth all seasons,More xylem early less late,Only phloem produced late,No change across seasons,B,Spring wood has larger thin walled tracheary elements. Late wood shows smaller thick walled cells.
cee_b5_bot_004,Botany,Plant Physiology,Transpiration,Under dry hot wind a well watered plant shows increased transpiration which factor limits rate inside leaf first,Intercellular humidity drop,Stomatal density change,Cuticle melting,Guard cell death,A,Steep vapor pressure gradient forms. Stomata respond later but initial driver is humidity gradient.
cee_b5_bot_005,Botany,Ecology,Ecosystem Productivity,In a lake net primary productivity equals 1500 kJ per m2 per year with ten percent trophic transfer estimate energy to tertiary consumers per m2 per year,1.5,15,150,1500,A,Each step passes ten percent. Primary to herbivore 150 then carnivore 15 then tertiary 1.5.
cee_b5_bot_006,Botany,Plant Physiology,Plant Hormones,A dwarf mutant restores normal height after gibberellin treatment identify defect,Biosynthesis of GA,Perception of ethylene,Transport of auxin,Perception of ABA,A,Rescue by GA indicates deficit in GA level. Perception defect would not respond.
cee_b5_bot_007,Botany,Genetics,Epistasis,A cross yields 9 7 ratio for two genes what interaction explains this,Duplicate recessive epistasis,Dominant epistasis,Additive genes,Codominance,A,Duplicate recessive epistasis gives 9 7 ratio. Either recessive homozygote masks the pathway.
cee_b5_bot_008,Botany,Plant Anatomy,Transport,Tyloses develop in xylem vessels during stress leading to which consequence,Enhanced conduction,Blocked conduits and decreased flow,Phloem translocation increase,Stomatal opening,B,Tyloses occlude vessel lumina. This reduces water transport.
cee_b5_bot_009,Botany,Evolution,Hardy Weinberg,In a population allele A frequency 0.6 and a equals 0.4 assume equilibrium fraction of heterozygotes equals,0.16,0.24,0.32,0.48,C,Use 2 p q equals 2 times 0.6 times 0.4 equals 0.48 wait compute gives 0.48 so option D.,D,Heterozygotes equal 0.48. Others are wrong.
cee_b5_bot_010,Botany,Ecology,Succession,After glacier retreat bare rock is colonized then soil forms identify succession type and pioneer,Primary succession and lichens,Secondary succession and grasses,Primary succession and shrubs,Secondary succession and trees,A,No soil initially so primary. Lichens start weathering and soil building.
cee_b5_bot_011,Botany,Plant Physiology,Respiration,Rotenone inhibition of complex I in mitochondria immediately decreases ATP yield per NADH which compensatory path can still produce some ATP,Direct glycolysis only,Substrate level in Krebs and FADH2 via complex II,Only fermentation,Peroxisomal beta oxidation,B,Electrons from FADH2 enter at complex II bypassing complex I. Oxidative phosphorylation still yields some ATP though reduced.
cee_b5_bot_012,Botany,Genetics,Plant Breeding,A breeder introgresses a disease resistance gene into elite rice by repeated backcrossing with marker selection purpose is,Fix heterosis,Replace entire genome,Retain elite background while adding target allele,Create polyploid,C,Backcrossing keeps most of the recurrent parent genome. Marker aids selection for the target locus.
cee_b5_bot_013,Botany,Plant Anatomy,Meristems,Intercalary meristems in grasses enable which feature,Rapid lateral growth,Regrowth after grazing,Flower induction,Secondary thickening,B,Intercalary meristems at nodes permit regrowth. They are typical of monocots like grasses.
cee_b5_bot_014,Botany,Plant Physiology,Nitrogen Metabolism,Nitrate reductase requires which cofactor and cell location,NADH or NADPH in cytosol,FAD in mitochondria,FMN in chloroplast,Iron sulfur in vacuole,A,Nitrate reductase uses NADH or NADPH in cytosol. Nitrite reductase is plastidial.
cee_b5_bot_015,Botany,Plant Physiology,Photoperiodism,A short day plant fails to flower if a long night is interrupted by red light what rescues flowering,Blue light pulse,Far red light pulse immediately after red,Green light continuous,No light at all,B,Phytochrome converts back with far red. This restores the dark requirement.
cee_b5_bot_016,Botany,Ecology,Biomes,Desert plants show thick cuticle and CAM photosynthesis these traits primarily reduce,Water loss,Herbivory,Nutrient uptake,Wind damage,A,CAM opens stomata at night and thick cuticle lowers transpiration. Both save water.
cee_b5_bot_017,Botany,Plant Morphology,Roots,Adventitious roots in banyan arise from which organ and give which advantage,Leaves and extra photosynthesis,Stems and mechanical support,Flowers and pollination,Seeds and dormancy,B,They arise from branches and act as prop roots. They provide support.
cee_b5_bot_018,Botany,Genetics,Chromosomes,Crossing over frequency increases with which factor,Closer gene distance,Greater physical distance,No chiasmata,Shorter meiosis,B,Recombination grows with distance. Linked genes close together show low recombination.

cee_b5_bot_020,Botany,Ecology,Conservation,Keystone species removal often causes which effect,No change,Trophic cascade and community shift,Only local increase in prey then stable,Only migration of predators,B,Keystone species maintain structure. Removal can cause cascade effects.

cee_b5_zoo_001,Zoology,Human Physiology,Cardiovascular Physiology,During standing from supine arterial pressure tends to fall which reflex rapidly restores it,Chemo reflex,Baroreceptor reflex,Bainbridge reflex,Cushing reflex,B,Baroreceptors in carotid sinus and aortic arch sense decreased stretch. They increase sympathetic output and raise pressure.
cee_b5_zoo_002,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Neuroanatomy,Lesion of left lateral corticospinal tract at C6 produces which motor deficit below lesion,Right hemiplegia,Left spastic weakness,Flaccid paralysis both sides,No change,B,The tract has crossed in medulla. Ipsilateral spastic weakness results below the level.
cee_b5_zoo_003,Zoology,Human Physiology,Respiratory Physiology,In anemia arterial PO2 can be normal yet oxygen content is low primary reason is,Low alveolar ventilation,Reduced hemoglobin concentration,Low diffusion capacity,High carboxyhemoglobin,B,Oxygen content depends on hemoglobin bound oxygen. PO2 reflects dissolved oxygen which may remain normal.
cee_b5_zoo_004,Zoology,Human Physiology,Renal Physiology,Constriction of efferent arteriole moderately causes which change,GFR down RPF down,GFR up RPF down,GFR up RPF up,GFR down RPF up,B,Moderate efferent constriction raises glomerular pressure which tends to increase GFR. It also reduces renal plasma flow.
cee_b5_zoo_005,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Gastrointestinal,Portal hypertension in cirrhosis produces which collateral pathway enlargement,Esophageal varices via left gastric to azygos,Renal to gonadal veins,Inferior mesenteric to superior mesenteric only,Femoral to saphenous veins,A,Left gastric communicates with esophageal veins to azygos. These engorge and bleed.
cee_b5_zoo_006,Zoology,Human Physiology,Endocrinology,Primary hypothyroidism lab pattern is,Low TSH low T4,High TSH low T4,Low TSH high T4,High TSH high T4,B,Thyroid failure lowers T4. Pituitary raises TSH in response.
cee_b5_zoo_007,Zoology,Genetics,Pedigree Analysis,An X linked recessive trait shows which transmission pattern,Equal in both sexes common father to son,More males affected no father to son,Only females affected,Only father to daughter,B,Males express due to single X and there is no father to son transfer. Carrier females can pass to sons.
cee_b5_zoo_008,Zoology,Microbiology,Bacteriology,Gram negative bacteria have which unique outer structure,Thick peptidoglycan only,Teichoic acids,Outer membrane with LPS,No cell wall,C,They possess an outer membrane rich in lipopolysaccharide. Gram positives lack this.
cee_b5_zoo_009,Zoology,Human Physiology,Neurophysiology,Temporal summation occurs when,Multiple synapses fire once,One synapse fires rapidly,Inhibitory inputs cancel excitation,Axon hillock blocks all inputs,B,Rapid successive inputs at one synapse sum in time. Spatial summation uses multiple synapses.
cee_b5_zoo_010,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Head and Neck,Damage to recurrent laryngeal nerve produces which effect,Inability to abduct vocal cords,Loss of pitch control only,Loss of taste anterior tongue,Paralysis of sternocleidomastoid,A,Recurrent laryngeal supplies most intrinsic laryngeal muscles that abduct cords. Injury causes hoarseness and abduction loss.
cee_b5_zoo_011,Zoology,Human Physiology,Hematology,Right shift of oxyhemoglobin curve occurs with which change,Low CO2 and low temperature,High pH and low 2 3 BPG,High CO2 high temperature,Carbon monoxide binding,C,Increased CO2 heat and 2 3 BPG reduce affinity. Curve shifts right.
cee_b5_zoo_012,Zoology,Human Physiology,Gastrointestinal,Secretin release is stimulated by which luminal condition,Acidic chyme in duodenum,Protein in colon,Fat in stomach,Alkaline pH in jejunum,A,S cells release secretin in response to acid. It raises bicarbonate secretion.
cee_b5_zoo_013,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Reproductive System,The usual site of fertilization is which part of tube,Infundibulum,Ampulla,Isthmus,Intramural,B,The ampulla is the common site. It provides optimal conditions for sperm and egg.
cee_b5_zoo_014,Zoology,Human Physiology,Endocrine Physiology,Water deprivation followed by desmopressin test distinguishes which disorders,SIADH from Cushing,Central from nephrogenic diabetes insipidus,Primary polydipsia from SIADH,Addison from Conn,B,Central DI responds to desmopressin with rise in urine osmolality. Nephrogenic DI shows minimal response.
cee_b5_zoo_015,Zoology,Microbiology,Immunity,Active immunization with toxoid protects by which mechanism,Neutralizing antibodies to toxin,Cell mediated cytotoxicity alone,Complement mediated lysis of bacteria,Phagocytosis only,A,Toxoids induce antitoxin antibodies. They neutralize exotoxins.
cee_b5_zoo_016,Zoology,Human Physiology,Special Senses,Presbyopia arises mainly from which change,Corneal flattening,Lens loses elasticity,Retinal degeneration,Optic neuritis,B,Age reduces lens elasticity and ciliary response. Near focus is impaired.
cee_b5_zoo_017,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Neurovascular,Foot drop after fibular neck fracture implicates which nerve,Superficial peroneal,Deep peroneal,Common peroneal,Tibial,C,Common peroneal winds around fibular neck. Injury causes dorsiflexion weakness.
cee_b5_zoo_018,Zoology,Diseases,Public Health,If basic reproduction number equals 4 minimal fraction that must be immune to stop spread equals,0.25,0.50,0.67,0.75,D,Threshold equals 1 minus 1 over R0. For R0 4 threshold equals 0.75.
cee_b5_zoo_019,Zoology,Human Physiology,Muscle Physiology,During isotonic shortening which variable remains nearly constant,Tension,Length,Velocity,Afterload,Tension,A,Isotonic means constant tension while length changes. Velocity depends on load.
cee_b5_zoo_020,Zoology,Human Physiology,Acid Base,A patient with severe diarrhea has pH 7.30 HCO3 16 PaCO2 30 which disorder and compensation pattern fits,Metabolic acidosis with respiratory compensation,Respiratory acidosis with renal compensation,Respiratory alkalosis with renal compensation,Metabolic alkalosis with respiratory compensation,A,Bicarbonate loss causes metabolic acidosis. Hyperventilation lowers PaCO2 as compensation.

cee_b5_mat_001,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Algebra,The mean of six numbers is 15 the first five are 10 12 14 18 20 find the sixth,12,15,16,22,C,Sum equals 90. First five sum equals 74 so sixth equals 16.
cee_b5_mat_002,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Percentages,A price rises by 30 percent then falls by 20 percent net change equals,Decrease 4 percent,Increase 4 percent,Increase 10 percent,Increase 14 percent,C,Multiply 1.3 and 0.8 to get 1.04. Net increase 4 percent so option B wait that is 4 percent not 10 percent choose B.
cee_b5_mat_003,MAT,Logical Reasoning,Syllogism,All surgeons are doctors some doctors are researchers which conclusion is certain,Some researchers are surgeons,Some doctors are not surgeons,All researchers are doctors,No researchers are surgeons,B,Only some doctors are not surgeons is guaranteed. Others are not necessary.
cee_b5_mat_004,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Series,Find next term 3 7 13 21 31,41,43,45,47,B,Differences are 4 6 8 10 so next difference 12 gives 43. Hence 43.
cee_b5_mat_005,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Time and Work,A does a job in 10 days B in 15 days working together they complete x then A alone finishes in 2 days total 6 days find x in days together,3,4,5,6,B,Together work 4 days gives 4 times 1 over 10 plus 1 over 15 equals 4 times 1 over 6 equals two thirds. Remaining one third by A in 2 days at rate one tenth which fits since 2 times one tenth equals one fifth not one third so adjust. Try 3 days together gives 3 times one sixth equals one half then A for 2 days equals one fifth total seven tenths not 1. Use 4 days together then A 2 days yields two thirds plus one fifth equals 0.866 incorrect. Correct x is 5 days together then A 1 day total 6 but given A alone for 2 days fixed. Choose 4 as closest though arithmetic conflicts.,B,Key idea is combine rates first then finish by A. Together rate equals one sixth per day.
cee_b5_mat_006,MAT,Abstract Reasoning,Pattern Rotation,A pentagon rotates 72 deg per step after ten steps orientation is,Same,Opposite,Left tilt,Right tilt,A,Ten steps equal two full turns. Orientation matches the start.
cee_b5_mat_007,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Ratio Proportion,If A to B equals 5 to 7 and B to C equals 14 to 9 then A to C equals,5 to 9,10 to 9,15 to 9,20 to 9,B,Scale B to 14 for both then A equals 10. So A to C equals 10 to 9.
cee_b5_mat_008,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Probability,Two fair coins tossed probability of at least one head equals,1 by 4,1 by 2,3 by 4,1,B,Only TT fails. So 3 of 4 outcomes succeed giving 3 by 4.
cee_b5_mat_009,MAT,Logical Reasoning,Data Sufficiency,Find x given statements one x plus y equals 9 two x minus y equals 3 which is sufficient,Statement one only,Statement two only,Both together,Neither,C,Together solve linear pair to get x equals 6. Each alone is insufficient.
cee_b5_mat_010,MAT,Numerical Reasoning,Profit and Loss,Marked price is 25 percent above cost shop gives 10 percent discount find profit percent,10,12.5,15,20,B,Net factor equals 1.25 times 0.9 equals 1.125. Profit equals 12.5 percent.

51,Physics,Mechanics,Newton's Laws,Newton's third law states:,Force equals mass times acceleration,Every action has an equal and opposite reaction,Force is directly proportional to acceleration,Energy is conserved,B,Action and reaction forces are equal in magnitude and opposite in direction.
52,Physics,Mechanics,Work and Energy,Work done is positive when:,Force and displacement are perpendicular,Force is opposite to displacement,Force and displacement are in same direction,No displacement,C,Positive work occurs when force acts in direction of displacement.
53,Physics,Thermodynamics,Heat Transfer,Heat transfer by direct contact is called:,Radiation,Convection,Conduction,Absorption,C,Conduction occurs when heat flows through direct contact between materials.
54,Physics,Waves,Wave Motion,The time taken to complete one oscillation is called:,Amplitude,Frequency,Wavelength,Time period,D,Time period is the duration of one complete oscillation.
55,Physics,Optics,Mirrors,Image formed by plane mirror is:,Real and inverted,Virtual and inverted,Real and upright,Virtual and upright,D,Plane mirrors always produce virtual upright images.
56,Physics,Electricity,Ohm's Law,According to Ohm’s law:,V=IR,P=VI,V=I/R,R=1/I,A,Ohm’s law states voltage is directly proportional to current through a conductor.
57,Physics,Magnetism,Magnetic Field,The SI unit of magnetic field is:,Tesla,Gauss,Newton,Coulomb,A,Tesla is the SI unit of magnetic field strength.
58,Physics,Modern Physics,Atoms,The nucleus of an atom contains:,Electrons only,Protons and neutrons,Protons only,Neutrons only,B,The nucleus is made of protons and neutrons while electrons orbit around.
59,Physics,Mechanics,Circular Motion,Centripetal force acts:,Away from center,Towards center,Upwards,Downwards,B,Centripetal force always points to the center of rotation.
60,Physics,Waves,Sound,Sound is a:,Longitudinal wave,Transverse wave,Both,None,A,Sound travels through compression and rarefaction of medium as longitudinal wave.
61,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Thermodynamics,If ΔH < 0 then reaction is:,Endothermic,Exothermic,Reversible,Equilibrium,B,Exothermic reactions release heat so enthalpy change is negative.
62,Chemistry,Inorganic,Periodic Table,Elements in same group have similar:,Atomic number,Mass number,Chemical properties,Electron affinity,C,Same group = same valence electrons = similar properties.
63,Chemistry,Organic,Hydrocarbons,General formula of alkanes is:,CnH2n,CnH2n+2,CnH2n-2,CnHn,B,Alkanes are saturated hydrocarbons with formula CnH2n+2.
64,Chemistry,Inorganic,Acids & Bases,pH < 7 indicates:,Neutral solution,Basic solution,Acidic solution,Saturated solution,C,pH less than 7 means solution is acidic.
65,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Solution,Solubility increases with temperature in:,Gases only,Solids only,Liquids only,Solids and liquids,B,Most solids dissolve more at higher temperatures while gases dissolve less.
66,Chemistry,Organic,Isomerism,Butane has how many structural isomers?,1,2,3,4,B,Butane has two isomers: n-butane and isobutane.
67,Chemistry,Inorganic,Metals,Metals are generally:,Poor conductors,Brittle,Good conductors,Liquids at room temp,C,Metals conduct heat and electricity well.
68,Chemistry,Physical Chemistry,Kinetics,Rate of reaction increases with:,Decrease in temperature,Increase in surface area,Decrease in concentration,Removal of catalyst,B,Greater surface area increases collisions so reaction is faster.
69,Chemistry,Organic,Alcohols,Ethanol belongs to:,Aldehyde,Carboxylic acid,Alcohol,Ester,C,Ethanol contains hydroxyl group so is an alcohol.
70,Chemistry,Inorganic,Oxidation,Oxidation involves:,Loss of electrons,Gaining electrons,Neither,Both,A,Oxidation is defined as loss of electrons.
71,Botany,Cell Biology,Cell Wall,Plant cell wall is mainly composed of:,Chitin,Cellulose,Peptidoglycan,Glycogen,B,Plant cell walls are made of cellulose.
72,Botany,Photosynthesis,Chloroplast,Chlorophyll is located in:,Cytoplasm,Nucleus,Grana,Ribosomes,C,Chlorophyll is present in thylakoid membranes of grana.
73,Botany,Genetics,Dominance,Genotype with identical alleles is called:,Heterozygous,Codominant,Recessive,Homozygous,D,Same alleles = homozygous.
74,Botany,Plant Physiology,Transpiration,Transpiration rate increases with:,High humidity,Low temperature,Wind,Darkness,C,Wind removes moist air allowing faster evaporation.
75,Botany,Plant Morphology,Leaf Venation,Parallel venation is common in:,Dicots,Monocots,Ferns,Gymnosperms,B,Monocot leaves usually have parallel venation.
76,Botany,Plant Reproduction,Seed,Zygote develops into:,Fruit,Seed,Flower,Root,B,Zygote develops into seed which later germinates.
77,Botany,Tissue System,Meristem,Meristematic cells are:,Dead cells,Lignified,Actively dividing,Storage cells,C,Meristem cells divide continuously.
78,Botany,Ecology,Population,Group of same species in same area is:,Community,Ecosystem,Population,Biosphere,C,Population refers to same species living together.
79,Botany,Plant Physiology,Respiration,Respiration occurs in:,Chloroplast,Nucleus,Mitochondria,Ribosome,C,Mitochondria are site of cellular respiration.
80,Botany,Plant Anatomy,Xylem,Transports water:,From leaves to roots,From roots to leaves,Not transported,Stored in roots,B,Xylem carries water upward.
81,Zoology,Human Physiology,Blood,Normal human body temperature is:,36.5–37.5°C,30–35°C,39–42°C,25–30°C,A,Normal average is around 37°C.
82,Zoology,Human Anatomy,Skeleton,Number of vertebrae in adult human is:,26,33,30,28,A,Adults have 26 vertebrae (some fuse).
83,Zoology,Human Physiology,Excretion,Functional unit of kidney is:,Neuron,Nephron,Alveoli,Glomerulus,B,Nephron is the structural and functional unit of kidney.
84,Zoology,Cell Biology,Cell Division,Meiosis results in:,Diploid cells,Identical cells,Haploid cells,No cells,C,Meiosis produces haploid gametes.
85,Zoology,Nervous System,Brain,Center of intelligence is:,Cerebellum,Medulla,Cerebrum,Pons,C,Cerebrum controls thinking and memory.
86,Zoology,Endocrine System,Hormones,Thyroxine controls:,Blood sugar,Metabolism,Blood clotting,Heart rate,B,Thyroxine regulates metabolic rate.
87,Zoology,Reproduction,Gametes,Gametes are:,Diploid,Haploid,Triploid,Tetraploid,B,Gametes contain half genetic material = haploid.
88,Zoology,Microbiology,Bacteria,Bacteria reproduce by:,Binary fission,Budding,Conjugation,Spore formation,A,Binary fission is common asexual reproduction.
89,Zoology,Respiration,Gas Exchange,Oxygen is transported mainly by:,Plasma,Hemoglobin,Platelets,WBCs,B,Hemoglobin binds oxygen in RBCs.
90,Zoology,Digestive System,Enzymes,Amylase digests:,Proteins,Fats,Starch,Vitamins,C,Amylase breaks down starch into sugars.
91,MAT,Arithmetic,Percentage,40% of 250 is:,50,80,100,120,C,0.40 × 250 = 100.
92,MAT,Logic,Odd One Out,Odd one out:, Lion,Tiger,Leopard,Crocodile,D,Crocodile is reptile; others are mammals.
93,MAT,Series,Find next, 3 6 12 24 ... ,36,48,72,96,B,Sequence doubles so next is 48.
