"bio_0001","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which of the following tissues is responsible for secondary growth in dicot stems?","Intercalary meristem","Lateral meristem","Apical meristem","Dermal tissue","B","Lateral meristems cause secondary growth in dicot stems."
"bio_0003","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Vascular Bundles","In dicot stems, the vascular bundles are described as","Closed and scattered","Open and arranged in a ring","Closed and arranged in a ring","Open and scattered","B","Open vascular bundles in a ring allow secondary growth."
"bio_0004","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Echinodermata","Which group of animals is characterized by the presence of a water vascular system?","Annelida","Arthropoda","Echinodermata","Mollusca","C","Echinoderms have a water vascular system for movement."
"bio_0005","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for the initiation of seed dormancy?","Gibberellin","Abscisic acid","Cytokinin","Ethylene","B","Abscisic acid induces seed dormancy and inhibits germination."
"bio_0006","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot and Monocot Stems","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot stems but not monocot stems?","Vascular bundles are scattered","Presence of cambium","Closed vascular bundles","Absence of pith","B","Dicot stems have cambium that allows secondary growth."
"bio_0007","Biology","Zoology - Circulatory System","Frog Heart","In a frog's heart, the structure that prevents the mixing of oxygenated and deoxygenated blood is the","Tricuspid valve","Interatrial septum","Spiral valve","Semilunar valve","C","Spiral valve separates oxygenated and deoxygenated blood."
"bio_0008","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which of the following tissues is responsible for the secondary growth in dicot stems?","Vascular cambium","Epidermis","Palisade parenchyma","Endodermis","A","Vascular cambium adds secondary xylem and phloem."
"bio_0010","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for breaking seed dormancy and promoting germination?","Abscisic acid","Gibberellin","Ethylene","Cytokinin","B","Gibberellin breaks dormancy and promotes germination."
"bio_0012","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip is found in which of the following plant tissues?","Endodermis of roots","Cortex of stems","Phloem of leaves","Epidermis of flowers","A","Casparian strip in endodermis controls water flow to xylem."
"bio_0013","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Fertilization","Which of the following animals exhibits external fertilization?","Frog","Dog","Cow","Hen","A","Frog fertilization occurs externally in water."
"bio_0014","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which of the following tissues is responsible for the increase in the girth of dicot stems?","Cork cambium","Vascular cambium","Epidermis","Phloem","B","Vascular cambium produces secondary tissues for girth growth."
"bio_0015","Biology","Zoology - Circulatory System","Vertebrate Heart","Which of the following structures is present in the heart of all vertebrates?","Tricuspid valve","Vena cava","Sinus venosus","Pulmonary vein","C","Sinus venosus is found in all primitive vertebrate hearts."
"bio_0016","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot and Monocot Stems","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot stem but not of monocot stem?","Scattered vascular bundles","Presence of cambium","Closed vascular bundles","Absence of secondary growth","B","Dicot stems have open bundles with cambium present."
"bio_0017","Biology","Human Physiology","Digestive Enzymes","Which enzyme is secreted by the gastric glands of the stomach in infants to help in the digestion of milk protein?","Pepsin","Rennin","Trypsin","Amylase","B","Rennin coagulates milk protein for digestion in infants."
"bio_0018","Biology","Plant Morphology","Placentation","Which type of placentation is found in the ovary of Dianthus?","Axile","Marginal","Basal","Free central","D","Dianthus has free central placentation in its ovary."
"bio_0019","Biology","Zoology - Circulatory System","Fish Heart","In which of the following animals is the heart two-chambered?","Frog","Lizard","Shark","Pigeon","C","Shark has a two-chambered heart typical of fishes."
"bio_0020","Biology","Plant Morphology","Inflorescence","Which type of inflorescence is characterized by the youngest flowers at the base and oldest at the apex?","Cymose","Racemose","Capitulum","Umbel","B","Racemose inflorescence has youngest flowers at the base."
"bio_0022","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for the closing of stomata during water stress?","Gibberellin","Cytokinin","Abscisic acid","Ethylene","C","Abscisic acid causes stomatal closure during drought."
"bio_0023","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot and Monocot Stems","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot stem but not monocot stem in T.S.?","Scattered vascular bundles","Presence of cambium","Closed vascular bundles","Absence of cortex","B","Presence of cambium distinguishes dicot from monocot stems."
"bio_0024","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Parthenogenesis","In honey bees, the phenomenon where unfertilized eggs develop into males is called","Parthenogenesis","Polyembryony","Apomixis","Metamorphosis","A","Unfertilized eggs in bees develop into drones via parthenogenesis."
"bio_0025","Biology","Plant Diversity","Bryophytes","In which group of plants is the sporophyte completely dependent on the gametophyte for nutrition?","Bryophytes","Gymnosperms","Pteridophytes","Angiosperms","A","Sporophyte depends on gametophyte in bryophytes."
"bio_0026","Biology","Zoology - Mammals","Characteristics of Mammals","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of mammals?","Three-chambered heart","External fertilization","Presence of diaphragm","Scaly skin","C","Mammals have a diaphragm for respiration."
"bio_0027","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Tissue","Which of the following is a function of companion cells in phloem tissue?","Synthesize lignin for vessel walls","Assist sieve tube elements in translocation","Provide mechanical support","Store starch granules","B","Companion cells assist sieve tubes in food transport."
"bio_0028","Biology","Zoology - Circulation","Circulatory System","Which of the following animals exhibits a closed circulatory system?","Earthworm","Cockroach","Prawn","Housefly","A","Earthworm has a closed circulatory system with blood vessels."
"bio_0029","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","Casparian strips are present in the","Endodermis of roots","Cortex of stems","Pericycle of roots","Epidermis of leaves","A","Casparian strips are suberized bands in root endodermis."
"bio_0030","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Fertilization","Which one of the following animals exhibits external fertilization?","Frog","Dog","Cow","Parrot","A","Frog undergoes external fertilization in water."
"bio_0031","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Tissue","Which group of plants is characterized by the presence of sieve tubes and companion cells in their phloem?","Bryophytes","Pteridophytes","Gymnosperms","Angiosperms","D","Angiosperms have sieve tubes and companion cells."
"bio_0033","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Xylem Function","Which of the following tissues in plants is responsible for the movement of water and minerals from roots to leaves?","Phloem","Xylem","Cork","Collenchyma","B","Xylem conducts water and minerals upward in plants."
"bio_0035","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which of the following plant hormones is primarily responsible for inducing dormancy in seeds and buds?","Auxin","Gibberellin","Abscisic acid","Cytokinin","C","Abscisic acid induces dormancy in buds and seeds."
"bio_0036","Biology","Zoology - Circulatory System","Aves","In which group of animals is a four-chambered heart a characteristic feature?","Amphibians","Reptiles","Aves","Amphioxus","C","Birds (Aves) have a fully divided four-chambered heart."
"bio_0037","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Stem Structure","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot stem in transverse section?","Scattered vascular bundles","Vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Presence of bulliform cells","Closed vascular bundles","B","Dicot stems have vascular bundles in a ring arrangement."
"bio_0039","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Function","Which of the following tissues in angiosperms is responsible for the transport of organic nutrients primarily?","Xylem","Phloem","Collenchyma","Sclerenchyma","B","Phloem transports sugars and organic solutes."
"bio_0040","Biology","Zoology - Nervous System","Frog Sound Organs","In frogs, the organ that acts as a sound-producing structure is the","Nictitating membrane","Tympanum","Vocal sac","Cloaca","C","Male frogs use vocal sacs to produce mating calls."
"bio_0041","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a feature unique to monocot stems when compared to dicot stems?","Presence of vascular bundles in a ring","Vascular bundles are closed and scattered","Secondary growth is common","Presence of cambium between xylem and phloem","B","Monocot stems have closed and scattered vascular bundles."
"bio_0042","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Chordates","In which group of animals does the notochord persist throughout life?","Pisces","Cyclostomata","Urochordata","Cephalochordata","D","Cephalochordates retain the notochord throughout life."
"bio_0043","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which of the following tissues is responsible for the increase in girth of dicot stems?","Apical meristem","Intercalary meristem","Cork cambium","Vascular cambium","D","Vascular cambium contributes to secondary growth in stems."
"bio_0044","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","In mammals, which part of the nephron is primarily responsible for selective reabsorption of glucose?","Distal convoluted tubule","Loop of Henle","Proximal convoluted tubule","Collecting duct","C","Proximal convoluted tubule reabsorbs glucose actively."
"bio_0045","Biology","Plant Diversity","Bryophytes","In which of the following plant groups is the sporophyte completely dependent on the gametophyte for nutrition?","Bryophyta","Pteridophyta","Gymnosperms","Angiosperms","A","Sporophyte in bryophytes depends on gametophyte nutrition."
"bio_0047","Biology","Zoology - Mammals","Characteristics of Mammals","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of mammals but not present in other vertebrates?","Presence of a four-chambered heart","External fertilization","Mammary glands","Scales on the body","C","Mammals uniquely possess mammary glands."
"bio_0048","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Vascular Cambium Formation","In dicot stems, the vascular cambium is mainly formed by the activity of","Pericycle cells","Medullary ray cells and intrafascicular cambium","Pith cells","Endodermal cells","B","Vascular cambium arises from intrafascicular and ray cells."
"bio_0051","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a distinguishing feature of dicot stems when compared to monocot stems?","Presence of scattered vascular bundles","Absence of cambium","Vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Closed vascular bundles","C","Dicot stems have vascular bundles in a ring pattern."
"bio_0052","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Insects","The primary function of Malpighian tubules in insects is","Respiration","Excretion","Digestion","Reproduction","B","Malpighian tubules remove nitrogenous waste in insects."
"bio_0053","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis (C4 Pathway)","Which of the following is a C4 plant?","Rice","Wheat","Maize","Pea","C","Maize follows the C4 pathway for photosynthesis."
"bio_0054","Biology","Zoology - Endocrine System","Amphibian Metamorphosis","Which hormone is responsible for the metamorphosis of tadpoles into adult frogs?","Thyroxine","Adrenaline","Insulin","Glucagon","A","Thyroxine controls metamorphosis in amphibians."
"bio_0055","Biology","Plant Morphology","Fruits","Which of the following is an example of a parthenocarpic fruit?","Apple","Banana","Mango","Pomegranate","B","Banana develops without fertilization, forming seedless fruit."
"bio_0057","Biology","Plant Taxonomy","Fabaceae Family","In which of the following plant families is the fruit typically a legume?","Solanaceae","Fabaceae","Poaceae","Liliaceae","B","Fabaceae members produce leguminous fruits."
"bio_0058","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Onychophora","Which of the following is a connecting link between annelids and arthropods?","Peripatus","Limulus","Nereis","Palaemon","A","Peripatus shows features of both annelids and arthropods."
"bio_0059","Biology","Plant Morphology","Seeds","Which of the following is an example of a non-endospermic seed?","Wheat","Castor","Bean","Maize","C","Bean uses all endosperm during embryo development."
"bio_0060","Biology","Zoology - Circulatory System","Respiratory Pigment","In which animal is the respiratory pigment dissolved directly in plasma and not contained within blood cells?","Frog","Human","Cockroach","Pigeon","C","Cockroach has hemolymph with dissolved hemocyanin pigment."
"bio_0061","Biology","Biological Classification","Modes of Nutrition","Which of the following pairs is correctly matched with respect to their mode of nutrition?","Paramecium – Holozoic","Agaricus – Autotrophic","Ulothrix – Saprophytic","Cuscuta – Insectivorous","A","Paramecium feeds holozoically by engulfing food particles."
"bio_0062","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Annelida","The excretory organ in earthworm is","Malpighian tubules","Green glands","Nephridia","Flame cells","C","Earthworms excrete waste through nephridia."
"bio_0063","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","In dicot stems, the vascular bundles are","Scattered in the ground tissue","Arranged in a ring","Located only in the pith","Absent","B","Dicot stems have vascular bundles arranged in a ring."
"bio_0064","Biology","Zoology - Life Processes","Metamorphosis","Which animal exhibits metamorphosis during its life cycle?","Earthworm","Frog","Pigeon","Rabbit","B","Frog undergoes metamorphosis from tadpole to adult."
"bio_0065","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Nitrogenous Wastes","The primary nitrogenous waste excreted by adult amphibians is","Ammonia","Urea","Uric acid","Creatinine","B","Adult amphibians are ureotelic and excrete urea."
"bio_0066","Biology","Zoology - Circulation","Blood Composition","Which of the following animal tissues is responsible for the transport of oxygen in vertebrates?","Nervous tissue","Muscular tissue","Connective tissue","Epithelial tissue","C","Blood, a connective tissue, transports oxygen via hemoglobin."
"bio_0067","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for the dormancy of seeds and buds?","Gibberellin","Auxin","Abscisic acid","Cytokinin","C","Abscisic acid induces dormancy in seeds and buds."
"bio_0068","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Anomalous Secondary Growth","Which of the following plants exhibits anomalous secondary growth?","Wheat","Sunflower","Dracaena","Pea","C","Dracaena shows secondary growth in monocots abnormally."
"bio_0070","Biology","Plant Morphology","Leaf Venation","Which one of the following characteristics is typical of dicotyledonous leaves but not monocotyledonous leaves?","Parallel venation","Presence of bulliform cells","Reticulate venation","Sheathing leaf base","C","Dicot leaves show reticulate venation."
"bio_0071","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Reptiles","The major nitrogenous waste product in the excreta of reptiles is","Ammonia","Urea","Uric acid","Creatinine","C","Reptiles are uricotelic and excrete uric acid to conserve water."
"bio_0073","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Tissue","In which plant tissue are companion cells typically associated?","Xylem","Phloem","Cork","Collenchyma","B","Companion cells are found in phloem with sieve tubes."
"bio_0074","Biology","Human Reproduction","Male Reproductive System","Which of the following structures is not a part of the human male reproductive system?","Seminal vesicle","Epididymis","Fimbriae","Vas deferens","C","Fimbriae belong to the female reproductive system."
"bio_0075","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which one of the following is a characteristic feature of dicotyledonous stems but not monocotyledonous stems?","Vascular bundles are scattered","Presence of cambium between xylem and phloem","Absence of cortex","Closed vascular bundles","B","Dicots have cambium that enables secondary growth."
"bio_0077","Biology","Plant Reproduction","Anther Structure","Which of the following is NOT a function of the tapetum in angiosperm anthers?","Providing nourishment to developing microspores","Formation of pollen wall components","Supporting meiosis in microspore mother cells","Secretion of enzymes for pollen release","C","Tapetum nourishes microspores but not meiosis directly."
"bio_0079","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which of the following hormones is mainly responsible for the growth of lateral buds in plants?","Gibberellin","Cytokinin","Abscisic acid","Ethylene","B","Cytokinin promotes lateral bud growth."
"bio_0080","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Mammalian Development","In mammals, the structure responsible for oxygenated blood supply to the fetus is the","Amniotic sac","Placenta","Allantois","Yolk sac","B","Placenta exchanges nutrients and oxygen between mother and fetus."
"bio_0081","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Arthropoda","In which of the following phyla is the body typically divided into a head, thorax, and abdomen?","Mollusca","Annelida","Arthropoda","Echinodermata","C","Arthropods have a segmented body with head, thorax, and abdomen."
"bio_0082","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for inducing dormancy in seeds and buds?","Gibberellin","Cytokinin","Abscisic acid","Ethylene","C","Abscisic acid induces dormancy in plant organs."
"bio_0083","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which one of the following plant hormones is primarily responsible for inducing seed dormancy?","Gibberellin","Abscisic acid","Auxin","Ethylene","B","Abscisic acid inhibits seed germination by causing dormancy."
"bio_0084","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for promoting seed dormancy and inhibiting germination?","Auxin","Gibberellin","Abscisic acid","Cytokinin","C","Abscisic acid maintains dormancy and prevents germination."
"bio_0085","Biology","Human Physiology","Nervous System","Which structure in mammals is responsible for the production of cerebrospinal fluid?","Corpus callosum","Choroid plexus","Pineal gland","Hypothalamus","B","Choroid plexus secretes cerebrospinal fluid in the brain."
"bio_0086","Biology","Plant Morphology","Modified Organs","Which of the following plants exhibits phylloclade as its main photosynthetic organ?","Opuntia","Pisum","Solanum","Zea","A","Opuntia uses stem (phylloclade) for photosynthesis."
"bio_0087","Biology","Zoology - Circulation","Respiratory Pigments","In which animal is the respiratory pigment dissolved directly in plasma, rather than being contained within cells?","Frog","Cockroach","Rabbit","Pigeon","B","Cockroach hemolymph carries pigment dissolved in plasma."
"bio_0088","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot stem but not monocot stem?","Scattered vascular bundles","Presence of cambium","Closed vascular bundles","Large pith","B","Dicot stems have cambium that allows secondary growth."
"bio_0089","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a feature characteristic of dicotyledonous stem but not monocotyledonous stem?","Vascular bundles are scattered","Vascular bundles are closed","Presence of cambium between xylem and phloem","Absence of secondary growth","C","Cambium between xylem and phloem is typical of dicots."
"bio_0090","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","The hormone responsible for the ripening of fruits in plants is","Auxin","Ethylene","Gibberellin","Cytokinin","B","Ethylene triggers fruit ripening in plants."
"bio_0091","Biology","Plant Physiology","Mineral Nutrition","Which of the following is an example of a phloem mobile mineral in plants?","Calcium","Sulphur","Boron","Potassium","D","Potassium is a phloem-mobile element in plants."
"bio_0092","Biology","Plant Diversity","Gymnosperms","Which of the following is an example of a gymnosperm with pinnately compound leaves?","Cycas","Pinus","Cedrus","Ginkgo","A","Cycas has pinnately compound leaves among gymnosperms."
"bio_0093","Biology","Zoology - Circulation","Fish Circulation","In which animal does blood flow through the heart only once during each complete circuit of the body?","Frog","Lizard","Shark","Pigeon","C","Fish like sharks have a single circulation pathway."
"bio_0094","Biology","Plant Morphology","Leaf Venation","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicotyledonous leaves?","Parallel venation","Reticulate venation","Presence of bulliform cells","Closed vascular bundles","B","Dicot leaves show reticulate venation pattern."
"bio_0095","Biology","Zoology - Endocrine System","Amphibian Metamorphosis","The hormone responsible for the metamorphosis of tadpoles into adult frogs is","Insulin","Thyroxine","Adrenaline","Testosterone","B","Thyroxine controls amphibian metamorphosis."
"bio_0096","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a feature unique to dicot stems when compared to monocot stems?","Presence of scattered vascular bundles","Closed vascular bundles","Vascular cambium present between xylem and phloem","Absence of cortex","C","Dicots have vascular cambium for secondary growth."
"bio_0097","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which hormone is primarily responsible for the ripening of fruits in plants?","Ethylene","Cytokinin","Gibberellin","Abscisic acid","A","Ethylene regulates fruit ripening process."
"bio_0098","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which of the following plant hormones is primarily responsible for the promotion of cell elongation in stems?","Gibberellin","Ethylene","Abscisic acid","Cytokinin","A","Gibberellin promotes stem elongation and growth."
"bio_0099","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","Which structure in the mammalian nephron is mainly responsible for filtration of blood?","Loop of Henle","Bowman’s capsule","Collecting duct","Distal convoluted tubule","B","Bowman’s capsule filters blood in the nephron."
"bio_0100","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Birds","Which of the following is the main nitrogenous waste excreted by birds?","Urea","Uric acid","Ammonia","Creatinine","B","Birds excrete uric acid to conserve water."
"bio_0101","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","The tissue responsible for the increase in the girth of dicot stems is","Apical meristem","Intercalary meristem","Vascular cambium","Protoderm","C","Vascular cambium adds new tissues for stem thickening."
"bio_0102","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a feature of dicotyledonous stems but NOT monocotyledonous stems?","Vascular bundles are scattered","Presence of cambium","Closed vascular bundles","Absence of medullary rays","B","Dicot stems possess cambium between vascular tissues."
"bio_0103","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Fertilization","Which animal exhibits external fertilization?","Frog","Dog","Pigeon","Cow","A","Frog lays eggs externally where fertilization occurs."
"bio_0104","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which of the following plant hormones is primarily responsible for the breaking of seed dormancy and promoting germination?","Abscisic acid","Ethylene","Gibberellin","Cytokinin","C","Gibberellin promotes germination by breaking dormancy."
"bio_0106","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Function","Which of the following tissues in plants is responsible mainly for the transport of organic nutrients?","Xylem","Phloem","Collenchyma","Sclerenchyma","B","Phloem transports food from leaves to other parts."
"bio_0108","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which one of the following is the main photosynthetic tissue in the leaves of dicot plants?","Spongy mesophyll","Palisade parenchyma","Epidermis","Collenchyma","B","Palisade parenchyma performs most photosynthesis."
"bio_0109","Biology","Human Physiology","Endocrine System","Which hormone is primarily responsible for the development of secondary sexual characteristics in males?","Estrogen","Progesterone","Testosterone","Oxytocin","C","Testosterone regulates male secondary sex traits."
"bio_0110","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Pisces","Which of the following is an example of a cartilaginous fish?","Labeo","Rohu","Scoliodon","Catla","C","Scoliodon (dogfish) is a cartilaginous fish."
"bio_0111","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Root","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicotyledonous roots but not monocotyledonous roots?","Presence of pith","Radial vascular bundles","Exarch xylem","Secondary growth","D","Dicot roots show secondary growth, monocot roots do not."
"bio_0112","Biology","Zoology - Circulatory System","Reptiles","In which group of animals is the heart completely four-chambered?","Amphibians","Reptiles (except crocodiles)","Crocodiles","Fishes","C","Crocodiles have a fully divided four-chambered heart."
"bio_0113","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip found in the roots is chemically composed of","Lignin","Suberin","Cutin","Pectin","B","Casparian strip is made of suberin in endodermal cells."
"bio_0114","Biology","Zoology - Life Processes","Metamorphosis","Which one of the following animals exhibits metamorphosis during its life cycle?","Earthworm","Cockroach","Leech","Hydra","B","Cockroach undergoes incomplete metamorphosis."
"bio_0115","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip is found in which part of the plant root?","Cortex","Endodermis","Pericycle","Epidermis","B","Casparian strip occurs in the endodermis of roots."
"bio_0116","Biology","Zoology - Endocrine System","Insect Hormones","Which hormone is responsible for the process of moulting in insects?","Insulin","Ecdysone","Thyroxine","Oxytocin","B","Ecdysone triggers moulting in insects."
"bio_0117","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip, found in plant roots, is primarily composed of","Cellulose","Lignin","Pectin","Suberin","D","Casparian strip is made of suberin in endodermal cells."
"bio_0118","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip is found in the","Cortex of the root","Epidermis of the stem","Endodermis of the root","Pericycle of the stem","C","Casparian strip occurs in the root endodermis."
"bio_0119","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","In dicot stem, the vascular bundles are","Scattered throughout the ground tissue","Arranged in a ring","Absent","Conjoint and collateral but closed","B","Dicot stems have ring-arranged vascular bundles."
"bio_0120","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for the initiation of seed germination by breaking seed dormancy?","Gibberellin","Ethylene","Abscisic acid","Cytokinin","A","Gibberellin breaks dormancy and promotes germination."
"bio_0121","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for the closure of stomata during water stress?","Gibberellin","Cytokinin","Abscisic acid","Ethylene","C","Abscisic acid closes stomata to reduce water loss."
"bio_0122","Biology","Zoology - Respiration","Amphibians","In adult frogs, which structure is responsible for oxygen exchange when submerged in water?","Gills","Lungs","Moist skin","Buccal cavity","C","Adult frogs respire through moist skin in water."
"bio_0123","Biology","Plant Morphology","Stem Modification","Which of the following is an example of a stem modification for food storage?","Bulb of onion","Tuber of potato","Tendrils of pea","Corm of colocasia","B","Potato tuber is a stem modification storing starch."
"bio_0124","Biology","Plant Diversity","Bryophytes","Which group of plants is characterized by the presence of archegonia and flagellated sperm?","Gymnosperms","Bryophytes","Angiosperms","Algae","B","Bryophytes have archegonia and motile sperm."
"bio_0126","Biology","Zoology - Muscular System","Muscle Structure","The functional unit of contractile tissue in skeletal muscle is known as","Sarcomere","Myofibril","Sarcoplasm","Myosin","A","Sarcomere is the functional contractile unit of muscle."
"bio_0127","Biology","Plant Morphology","Stem Modification","Which one of the following plants exhibits phylloclade modification as an adaptation to arid conditions?","Opuntia","Pisum","Mangifera","Brassica","A","Opuntia stem acts as a phylloclade for photosynthesis."
"bio_0128","Biology","Zoology - Digestive System","Annelida","Which structure in earthworm acts as a temporary storage organ for food?","Gizzard","Crop","Buccal cavity","Intestine","B","Crop in earthworm stores food before digestion."
"bio_0129","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Anatomy","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot leaf anatomy?","Parallel venation","Presence of bulliform cells","Isobilateral symmetry","Presence of palisade parenchyma","D","Dicot leaves contain palisade parenchyma for photosynthesis."
"bio_0130","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Annelida","The main excretory organ in earthworm is","Malpighian tubule","Nephridia","Green gland","Flame cell","B","Nephridia remove nitrogenous waste in earthworms."
"bio_0131","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicotyledonous stems but not monocotyledonous stems?","Vascular bundles are scattered","Vascular bundles are closed","Vascular bundles are arranged in a ring","Phloem is present only on one side of xylem","C","Dicot stems have ring-arranged open vascular bundles."
