"bio_0169","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Echinodermata","In which phylum does the water vascular system serve as a primary means of locomotion?","Annelida","Arthropoda","Echinodermata","Mollusca","C","Echinoderms move using the water vascular system."
"bio_0170","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Insects","In which animal is malpighian tubules the main excretory organ?","Earthworm","Cockroach","Frog","Leech","B","Cockroach excretes through Malpighian tubules."
"bio_0172","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is characteristic of dicot stem anatomy but not monocot stem anatomy?","Vascular bundles are scattered","Presence of cambium between xylem and phloem","Closed vascular bundles","Absence of secondary growth","B","Dicot stems have cambium enabling secondary growth."
"bio_0173","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Fertilization","In which of the following animals does external fertilization occur?","Frog","Dog","Rabbit","Human","A","Frogs fertilize externally in water."
"bio_0174","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Periderm","The cork cells of bark in woody plants are impervious to water and gases due to the presence of:","Lignin","Suberin","Pectin","Cutin","B","Suberin makes cork cells waterproof."
"bio_0175","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Honeybee Colony","In honeybees, the function of the drone is to:","Collect nectar","Defend the hive","Fertilize the queen","Build honeycombs","C","Drones exist to mate with the queen bee."
"bio_0176","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip found in endodermal cells of plant roots is mainly composed of:","Suberin","Cellulose","Lignin","Pectin","A","Casparian strip is made of suberin in endodermal cells."
"bio_0177","Biology","Zoology - Circulatory System","Reptiles","In which animal is the heart completely four-chambered, preventing mixing of oxygenated and deoxygenated blood?","Frog","Crocodile","Lizard","Turtle","B","Crocodile has a fully divided four-chambered heart."
"bio_0178","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","In dicot stems, the vascular bundles are described as:","Scattered and closed","Arranged in a ring and open","Arranged in a ring and closed","Scattered and open","B","Dicot stems have open vascular bundles in a ring."
"bio_0179","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Fertilization","Which of the following is an example of an organism exhibiting external fertilization?","Frog","Human","Dog","Cow","A","Frog reproduces by external fertilization."
"bio_0180","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","Which of the following is the primary function of casparian strip in plant roots?","Prevention of water loss","Facilitation of active transport","Blockage of apoplastic pathway","Enhancement of root hair formation","C","Casparian strip blocks apoplastic movement into xylem."
"bio_0181","Biology","Human Physiology","Circulatory System","Which structure in the mammalian heart prevents the backflow of blood from the right ventricle to the right atrium?","Bicuspid valve","Pulmonary valve","Aortic valve","Tricuspid valve","D","Tricuspid valve stops backflow in right heart chambers."
"bio_0182","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot stem but not found in monocot stem?","Vascular bundles are scattered","Presence of cambium","Absence of secondary growth","Closed vascular bundles","B","Dicot stems have cambium for secondary growth."
"bio_0183","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Echinodermata","In which phylum does the body show radial symmetry in adults but bilateral symmetry in the larval stage?","Mollusca","Echinodermata","Arthropoda","Annelida","B","Echinoderms have bilateral larvae and radial adults."
"bio_0185","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Insects","The Malpighian tubules in insects are primarily involved in:","Gas exchange","Excretion of nitrogenous wastes","Digestion of proteins","Secretion of digestive enzymes","B","Malpighian tubules excrete nitrogenous waste in insects."
"bio_0186","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","In a dicot stem, the vascular bundles are characterized by being:","Scattered and closed","Radial and open","Conjoint and closed","Conjoint and open","D","Dicot stems have conjoint, collateral, and open bundles."
"bio_0187","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Insects","The primary function of Malpighian tubules in insects is:","Respiration","Excretion","Digestion","Reproduction","B","Insects use Malpighian tubules for excretion."
"bio_0188","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which of the following tissues is responsible for secondary growth in the stems of dicotyledonous plants?","Apical meristem","Intercalary meristem","Vascular cambium","Protoderm","C","Vascular cambium produces secondary xylem and phloem."
"bio_0190","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis (C4 Pathway)","Which of the following plants exhibits C4 photosynthetic pathway?","Wheat","Rice","Maize","Pea","C","Maize uses the C4 pathway for photosynthesis."
"bio_0191","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicotyledonous stems?","Closed vascular bundles","Scattered vascular bundles","Cambium present between xylem and phloem","Absence of endodermis","C","Dicot stems have cambium between xylem and phloem."
"bio_0194","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Function","Which plant tissue is responsible for the transport of organic nutrients from leaves to other parts of the plant?","Xylem","Phloem","Collenchyma","Sclerenchyma","B","Phloem translocates sugars and nutrients."
"bio_0195","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a distinguishing feature of dicot stems compared to monocot stems?","Presence of scattered vascular bundles","Vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Absence of cambium","Closed vascular bundles","B","Dicot stems have ring-arranged open bundles."
"bio_0196","Biology","Zoology - Circulatory System","Amphibians","In which animal does the heart consist of two auricles and one ventricle?","Frog","Cockroach","Human","Fish","A","Frog has a three-chambered heart with two atria and one ventricle."
"bio_0197","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which of the following is the main photosynthetic tissue in the leaves of most dicot plants?","Spongy parenchyma","Palisade parenchyma","Collenchyma","Sclerenchyma","B","Palisade parenchyma performs photosynthesis."
"bio_0199","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which of the following plant tissues is responsible for the increase in the girth of dicot stems?","Apical meristem","Intercalary meristem","Vascular cambium","Epidermis","C","Vascular cambium increases girth through secondary growth."
"bio_0200","Biology","Cell Biology","Metabolism","In which organelle of animal cells does the beta-oxidation of fatty acids primarily occur?","Mitochondria","Nucleus","Golgi apparatus","Lysosome","A","Beta-oxidation occurs in mitochondria."
"bio_0201","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","Casparian strip is chemically composed of","Suberin","Lignin","Pectin","Cellulose","A","Casparian strip is suberized to block apoplastic transport."
"bio_0202","Biology","Human Physiology","Digestive System","The hormone responsible for stimulating the secretion of gastric juice in humans is","Secretin","Gastrin","Cholecystokinin","Enterokinase","B","Gastrin stimulates gastric juice secretion."
"bio_0204","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which of the following is primarily responsible for the opening and closing of stomata in leaves?","Guard cells","Trichomes","Palisade cells","Companion cells","A","Guard cells control stomatal opening and closing."
"bio_0205","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Echinodermata","In which phylum does the water vascular system function as a means of locomotion?","Annelida","Arthropoda","Echinodermata","Mollusca","C","Echinoderms move using the water vascular system."
"bio_0206","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","Which of the following statements correctly describes the function of the Casparian strip in plant roots?","It facilitates the passive movement of water into xylem","It prevents the backflow of phloem sap","It blocks the apoplastic pathway, forcing substances through the plasma membrane","It increases the surface area for absorption","C","Casparian strip forces water through endodermal membranes."
"bio_0207","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Echinodermata","In which phylum does the body exhibit radial symmetry in adults but bilateral symmetry in the larval stage?","Arthropoda","Mollusca","Echinodermata","Annelida","C","Echinoderms show bilateral larvae and radial adults."
"bio_0208","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which of the following is the main photosynthetic tissue in a typical dicotyledonous leaf?","Palisade parenchyma","Xylem","Phloem","Epidermis","A","Palisade parenchyma performs photosynthesis in leaves."
"bio_0209","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","In which part of the human nephron does selective reabsorption of glucose primarily occur?","Bowman’s capsule","Loop of Henle","Proximal convoluted tubule","Distal convoluted tubule","C","Proximal convoluted tubule reabsorbs glucose and ions."
"bio_0210","Biology","Plant Morphology","Phyllotaxy","In which type of phyllotaxy do leaves arise in pairs at each node, opposite to each other?","Alternate","Opposite","Whorled","Spiral","B","Opposite phyllotaxy has paired leaves at each node."
"bio_0211","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","Which of the following is the main function of casparian strip in roots?","Facilitating active uptake of minerals","Preventing apoplastic movement of water","Increasing root surface area","Promoting root hair formation","B","Casparian strip blocks apoplastic flow into xylem."
"bio_0212","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Function","Which of the following tissues in plants is mainly responsible for the translocation of organic nutrients?","Xylem","Phloem","Collenchyma","Sclerenchyma","B","Phloem transports sugars throughout the plant."
"bio_0213","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","In mammals, which structure is primarily responsible for the ultrafiltration of blood to form urine?","Collecting duct","Loop of Henle","Bowman’s capsule","Ureter","C","Bowman’s capsule performs ultrafiltration in the kidney."
"bio_0214","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Earthworm","In earthworms, which structure is involved in the storage of sperm received from another individual during copulation?","Clitellum","Seminal vesicles","Seminal receptacles","Nephridia","C","Seminal receptacles store received sperm."
"bio_0215","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Fertilization","In which animal does fertilization occur externally?","Frog","Cow","Dog","Pigeon","A","Frog reproduces by external fertilization."
"bio_0216","Biology","Plant Taxonomy","Fabaceae Family","Which of the following plant families is characterized by the presence of zygomorphic flowers and diadelphous stamens?","Fabaceae","Solanaceae","Liliaceae","Poaceae","A","Fabaceae flowers are zygomorphic with diadelphous stamens."
"bio_0217","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Tissue","In which plant tissue are sieve tubes and companion cells found together?","Xylem","Phloem","Cortex","Epidermis","B","Sieve tubes and companion cells occur in phloem."
"bio_0218","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Fertilization","Which of the following organisms exhibits external fertilization?","Earthworm","Frog","Pigeon","Rabbit","B","Frog shows external fertilization in water."
"bio_0219","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","Which of the following structures in plants is primarily responsible for the absorption of water and minerals from the soil?","Root hairs","Stomata","Lenticels","Leaf veins","A","Root hairs absorb water and minerals from soil."
"bio_0220","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Chordata","In which group of animals is the notochord present throughout life?","Urochordata","Cephalochordata","Vertebrata","Hemichordata","B","Cephalochordates retain the notochord for life."
"bio_0221","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which one of the following is the main photosynthetic tissue in the leaves of dicotyledonous plants?","Epidermis","Palisade parenchyma","Collenchyma","Phloem","B","Palisade parenchyma performs most photosynthesis."
"bio_0222","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Earthworm","Which structure in earthworm is responsible for secreting the cocoon during reproduction?","Clitellum","Setae","Prostomium","Nephridia","A","Clitellum secretes the cocoon in earthworms."
"bio_0223","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Annelida","In which of the following phyla does the body cavity originate as a split in mesodermal tissue?","Annelida","Arthropoda","Echinodermata","Mollusca","A","Annelids have a schizocoelous coelom formation."
"bio_0224","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which plant tissue is responsible for the increase in the girth of dicot stems?","Vascular cambium","Epidermis","Collenchyma","Xylem","A","Vascular cambium causes secondary thickening in stems."
"bio_0225","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a feature of dicotyledonous stems but not monocotyledonous stems?","Vascular bundles are scattered","Secondary growth is commonly present","Vascular bundles are closed","Fibrous root system is present","B","Dicot stems undergo secondary growth, unlike monocots."
"bio_0226","Biology","Plant Morphology","Placentation","Which type of placentation is found in the family Fabaceae?","Axile","Parietal","Marginal","Basal","C","Fabaceae shows marginal placentation in ovary."
"bio_0227","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","In which part of the human nephron does maximum reabsorption of glomerular filtrate occur?","Distal convoluted tubule","Proximal convoluted tubule","Loop of Henle","Collecting duct","B","Proximal convoluted tubule reabsorbs most filtrate."
"bio_0230","Biology","Human Physiology","Nervous System","The organ of Corti is a structure found in which part of the mammalian body?","Heart","Kidney","Inner ear","Eye","C","Organ of Corti in the cochlea detects sound vibrations."
"bio_0232","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","Which of the following is the primary function of the Casparian strip in plant roots?","Facilitating symbiotic nitrogen fixation","Preventing the passive flow of water and solutes into the stele","Enhancing photosynthesis in root cells","Transporting sugars from leaves to roots","B","Casparian strip regulates solute entry into vascular tissues."
"bio_0233","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Echinodermata","In which phylum would you most likely find animals exhibiting a water vascular system and tube feet?","Annelida","Arthropoda","Echinodermata","Mollusca","C","Echinoderms have a water vascular system for locomotion."
"bio_0234","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis","Which pigment is primarily responsible for the absorption of light during photosynthesis in higher plants?","Chlorophyll a","Carotene","Xanthophyll","Anthocyanin","A","Chlorophyll a captures light energy in photosynthesis."
"bio_0236","Biology","Plant Morphology","Phyllotaxy","Which of the following plants exhibits phyllotaxy in a whorled pattern?","Nerium","China rose","Mustard","Sunflower","A","Nerium shows whorled leaf arrangement at each node."
"bio_0237","Biology","Zoology - Endocrine System","Amphibian Metamorphosis","Which hormone is primarily responsible for the metamorphosis of tadpoles into adult frogs?","Thyroxine","Insulin","Adrenaline","Testosterone","A","Thyroxine controls metamorphosis in amphibians."
"bio_0238","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The casparian strip in plant roots is primarily found in which tissue?","Cortex","Pericycle","Endodermis","Epidermis","C","Casparian strip is present in endodermal cells of roots."
"bio_0239","Biology","Zoology - Circulatory System","Reptiles","In which of the following animals is the heart completely four-chambered?","Frog","Crocodile","Lizard","Turtle","B","Crocodiles have a four-chambered heart."
"bio_0240","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which one of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot stem but not monocot stem in transverse section?","Scattered vascular bundles","Presence of cambium","Closed vascular bundles","Absence of pith","B","Dicot stems possess cambium for secondary growth."
"bio_0242","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which of the following is the main photosynthetic tissue in the leaves of higher plants?","Epidermis","Palisade parenchyma","Phloem","Collenchyma","B","Palisade parenchyma performs photosynthesis."
"bio_0243","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Pisces","In which animal is the heart two-chambered, consisting of one atrium and one ventricle?","Frog","Lizard","Shark","Pigeon","C","Fish have a two-chambered heart with single circulation."
"bio_0245","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Tissue","In which of the following plant tissues are sieve tubes and companion cells found adjacent to each other?","Xylem","Phloem","Cork","Sclerenchyma","B","Sieve tubes and companion cells occur together in phloem."
"bio_0246","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Birds","Which of the following is the primary nitrogenous waste excreted by birds?","Ammonia","Urea","Uric acid","Creatinine","C","Birds excrete uric acid to conserve water."
"bio_0247","Biology","Cell Division","Mitosis","In which phase of mitosis do the sister chromatids separate and move towards opposite poles?","Prophase","Metaphase","Anaphase","Telophase","C","Anaphase involves separation of sister chromatids."
"bio_0248","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Mammals","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of mammals but NOT of other vertebrates?","Triploblastic body plan","Dorsal nerve cord","Presence of mammary glands","Closed circulatory system","C","Mammary glands are unique to mammals."
"bio_0249","Biology","Plant Diversity","Gymnosperms","In which of the following plants is the endosperm formed before fertilization?","Pinus","Wheat","Pea","Maize","A","Gymnosperms form endosperm before fertilization."
"bio_0250","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Reptiles","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of reptiles but not of amphibians?","Moist skin","External fertilization","Amniotic egg","Gills in larval stage","C","Reptiles lay amniotic eggs adapted to land."
"bio_0251","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for promoting cell elongation in stems?","Cytokinin","Abscisic acid","Gibberellin","Ethylene","C","Gibberellin promotes cell elongation and growth."
"bio_0252","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicotyledonous stem in transverse section?","Scattered vascular bundles","Vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Closed vascular bundles","Absence of cortex","B","Dicot stems have ring-arranged vascular bundles."
"bio_0253","Biology","Human Physiology","Nervous System","In mammals, the corpus callosum is primarily responsible for:","Regulating heartbeat","Connecting the two cerebral hemispheres","Secreting cerebrospinal fluid","Controlling voluntary muscle movement","B","Corpus callosum connects brain hemispheres."
"bio_0254","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for inducing seed dormancy?","Gibberellin","Auxin","Abscisic acid","Cytokinin","C","Abscisic acid induces seed dormancy."
"bio_0255","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Mammalian Reproduction","In mammals, the structure that directly connects the developing embryo to the maternal tissues for nutrient exchange is called:","Placenta","Umbilical cord","Amniotic sac","Yolk sac","A","Placenta allows exchange between mother and embryo."
"bio_0256","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which of the following is the main photosynthetic tissue in a dicot leaf?","Palisade parenchyma","Phloem","Epidermis","Spongy sclerenchyma","A","Palisade parenchyma performs photosynthesis."
"bio_0257","Biology","Plant Morphology","Leaf Venation","Which one of the following is a characteristic feature of dicotyledonous leaves?","Parallel venation","Reticulate venation","Whorled phyllotaxy","Presence of bulliform cells","B","Dicot leaves show reticulate venation."
"bio_0259","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a feature of dicotyledonous stem but not monocotyledonous stem?","Vascular bundles are arranged in a ring","Scattered vascular bundles","Closed vascular bundles","Presence of bulliform cells","A","Dicot stems have ring-arranged open vascular bundles."
"bio_0260","Biology","Cell Biology","Cell Organelles","Which organelle in animal cells is primarily responsible for the synthesis of steroid hormones?","Smooth endoplasmic reticulum","Golgi apparatus","Lysosome","Rough endoplasmic reticulum","A","Smooth ER synthesizes steroid hormones."
"bio_0261","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which meristem is responsible for the increase in girth of dicot stems?","Intercalary meristem","Apical meristem","Lateral meristem","Basal meristem","C","Lateral meristem causes secondary thickening."
"bio_0262","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which of the following is the main photosynthetic tissue in a typical dicot leaf?","Palisade parenchyma","Collenchyma","Phloem","Epidermis","A","Palisade parenchyma carries out photosynthesis."
"bio_0263","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicotyledonous stems but NOT monocotyledonous stems?","Vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Scattered vascular bundles","Absence of cambium","Closed vascular bundles","A","Dicot stems have open ringed vascular bundles."
"bio_0265","Biology","Zoology - Circulatory System","Reptiles","In which of the following animals is the heart four-chambered but both oxygenated and deoxygenated blood get mixed?","Crocodile","Pigeon","Turtle","Frog","C","Turtle heart allows partial mixing despite three chambers."
"bio_0266","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for promoting the elongation of internodes in deepwater rice?","Ethylene","Abscisic acid","Gibberellin","Cytokinin","C","Gibberellin promotes internodal elongation."
"bio_0267","Biology","Zoology - Muscular System","Muscle Structure","The functional unit of a striated muscle fiber responsible for contraction is called","Myofibril","Sarcomere","Sarcoplasm","Myosin","B","Sarcomere is the contractile unit of muscle."
"bio_0268","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which one of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot leaf anatomy?","Presence of parallel venation","Stomata only on the upper surface","Palisade mesophyll present beneath the upper epidermis","Bulliform cells in the epidermis","C","Dicot leaves have palisade mesophyll under upper epidermis."
"bio_0269","Biology","Plant Reproduction","Seeds","Which of the following is a non-endospermic seed?","Pea","Castor","Maize","Coconut","A","Pea is a non-endospermic dicot seed."
"bio_0271","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","In dicot stems, the vascular bundles are arranged in which of the following ways?","Scattered throughout the ground tissue","Arranged in a ring","Concentrated at the center","Arranged in parallel rows","B","Dicot stems have vascular bundles in a ring."
"bio_0272","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Earthworm","Which structure in earthworms is responsible for the secretion of cocoon during reproduction?","Clitellum","Setae","Nephridia","Prostomium","A","Clitellum secretes the cocoon in earthworm reproduction."
"bio_0273","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Insects","In which group of animals is the excretory organ known as Malpighian tubules found?","Insects","Molluscs","Echinoderms","Annelids","A","Malpighian tubules excrete waste in insects."
"bio_0274","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which one of the following is a feature of dicot stem but not monocot stem in T.S.?","Vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Vascular bundles are scattered","Closed vascular bundles","Absence of cambium","A","Dicot stems have ring-arranged open vascular bundles."
"bio_0275","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis","Which of the following is an example of a plant showing CAM (Crassulacean Acid Metabolism) pathway?","Opuntia","Wheat","Rice","Sunflower","A","Opuntia performs CAM photosynthesis."
"bio_0276","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Echinodermata","In which phylum do animals possess a water vascular system for locomotion?","Echinodermata","Annelida","Arthropoda","Mollusca","A","Echinoderms use a water vascular system for movement."
"bio_0277","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which one of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot stem but not of monocot stem?","Vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Scattered vascular bundles","Presence of bulliform cells","Closed vascular bundles","A","Dicot stems have vascular bundles arranged in a ring."
"bio_0278","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Insects","The Malpighian tubules of insects primarily function in","Excretion of nitrogenous wastes","Respiration","Digestion of food","Circulation of blood","A","Malpighian tubules excrete nitrogenous waste."
"bio_0279","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","Which of the following is a distinguishing feature of dicotyledonous stems when viewed in a transverse section?","Vascular bundles are scattered throughout the ground tissue","Vascular bundles are arranged in a ring","Presence of large air cavities","Each vascular bundle is surrounded by a bundle sheath","B","Dicot stems have ring-arranged vascular bundles."
"bio_0280","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Echinodermata","In which phylum does the water vascular system primarily function in locomotion and food capture?","Arthropoda","Echinodermata","Mollusca","Annelida","B","Echinoderms use the water vascular system for movement."
"bio_0281","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Annelida","In earthworm, nephridia are primarily involved in the process of","Excretion","Respiration","Digestion","Reproduction","A","Nephridia excrete nitrogenous waste in earthworms."
"bio_0282","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Monocot vs Dicot Root","Which one of the following is a distinguishing feature of monocotyledonous roots?","Presence of many vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Secondary growth is common","Pith is well developed","Cortex is absent","C","Monocot roots have a large central pith."
"bio_0284","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Annelida","In which of the following groups do all members possess a true coelom?","Platyhelminthes","Annelida","Cnidaria","Porifera","B","Annelids have a true coelom."
"bio_0285","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for inducing seed dormancy in adverse conditions?","Auxin","Gibberellin","Abscisic acid","Cytokinin","C","Abscisic acid induces dormancy under stress."
"bio_0286","Biology","Plant Morphology","Phyllotaxy","Which of the following plants exhibit phyllotaxy in a whorled arrangement?","China rose","Guava","Alstonia","Mustard","C","Alstonia shows whorled phyllotaxy."
"bio_0287","Biology","Zoology - Nervous System","Frog","In frogs, the tympanum is responsible for which of the following functions?","Production of digestive enzymes","Regulation of body temperature","Reception of sound waves","Exchange of gases","C","Tympanum receives sound vibrations in frogs."
"bio_0288","Biology","Plant Reproduction","Double Fertilisation","In angiosperms, double fertilisation results in the formation of","zygote and antipodal cells","zygote and endosperm","endosperm and synergids","zygote and nucellus","B","Double fertilisation produces zygote and endosperm."
"bio_0289","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis (C4 Pathway)","Which one of the following is a C4 plant that efficiently fixes carbon dioxide in hot and dry environments?","Wheat","Rice","Maize","Pea","C","Maize follows the C4 carbon fixation pathway."
"bio_0291","Biology","Plant Reproduction","Fertilisation","In which of the following plants does double fertilization occur?","Pinus","Cycas","Mango","Funaria","C","Double fertilisation is unique to angiosperms like Mango."
"bio_0292","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Annelida","Which structure in an earthworm is primarily responsible for the excretion of metabolic wastes?","Malpighian tubules","Nephridia","Green glands","Flame cells","B","Nephridia remove waste in earthworms."
"bio_0293","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which of the following tissues is responsible for the secondary growth in the stems of dicotyledonous plants?","Cork cambium","Intercalary meristem","Apical meristem","Protoderm","A","Cork cambium produces protective outer layers."
"bio_0296","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","Which of the following is a distinguishing feature of dicot stems when observed in a transverse section?","Scattered vascular bundles","Vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Absence of endodermis","Presence of bulliform cells","B","Dicot stems show ring-arranged vascular bundles."
"bio_0297","Biology","Plant Morphology","Stem Modification","Which one of the following plants is an example of a stem succulent adapted to arid environments?","Opuntia","Pisum","Zea","Solanum","A","Opuntia stem stores water and performs photosynthesis."
"bio_0348","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Echinodermata","In which of the following animal phyla is the presence of a water vascular system a characteristic feature?","Annelida","Echinodermata","Arthropoda","Mollusca","B","Echinoderms possess a water vascular system for locomotion."
"bio_0349","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Annelida","Which of the following animals possesses a true coelom derived from mesoderm?","Planaria","Ascaris","Earthworm","Tapeworm","C","Earthworm has a true coelom lined by mesoderm."
"bio_0351","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which one of the following plant hormones is primarily responsible for promoting cell elongation in stems?","Gibberellin","Cytokinin","Abscisic acid","Ethylene","A","Gibberellin promotes elongation of stem cells."
"bio_0352","Biology","Human Physiology","Muscular System","In which of the following animal tissues would you expect to find intercalated discs?","Smooth muscle","Skeletal muscle","Cardiac muscle","Areolar connective tissue","C","Cardiac muscles contain intercalated discs."
"bio_0353","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Insects","The Malpighian tubules in insects are chiefly involved in:","Respiration","Excretion","Digestion","Circulation","B","Malpighian tubules remove nitrogenous wastes."
"bio_0354","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which plant tissue is responsible for the increase in the girth of stems and roots in dicot plants?","Intercalary meristem","Apical meristem","Vascular cambium","Epidermis","C","Vascular cambium enables secondary thickening."
"bio_0355","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Annelida","In which phylum do animals first exhibit a true coelom lined by mesodermal tissue?","Annelida","Platyhelminthes","Cnidaria","Porifera","A","Annelids show the first true coelom."
"bio_0356","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","In which plant tissue are casparian strips found, helping to regulate the movement of water and minerals?","Phloem","Cortex","Endodermis","Pericycle","C","Casparian strip occurs in the endodermis of roots."
"bio_0357","Biology","Zoology - Endocrine System","Insects","The process of ecdysis in arthropods is primarily controlled by which hormone?","Ecdysone","Insulin","Thyroxine","Adrenaline","A","Ecdysone triggers molting in arthropods."
"bio_0358","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Tissue","Which one of the following tissues in plants is primarily responsible for the transport of organic nutrients?","Xylem","Phloem","Collenchyma","Sclerenchyma","B","Phloem transports organic food from leaves."
"bio_0359","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Mammals","Which structure is characteristic of a mammalian nephron but absent in invertebrate excretory systems?","Loop of Henle","Malpighian tubule","Green gland","Flame cell","A","Loop of Henle is unique to mammalian nephrons."
"bio_0360","Biology","Zoology - Circulation","Reptiles","In which animal is the presence of a four-chambered heart an adaptation for complete separation of oxygenated and deoxygenated blood?","Frog","Lizard","Crocodile","Fish","C","Crocodiles have a fully divided four-chambered heart."
"bio_0361","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which of the following features is characteristic of dicot leaf anatomy but absent in monocot leaves?","Presence of palisade parenchyma","Parallel venation","Bulliform cells","Stomata on both surfaces","A","Dicot leaves have palisade parenchyma below the upper epidermis."
"bio_0362","Biology","Cell Biology","Cell Cycle","In which phase of the cell cycle does the replication of DNA take place in animal cells?","G1 phase","S phase","G2 phase","M phase","B","DNA replication occurs during the S phase."
"bio_0363","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicotyledonous roots but NOT monocotyledonous roots?","Presence of a well-developed pith","Exarch xylem","Polyarch vascular bundles","Secondary growth is common","D","Dicot roots show secondary growth due to cambium."
"bio_0365","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","Which of the following is the main function of the Casparian strip in plant roots?","Facilitating water absorption by osmosis","Restricting the passive flow of substances into the vascular cylinder","Enhancing photosynthesis in root cells","Transporting sugars from leaves to roots","B","Casparian strip regulates selective uptake into stele."
"bio_0367","Biology","Plant Morphology","Placentation","In which type of placentation are the ovules borne on a central axis with no septa between them?","Axile","Parietal","Free central","Marginal","C","Free central placentation lacks septa between locules."
"bio_0368","Biology","Biomolecules","Proteins","Which of the following is the most abundant protein in the animal world?","Collagen","Keratin","Myosin","Elastin","A","Collagen is the most abundant structural protein."
"bio_0369","Biology","Plant Physiology","Transpiration","Which of the following is NOT a function of the stomata in plants?","Facilitating gaseous exchange","Regulating transpiration","Absorbing mineral ions","Controlling water loss","C","Stomata do not absorb minerals from soil."
"bio_0371","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretion","In mammals, which organ is responsible for the production of urea?","Kidney","Liver","Lung","Pancreas","B","Liver converts ammonia to urea by the ornithine cycle."
"bio_0372","Biology","Plant Morphology","Inflorescence","Which type of inflorescence is characterized by the youngest flower being at the base and older flowers towards the apex?","Racemose","Cyathium","Cymose","Verticillaster","C","Cymose inflorescence shows basipetal succession."
"bio_0373","Biology","Plant Morphology","Phyllotaxy","Which of the following plants exhibits phyllotaxy in which leaves are arranged in pairs at each node, opposite to each other?","Hibiscus rosa-sinensis","Calotropis procera","Nerium indicum","China rose","C","Nerium shows opposite phyllotaxy."
"bio_0375","Biology","Plant Morphology","Stem Modification","Which of the following plants exhibits phylloclade modification to adapt to arid environments?","Opuntia","Pisum","Brassica","Mango","A","Opuntia uses stem for photosynthesis and water storage."
"bio_0376","Biology","Zoology - Circulation","Arthropoda","In which animal is the circulatory system described as being open type?","Earthworm","Cockroach","Frog","Human","B","Cockroach has an open circulatory system."
"bio_0377","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which of the following plant tissues is responsible for the secondary growth in dicot stems?","Phellogen","Vascular cambium","Epidermis","Collenchyma","B","Vascular cambium adds secondary xylem and phloem."
"bio_0378","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Cnidaria","In which phylum do animals exhibit radial symmetry and possess cnidocytes?","Annelida","Arthropoda","Cnidaria","Platyhelminthes","C","Cnidarians have cnidocytes for defense and capturing prey."
"bio_0379","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Xylem Tissue","Which one of the following plant tissues is responsible for the movement of water and minerals from roots to leaves?","Phloem","Xylem","Collenchyma","Epidermis","B","Xylem conducts water and dissolved minerals."
"bio_0380","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which one of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot stem but not monocot stem?","Scattered vascular bundles","Presence of cambium","Large pith","Closed vascular bundles","B","Dicot stems have cambium enabling secondary growth."
"bio_0381","Biology","Zoology - Respiration","Annelida","In earthworm, the respiratory exchange of gases occurs primarily through","Lungs","Moist skin","Gills","Book lungs","B","Earthworms respire through moist skin."
"bio_0382","Biology","Plant Reproduction","Seeds","Which one of the following is a non-endospermic seed?","Castor","Wheat","Pea","Maize","C","Pea is non-endospermic as cotyledons store food."
"bio_0384","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Platyhelminthes","In which animal is flame cell a part of the excretory system?","Earthworm","Cockroach","Planaria","Frog","C","Planaria excretes using flame cells."
"bio_0385","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Mammals","In mammals, the structure responsible for the filtration of blood in the nephron is the","Loop of Henle","Bowman’s capsule","Collecting duct","Distal convoluted tubule","B","Bowman’s capsule filters blood plasma in kidneys."
"bio_0387","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis (C4 Pathway)","Which one of the following is a C4 plant that shows Kranz anatomy?","Wheat","Rice","Maize","Pea","C","Maize shows Kranz anatomy typical of C4 plants."
"bio_0389","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","Which part of the root is primarily responsible for the absorption of water and minerals in plants?","Zone of elongation","Root cap","Root hair zone","Zone of maturation","C","Root hair zone absorbs water and minerals."
"bio_0390","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Xylem Tissue","In which plant tissue are tracheids and vessel elements primarily found?","Phloem","Xylem","Collenchyma","Epidermis","B","Tracheids and vessels are xylem elements."
"bio_0392","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Tissue","Which of the following tissues in plants is responsible for the transport of organic nutrients?","Xylem","Phloem","Collenchyma","Sclerenchyma","B","Phloem carries food from leaves to other parts."
"bio_0393","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Insects","In which animal does the process of metamorphosis occur during its life cycle?","Earthworm","Cockroach","Leech","Hydra","B","Cockroach undergoes incomplete metamorphosis."
"bio_0394","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","Which of the following cells in plant roots is responsible for the absorption of water and minerals from the soil?","Cortex cells","Root hair cells","Endodermal cells","Pericycle cells","B","Root hairs absorb water and minerals."
"bio_0395","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Echinodermata","In which phylum do animals possess a water vascular system used for locomotion and feeding?","Arthropoda","Echinodermata","Annelida","Mollusca","B","Echinoderms use water vascular system for movement."
"bio_0396","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which tissue is responsible for the increase in girth of dicot stems?","Cork cambium","Interfascicular cambium","Vascular cambium","Apical meristem","C","Vascular cambium forms secondary tissues."
"bio_0397","Biology","Plant Reproduction","Fertilisation","Which of the following statements about double fertilization in angiosperms is correct?","Both male gametes fertilize two egg cells","One male gamete fuses with egg, other with polar nuclei","Both male gametes fuse with polar nuclei","One male gamete fuses with antipodal cells","B","One sperm fertilizes egg, another forms endosperm."
"bio_0399","Biology","Plant Morphology","Inflorescence","Which type of inflorescence is characterized by a main axis that grows indefinitely and bears flowers laterally in an acropetal succession?","Cymose","Racemose","Capitulum","Umbel","B","Racemose inflorescence has indefinite main axis."
"bio_0400","Biology","Human Physiology","Nervous System","In mammals, the corpus callosum is primarily responsible for","Connecting the two cerebral hemispheres","Regulating hormonal secretion","Controlling voluntary muscle movement","Initiating reflex actions","A","Corpus callosum connects brain hemispheres."
"bio_0401","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which of the following is the major photosynthetic tissue in leaves of higher plants?","Epidermis","Palisade mesophyll","Xylem","Phloem","B","Palisade mesophyll is the main photosynthetic layer."
"bio_0403","Biology","Zoology - Sensory System","Frog Anatomy","In frogs, the structure responsible for equalizing the pressure on both sides of the tympanum is the","Glottis","Eustachian tube","Cloaca","Vomerine teeth","B","Eustachian tube balances air pressure on the tympanum."
"bio_0404","Biology","Human Physiology","Endocrine & Nervous Control","Which part of the human brain is primarily responsible for regulating body temperature?","Medulla oblongata","Hypothalamus","Cerebellum","Cerebrum","B","Hypothalamus maintains body temperature and homeostasis."
"bio_0405","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for initiating seed dormancy?","Auxin","Gibberellin","Abscisic acid","Cytokinin","C","Abscisic acid induces seed dormancy and inhibits germination."
"bio_0406","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Insects","The Malpighian tubules in insects are mainly involved in","Digestion of proteins","Excretion of nitrogenous wastes","Respiration","Circulation of blood","B","Malpighian tubules remove nitrogenous waste from body fluid."
"bio_0407","Biology","Zoology - Endocrine System","Insects","Which hormone is primarily responsible for stimulating the process of ecdysis in insects?","Ecdysone","Auxin","Gibberellin","Thyroxine","A","Ecdysone triggers molting in insects."
"bio_0408","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The main function of casparian strips found in the endodermal cells of roots is to","Allow free movement of water in all directions","Prevent symplastic movement of ions","Block the apoplastic pathway, forcing substances through the plasma membrane","Facilitate passive absorption of minerals","C","Casparian strip blocks apoplastic flow into the stele."
"bio_0409","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Comparative Excretion","Which of the following animals is correctly matched with its excretory organs?","Earthworm – Malpighian tubules","Cockroach – Nephridia","Frog – Kidneys","Amoeba – Flame cells","C","Frogs excrete through kidneys like higher vertebrates."
"bio_0410","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","In dicot stems, the vascular bundles are characterized by which of the following arrangements?","Scattered throughout the ground tissue","Arranged in a ring","Concentrated at the center","Arranged in pairs","B","Dicot stems have vascular bundles in a ring."
"bio_0411","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Earthworm","Which of the following structures in earthworm is responsible for secreting the cocoon during reproduction?","Clitellum","Setae","Typhlosole","Nephridia","A","Clitellum secretes cocoon for fertilized eggs."
"bio_0412","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for promoting seed dormancy and inhibiting seed germination?","Gibberellin","Ethylene","Abscisic acid","Cytokinin","C","Abscisic acid promotes dormancy and prevents germination."
"bio_0413","Biology","Plant Reproduction","Double Fertilisation","In angiosperms, double fertilization results in the formation of","Two embryos","One embryo and one endosperm","Two endosperms","Two zygotes","B","Double fertilisation produces embryo and endosperm."
"bio_0414","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Comparative Excretion","Which of the following animals is correctly matched with its mode of excretion?","Cockroach – Urea","Frog – Ammonia","Human – Uric acid","Bird – Uric acid","D","Birds excrete uric acid to conserve water."
"bio_0415","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a distinguishing feature of dicot stem when compared to monocot stem in T.S.?","Vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Scattered vascular bundles","Absence of cambium","Vascular bundles are closed","A","Dicot stems show ring-arranged vascular bundles."
"bio_0416","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip found in the roots is composed primarily of","Cellulose","Suberin","Lignin","Cutin","B","Casparian strip contains suberin, making it impermeable."
"bio_0417","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Cnidaria","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of phylum Cnidaria?","Presence of nephridia","Radial symmetry","Segmented body","Triploblastic body plan","B","Cnidarians exhibit radial symmetry."
"bio_0418","Biology","Plant Morphology","Stem Modification","Which of the following plants is an example of a stem succulent adapted to arid environments?","Opuntia","Pisum","Zea","Oryza","A","Opuntia stores water in its green stem."
"bio_0419","Biology","Zoology - Circulation","Annelids","In which group of animals is the respiratory pigment dissolved directly in plasma rather than being contained within cells?","Mammals","Insects","Annelids","Reptiles","C","Annelids have hemoglobin dissolved in plasma."
"bio_0420","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which one of the following plant hormones is primarily responsible for cell elongation in stems?","Gibberellin","Cytokinin","Abscisic acid","Ethylene","A","Gibberellin enhances stem elongation."
"bio_0421","Biology","Zoology - Circulation","Insects","In which of the following animals is the respiratory pigment dissolved directly in plasma rather than contained within cells?","Cockroach","Frog","Human","Pigeon","A","Cockroaches lack blood pigments; oxygen diffuses via trachea."
"bio_0422","Biology","Plant Diversity","Bryophytes","In which group of plants is the sporophyte completely dependent on the gametophyte for its nutrition?","Bryophytes","Pteridophytes","Gymnosperms","Angiosperms","A","Bryophyte sporophyte depends on gametophyte for food."
"bio_0423","Biology","Human Physiology","Circulatory System","The nodal tissue responsible for initiating the heartbeat in humans is known as the","Atrioventricular node","Purkinje fibers","Sinoatrial node","Bundle of His","C","Sinoatrial node acts as the natural pacemaker."
"bio_0424","Biology","Plant Diversity","Cyanobacteria","Which one of the following is an example of a symbiotic nitrogen-fixing cyanobacterium found in the coralloid roots of Cycas?","Anabaena","Frankia","Rhizobium","Azotobacter","A","Anabaena lives symbiotically in Cycas roots."
"bio_0426","Biology","Plant Reproduction","Seeds","In which of the following plants is the endosperm completely consumed by the developing embryo before seed maturation?","Castor","Wheat","Pea","Coconut","C","Pea is a non-endospermic seed."
"bio_0427","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Insects","The Malpighian tubules in insects are primarily responsible for","Respiration","Excretion","Digestion","Circulation","B","Malpighian tubules excrete nitrogenous wastes."
"bio_0428","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Honeybee","In honey bees, the queen substance is primarily responsible for","Attracting drones during mating flights","Inhibiting the development of ovaries in worker bees","Stimulating the production of royal jelly by workers","Regulating the temperature inside the hive","B","Queen substance suppresses worker ovary development."
"bio_0429","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a distinguishing feature of dicot stems when viewed in transverse section?","Scattered vascular bundles","Vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Absence of cambium","Closed vascular bundles","B","Dicot stems have ring-shaped open vascular bundles."
"bio_0430","Biology","Human Physiology","Endocrine System","The hormone responsible for the stimulation of milk ejection (let-down) in mammals is","Prolactin","Oxytocin","Vasopressin","Luteinizing hormone","B","Oxytocin triggers milk ejection."
"bio_0431","Biology","Zoology - Endocrine System","Arthropods","The hormone responsible for the molting process in arthropods is","Oxytocin","Thyroxine","Ecdysone","Insulin","C","Ecdysone controls molting in arthropods."
"bio_0432","Biology","Plant Morphology","Phyllotaxy","Which type of phyllotaxy is found in the leaves of Nerium?","Alternate","Opposite","Whorled","Rosette","C","Nerium shows whorled phyllotaxy."
"bio_0433","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Mammals","Which of the following animals is a viviparous mammal?","Platypus","Kangaroo","Crocodile","Turtle","B","Kangaroos give birth to young ones (viviparous)."
"bio_0434","Biology","Zoology - Circulation","Arthropods","In which animal is the circulatory system of the open type?","Earthworm","Frog","Cockroach","Human","C","Cockroach has an open circulatory system."
"bio_0435","Biology","Plant Diversity","Algae","Which of the following is a non-motile, colonial, freshwater green alga?","Spirogyra","Volvox","Chlamydomonas","Ulothrix","B","Volvox forms colonies of flagellated cells."
"bio_0437","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Primary Growth","Which of the following plant tissues is responsible for the formation of primary xylem and primary phloem?","Cork cambium","Interfascicular cambium","Vascular cambium","Procambium","D","Procambium forms primary vascular tissues."
"bio_0438","Biology","Human Physiology","Reproductive System","In mammals, which of the following structures is directly involved in the production of testosterone?","Seminiferous tubules","Leydig cells","Epididymis","Sertoli cells","B","Leydig cells secrete testosterone."
"bio_0439","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Echinodermata","Which of the following is a character exclusive to members of the phylum Echinodermata?","Presence of book lungs","Water vascular system","Segmented body","Exoskeleton of chitin","B","Echinoderms possess a unique water vascular system."
"bio_0440","Biology","Plant Reproduction","Double Fertilisation","In the process of double fertilization in angiosperms, one male gamete fuses with the egg while the other fuses with:","Synergid","Antipodal cell","Central cell","Nucellus","C","One sperm fertilizes egg; other fuses with central cell."
"bio_0441","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis","Which of the following is the principal photosynthetic pigment in cyanobacteria?","Chlorophyll a","Chlorophyll b","Phycoerythrin","Carotene","A","Cyanobacteria primarily use chlorophyll a."
"bio_0443","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","In which part of the nephron does maximum reabsorption of glomerular filtrate occur?","Distal convoluted tubule","Loop of Henle","Proximal convoluted tubule","Collecting duct","C","Proximal convoluted tubule reabsorbs most filtrate."
"bio_0444","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Collenchyma","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of collenchyma cells in plants?","Thick lignified secondary walls","Irregularly thickened cell corners","Large central vacuole","Presence of pits and perforations","B","Collenchyma has irregularly thickened corners."
"bio_0445","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which one of the following tissues is responsible for the secondary growth in dicot stems?","Cork cambium","Apical meristem","Intercalary meristem","Epidermis","A","Cork cambium adds protective secondary tissues."
"bio_0446","Biology","Human Physiology","Digestive System","The enzyme pepsin is secreted in an inactive form called:","Trypsinogen","Chymotrypsinogen","Procarboxypeptidase","Pepsinogen","D","Pepsinogen is activated to pepsin by HCl."
"bio_0447","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which plant tissue is responsible for the formation of annual rings in woody dicots?","Cork cambium","Intercalary meristem","Vascular cambium","Apical meristem","C","Vascular cambium forms annual rings."
"bio_0448","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Arthropods","Which one of the following animals is a uricotelic organism?","Frog","Human","Cockroach","Earthworm","C","Cockroach excretes uric acid."
"bio_0449","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot vs Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicotyledonous stems in transverse section?","Vascular bundles are scattered","Vascular bundles are arranged in a ring","Cambium is absent","Bundle sheath is well-developed","B","Dicot stems show ringed open vascular bundles."
"bio_0450","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis","Which of the following is the major photosynthetic pigment in higher plants?","Chlorophyll a","Chlorophyll b","Carotene","Xanthophyll","A","Chlorophyll a is the main pigment of photosynthesis."
"bio_0451","Biology","Zoology - Circulation","Reptiles","In which of the following animals is a four-chambered heart present?","Frog","Lizard","Crocodile","Turtle","C","Crocodiles have a four-chambered heart."
"bio_0453","Biology","Zoology - Diseases","Protozoan Diseases","Which of the following diseases is caused by a protozoan parasite in humans?","Amoebiasis","Tuberculosis","Ringworm","Ascariasis","A","Amoebiasis is caused by Entamoeba histolytica."
"bio_0454","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","In dicot stems, the vascular bundles are best described as:","Scattered and closed","Arranged in a ring and open","Scattered and open","Arranged in a ring and closed","B","Dicot stems have ringed open vascular bundles."
"bio_0455","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which one of the following is the main photosynthetic tissue in the leaves of higher plants?","Phloem","Xylem","Palisade parenchyma","Collenchyma","C","Palisade parenchyma performs photosynthesis."
"bio_0456","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Arthropoda","The exoskeleton of arthropods is primarily composed of which substance?","Cellulose","Chitin","Pectin","Keratin","B","Arthropod exoskeleton is made of chitin."
"bio_0457","Biology","Plant Morphology","Leaf Structure","Which of the following plants exhibits a pinnately compound leaf?","Neem","Lotus","China rose","Mustard","A","Neem has pinnately compound leaves."
"bio_0458","Biology","Zoology - Endocrine System","Insects","The hormone responsible for molting in insects is:","Ecdysone","Thyroxine","Adrenaline","Insulin","A","Ecdysone induces molting in insects."
"bio_0459","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Birds","In which animal does internal fertilization occur?","Frog","Earthworm","Pigeon","Fish","C","Pigeon undergoes internal fertilization."
"bio_0460","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Xylem Tissue","Which of the following plant tissues is responsible for the movement of water and minerals from roots to leaves?","Phloem","Sclerenchyma","Xylem","Collenchyma","C","Xylem transports water and minerals."
"bio_0461","Biology","Plant Morphology","Inflorescence","Which type of inflorescence is characterized by the youngest flowers located at the base and older flowers towards the apex?","Cymose","Racemose","Umbel","Capitulum","B","Racemose inflorescence shows acropetal succession."
"bio_0462","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Mammals","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of mammals but not of other vertebrates?","Triploblastic organization","Presence of gills at any life stage","Mammary glands","Internal fertilization","C","Mammals possess mammary glands."
"bio_0463","Biology","Plant Diversity","Algae","Which of the following is a major photosynthetic pigment found in red algae?","Chlorophyll b","Phycoerythrin","Carotene","Xanthophyll","B","Red algae contain phycoerythrin pigment."
"bio_0466","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Periderm","The cork cells in plants are impervious to water and gases due to the presence of which substance in their cell walls?","Lignin","Suberin","Cutin","Pectin","B","Suberin makes cork cells waterproof."
"bio_0467","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Annelida","Which one of the following animals possesses a true coelom lined by mesodermal epithelium?","Ascaris","Earthworm","Planaria","Hydra","B","Earthworm has a true coelom."
"bio_0468","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip in plant roots is primarily found in which cell layer?","Cortex","Endodermis","Pericycle","Epidermis","B","Casparian strip is found in the endodermis."
"bio_0469","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Aves","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of aves (birds)?","Presence of mammary glands","Three-chambered heart","Feathers and pneumatic bones","External fertilization","C","Birds have feathers and pneumatic bones."
"bio_0470","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Insects","Which one of the following animals exhibits metamorphosis during its development?","Earthworm","Cockroach","Pigeon","Rabbit","B","Cockroach undergoes metamorphosis."
"bio_0471","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for promoting lateral bud growth and overcoming apical dominance?","Auxin","Cytokinin","Gibberellin","Abscisic acid","B","Cytokinin promotes lateral bud growth."
"bio_0473","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","In dicot stems, the vascular bundles are arranged in which of the following patterns?","Scattered throughout the ground tissue","In a ring surrounding the pith","Radially along the epidermis","Concentrated at the center of the stem","B","Dicot stems show ringed vascular arrangement."
"bio_0474","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Annelids","Which of the following is the excretory organ in earthworms?","Malpighian tubules","Nephridia","Flame cells","Green glands","B","Earthworms excrete through nephridia."
"bio_0475","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which of the following plant hormones is primarily responsible for promoting fruit ripening in climacteric fruits?","Gibberellin","Ethylene","Cytokinin","Auxin","B","Ethylene promotes fruit ripening."
"bio_0476","Biology","Plant Morphology","Inflorescence","Which type of inflorescence is characterized by older flowers at the base and younger flowers towards the apex?","Cymose","Racemose","Capitulum","Umbel","B","Racemose inflorescence grows indefinitely."
"bio_0477","Biology","Plant Morphology","Inflorescence","Which type of inflorescence is characterized by the main axis ending in a flower and further growth continuing through lateral branches?","Racemose","Cymose","Capitulum","Spikelet","B","Cymose inflorescence has a determinate axis."
"bio_0478","Biology","Cell Biology","Meiosis","In which phase of meiosis do homologous chromosomes undergo crossing over?","Metaphase I","Prophase I","Anaphase II","Telophase I","B","Crossing over occurs during prophase I."
"bio_0479","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip is a characteristic feature of which plant tissue?","Cortex","Phloem","Endodermis","Epidermis","C","Casparian strip is found in the endodermal cells."
"bio_0481","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which of the following plant hormones is primarily responsible for promoting cell elongation in stems?","Abscisic acid","Gibberellin","Ethylene","Cytokinin","B","Gibberellin promotes stem elongation."
"bio_0482","Biology","Zoology - Circulation","Fish","In which animal does the heart pump only deoxygenated blood?","Frog","Lizard","Fish","Pigeon","C","Fish heart pumps only deoxygenated blood."
"bio_0483","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Echinodermata","Which phylum is characterized by the presence of a water vascular system used for locomotion?","Mollusca","Annelida","Echinodermata","Arthropoda","C","Echinoderms have a water vascular system."
"bio_0484","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip is a characteristic feature found in the","Cortex of root","Endodermis of root","Pericycle of stem","Epidermis of leaf","B","Casparian strip occurs in root endodermis."
"bio_0486","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The casparian strip is a characteristic feature of which plant tissue?","Cortex","Epidermis","Endodermis","Pericycle","C","Casparian strip is found in the endodermal cells."
"bio_0487","Biology","Zoology - Endocrine System","Arthropods","Which hormone is primarily responsible for stimulating the molting process in arthropods?","Ecdysone","Insulin","Vasopressin","Oxytocin","A","Ecdysone triggers molting in arthropods."
"bio_0488","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which of the following plant hormones is primarily responsible for apical dominance?","Auxin","Cytokinin","Gibberellin","Ethylene","A","Auxin maintains apical dominance."
"bio_0489","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Tissue","In which plant tissue are companion cells associated with sieve tube elements?","Xylem","Phloem","Collenchyma","Epidermis","B","Companion cells occur beside sieve tubes in phloem."
"bio_0490","Biology","Zoology - Endocrine System","Amphibians","Which hormone is primarily responsible for metamorphosis in frogs?","Insulin","Thyroxine","Adrenaline","Glucagon","B","Thyroxine controls metamorphosis in tadpoles."
"bio_0491","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis","Which of the following statements regarding C4 plants is correct?","They have Kranz anatomy in their leaves","They utilize only the Calvin cycle for carbon fixation","They are less efficient than C3 plants under high light intensity","They exhibit high rates of photorespiration","A","C4 plants possess Kranz anatomy."
"bio_0492","Biology","Human Physiology","Nervous System","In mammals, which structure is primarily responsible for the production of cerebrospinal fluid?","Pineal gland","Choroid plexus","Thalamus","Corpus callosum","B","Choroid plexus secretes cerebrospinal fluid."
"bio_0493","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","In which part of the nephron does selective reabsorption of glucose primarily occur?","Proximal convoluted tubule","Distal convoluted tubule","Collecting duct","Loop of Henle","A","Glucose is reabsorbed in the proximal convoluted tubule."
"bio_0494","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is mainly responsible for the initiation of seed dormancy?","Abscisic acid","Gibberellin","Auxin","Cytokinin","A","Abscisic acid induces seed dormancy."
"bio_0495","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","Which of the following structures is responsible for the absorption of water and minerals in the root of a plant?","Root cap","Root hair","Pericycle","Endodermis","B","Root hairs absorb water and minerals."
"bio_0496","Biology","Human Physiology","Nervous System","In mammals, which part of the brain is primarily responsible for thermoregulation?","Medulla oblongata","Hypothalamus","Cerebellum","Pineal gland","B","Hypothalamus controls body temperature."
"bio_0497","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Mammals","Which of the following animals is oviparous?","Cow","Kangaroo","Platypus","Bat","C","Platypus lays eggs (oviparous mammal)."
"bio_0498","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","Which of the following is a distinguishing feature of dicot stem when observed in a transverse section?","Vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Scattered vascular bundles","Absence of cambium","Closed vascular bundles","A","Dicot stems have vascular bundles in a ring."
"bio_0499","Biology","Plant Reproduction","Seed Structure","Which structure in a dicot seed is primarily responsible for storing food reserves for the developing embryo?","Endosperm","Cotyledons","Radicle","Testa","B","Cotyledons store food in dicot seeds."
"bio_0500","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Amphibians","In which of the following animal groups does external fertilization commonly occur?","Reptiles","Amphibians","Mammals","Birds","B","Amphibians exhibit external fertilization."
"bio_0501","Biology","Plant Reproduction","Seed Development","Which one of the following pairs is correctly matched with respect to their function in flowering plants?","Phloem – Transport of water and minerals","Xylem – Transport of organic food","Endosperm – Nutrition for developing embryo","Stomata – Absorption of water","C","Endosperm nourishes the developing embryo."
"bio_0502","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip, a characteristic feature in plant roots, is mainly composed of which substance?","Lignin","Cutin","Suberin","Cellulose","C","Casparian strip contains suberin."
"bio_0503","Biology","Plant Morphology","Placentation","Which type of placentation is found in the ovary of a tomato plant?","Axile","Parietal","Basal","Free central","A","Tomato shows axile placentation."
"bio_0504","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Echinodermata","In which phylum do animals exhibit a water vascular system used for locomotion and food capture?","Annelida","Echinodermata","Arthropoda","Mollusca","B","Echinoderms use a water vascular system."
"bio_0505","Biology","Human Physiology","Reproductive System","In mammals, which structure prevents polyspermy during fertilization?","Zona pellucida","Amnion","Chorion","Allantois","A","Zona pellucida blocks additional sperm entry."
"bio_0506","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Monocot Stem Structure","Which of the following features is unique to monocot stems but not found in dicot stems?","Vascular bundles are scattered","Presence of cambium","Secondary growth","Vascular bundles are arranged in a ring","A","Monocot stems have scattered vascular bundles."
"bio_0507","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot leaf anatomy but not monocot leaf anatomy?","Presence of stomata on both surfaces","Parallel venation","Isobilateral symmetry","Palisade parenchyma present below the upper epidermis","D","Dicot leaves have palisade parenchyma below the epidermis."
"bio_0508","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Amphibians","In which animal does fertilization occur externally in water, and the development is indirect?","Frog","Earthworm","Pigeon","Rabbit","A","Frog shows external fertilization and indirect development."
"bio_0509","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which of the following features is characteristic of dicot leaf anatomy but not monocot leaf anatomy?","Presence of bulliform cells","Parallel venation","Isobilateral leaf structure","Palisade parenchyma layer","D","Dicot leaves contain palisade tissue for photosynthesis."
"bio_0510","Biology","Human Physiology","Nervous System","In mammals, which structure is responsible for the production of cerebrospinal fluid?","Choroid plexus","Pia mater","Arachnoid villi","Dura mater","A","Choroid plexus secretes cerebrospinal fluid."
"bio_0511","Biology","Plant Morphology","Floral Formula","Which one of the following is a floral formula for a hypogynous flower with actinomorphic symmetry and five free petals?","⊕ K5 C5 A5 G(5)","⊕ K(5) C5 A5 G1","⊕ K5 C5 A5 G1","⚥ K(5) C(5) A5 G(2)","C","Actinomorphic hypogynous flower has ⊕ K5 C5 A5 G1 formula."
"bio_0512","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Amphibians","In frogs, which structure acts as the primary organ of excretion?","Malpighian tubules","Cloaca","Green glands","Kidneys","D","Frog excretes urea through kidneys."
"bio_0513","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot stem observed in T.S. (transverse section)?","Scattered vascular bundles","Closed vascular bundles","Presence of cambium between xylem and phloem","Absence of endodermis","C","Cambium between xylem and phloem allows secondary growth."
"bio_0514","Biology","Human Physiology","Endocrine System","Which hormone is primarily responsible for stimulating milk ejection (let-down reflex) in mammals?","Prolactin","Oxytocin","Progesterone","Estrogen","B","Oxytocin causes milk ejection in mammals."
"bio_0515","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Tissue","In which of the following plant tissues are companion cells associated?","Xylem vessels","Phloem sieve tubes","Cork cambium","Trichomes","B","Companion cells assist sieve tubes in transport."
"bio_0517","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which tissue is mainly responsible for the increase in girth of dicot stems?","Cork cambium","Intercalary meristem","Vascular cambium","Apical meristem","C","Vascular cambium adds secondary xylem and phloem."
"bio_0518","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Annelids","The excretory organ of earthworm is","Malpighian tubules","Green glands","Nephridia","Flame cells","C","Earthworm excretes via nephridia."
"bio_0519","Biology","Plant Morphology","Stem Modification","Which of the following is a modification of the stem for vegetative propagation in ginger?","Rhizome","Tuber","Corm","Bulb","A","Ginger propagates through rhizomes."
"bio_0520","Biology","Cell Biology","Cell Enzymes","Which enzyme is responsible for the breakdown of hydrogen peroxide in animal cells?","Catalase","Amylase","Pepsin","Lipase","A","Catalase breaks hydrogen peroxide into water and oxygen."
"bio_0521","Biology","Plant Reproduction","Double Fertilisation","In which group of plants does double fertilization occur?","Bryophytes","Gymnosperms","Pteridophytes","Angiosperms","D","Double fertilization occurs in angiosperms."
"bio_0522","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Insects","Which of the following is the primary nitrogenous excretory product in most aquatic insects?","Uric acid","Ammonia","Urea","Creatinine","B","Aquatic insects excrete ammonia."
