"bio_0525","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis","Which of the following is the major photosynthetic pigment in green plants?","Chlorophyll a","Carotene","Xanthophyll","Chlorophyll b","A","Chlorophyll a is the chief photosynthetic pigment."
"bio_0527","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","In dicot stems, the vascular bundles are characterized by being","Closed and scattered","Open and arranged in a ring","Closed and arranged in a ring","Open and scattered","B","Dicot stems have open vascular bundles in a ring."
"bio_0528","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip found in endodermal cells of plant roots is mainly composed of","Cutin","Lignin","Suberin","Cellulose","C","Casparian strip contains suberin in endodermis."
"bio_0529","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","Which one of the following is a characteristic feature of dicotyledonous stems?","Scattered vascular bundles","Closed vascular bundles","Vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Absence of cambium","C","Dicot stems show ring-shaped vascular bundles."
"bio_0530","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","In mammals, which structure acts as the functional unit of the kidney?","Nephron","Alveolus","Neuron","Hepatocyte","A","Nephron is the functional unit of kidney."
"bio_0531","Biology","Plant Physiology","Nitrogen Fixation","The process by which root nodules are formed in leguminous plants involves which of the following bacteria?","Azotobacter","Rhizobium","Clostridium","Nitrosomonas","B","Rhizobium forms nitrogen-fixing nodules."
"bio_0532","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which of the following hormones is responsible for apical dominance in plants?","Gibberellin","Cytokinin","Auxin","Ethylene","C","Auxin suppresses lateral buds, causing apical dominance."
