"bio_0613","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Amphibians","In which animal does external fertilization typically occur?","Frog","Dog","Cow","Human","A","Frogs show external fertilization."
"bio_0614","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for the elongation of stem cells?","Gibberellin","Cytokinin","Abscisic acid","Ethylene","A","Gibberellin promotes stem elongation."
"bio_0615","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Annelida","Which animal shows metameric segmentation throughout its body?","Earthworm","Cockroach","Snail","Leech","A","Earthworms have segmented bodies."
"bio_0616","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Platyhelminthes","In which animal is flame cell the excretory structure?","Planaria","Earthworm","Cockroach","Frog","A","Planaria excretes via flame cells."
"bio_0617","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which of the following is the main photosynthetic tissue in the leaf of higher plants?","Palisade parenchyma","Collenchyma","Xylem","Epidermis","A","Palisade parenchyma performs photosynthesis."
"bio_0619","Biology","Plant Reproduction","Seed Structure","Which of the following is a non-endospermic (exalbuminous) seed?","Castor","Wheat","Pea","Maize","C","Pea is a non-endospermic seed."
"bio_0620","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem Structure","Which of the following is a distinguishing feature of dicotyledonous stems when viewed in transverse section?","Scattered vascular bundles","Vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Absence of pith","Closed vascular bundles","B","Dicot stems have vascular bundles in a ring."
"bio_0622","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Arthropods","In which of the following animals is the excretory organ called Malpighian tubules?","Earthworm","Prawn","Cockroach","Frog","C","Cockroach excretes through Malpighian tubules."
"bio_0623","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Aves","Which one of the following is the main nitrogenous waste excreted by birds?","Ammonia","Urea","Uric acid","Creatinine","C","Birds excrete uric acid to conserve water."
"bio_0624","Biology","Plant Morphology","Stem Modification","Which of the following plants exhibits phylloclade as an adaptation for photosynthesis in arid regions?","Opuntia","Pisum","Mustard","Mango","A","Opuntia uses phylloclade for photosynthesis in dry areas."
"bio_0625","Biology","Cell Biology","Meiosis","In which phase of meiosis does crossing over between homologous chromosomes occur?","Anaphase I","Metaphase II","Pachytene","Telophase I","C","Crossing over occurs during pachytene stage."
"bio_0626","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Tissue","Which of the following is the main function of companion cells in angiosperms?","Transport of water","Support of sieve tube elements","Loading and unloading of sugars","Storage of starch","C","Companion cells manage sugar transport in phloem."
"bio_0627","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Arthropods","In which animal is the malpighian tubule the chief excretory organ?","Leech","Earthworm","Cockroach","Frog","C","Cockroach excretes via Malpighian tubules."
"bio_0628","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which one of the following is the main photosynthetic tissue in a typical dicot leaf?","Spongy parenchyma","Palisade parenchyma","Epidermis","Collenchyma","B","Palisade parenchyma carries out photosynthesis."
"bio_0629","Biology","Plant Morphology","Inflorescence","Which one of the following pairs is correctly matched regarding the type of inflorescence and its example?","Racemose – Sunflower","Cymose – Nerium","Spike – Bougainvillea","Umbel – Wheat","B","Nerium shows cymose inflorescence."
"bio_0630","Biology","Zoology - Circulation","Fishes","In which animal does blood flow through the heart only once during one complete circuit of the body?","Frog","Pigeon","Shark","Rabbit","C","Fish heart has single circulation."
"bio_0631","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for promoting seed dormancy?","Auxin","Gibberellin","Abscisic acid","Cytokinin","C","Abscisic acid induces seed dormancy."
"bio_0632","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Platyhelminthes","In which phylum are flame cells primarily involved in excretion?","Annelida","Platyhelminthes","Arthropoda","Mollusca","B","Flame cells occur in flatworms for excretion."
"bio_0633","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Xylem Tissue","Which of the following tissues is responsible for the movement of water and minerals from roots to leaves in angiosperms?","Phloem","Collenchyma","Xylem","Sclerenchyma","C","Xylem conducts water and minerals upward."
"bio_0634","Biology","Zoology - Classification","Mammals","Which of the following is a distinguishing feature of mammals among vertebrates?","Presence of air sacs in lungs","External fertilization","Hair on body","Cloaca for excretion","C","Hair is a defining mammalian trait."
"bio_0636","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Tissue","In which plant tissue are companion cells found closely associated with sieve tube elements?","Xylem","Phloem","Cambium","Pericycle","B","Companion cells occur with sieve tubes in phloem."
"bio_0637","Biology","Zoology - Endocrine System","Amphibians","The hormone responsible for inducing metamorphosis in amphibians is","Cortisol","Thyroxine","Adrenaline","Insulin","B","Thyroxine triggers metamorphosis in frogs."
"bio_0638","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","In mammals, the primary function of the loop of Henle in the nephron is to","Filter blood plasma","Concentrate urine","Secrete hormones","Reabsorb glucose","B","Loop of Henle concentrates urine."
"bio_0639","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem","Which one of the following is NOT a characteristic feature of dicot stems?","Vascular bundles are arranged in a ring","Presence of cambium","Closed vascular bundles","Presence of hypodermis","C","Dicot stems have open vascular bundles."
"bio_0640","Biology","Plant Morphology","Floral Structure","In which of the following plant families are zygomorphic flowers commonly found?","Fabaceae","Poaceae","Solanaceae","Brassicaceae","A","Fabaceae flowers are zygomorphic."
"bio_0641","Biology","Human Physiology","Endocrine System","Which hormone is primarily responsible for stimulating milk ejection (let-down) in mammalian females?","Prolactin","Oxytocin","Vasopressin","Estrogen","B","Oxytocin causes milk ejection."
"bio_0642","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which of the following plant hormones is primarily responsible for the closing of stomata during water stress?","Auxin","Ethylene","Abscisic acid","Gibberellin","C","Abscisic acid closes stomata during drought."
"bio_0643","Biology","Human Physiology","Nervous System","In mammals, the structure responsible for the production of cerebrospinal fluid is","Choroid plexus","Pia mater","Corpus callosum","Medulla oblongata","A","Choroid plexus secretes cerebrospinal fluid."
"bio_0644","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis","Which of the following is a C4 plant adapted for high photosynthetic efficiency in tropical climates?","Wheat","Rice","Maize","Potato","C","Maize is a C4 plant with Kranz anatomy."
"bio_0645","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which of the following plant hormones is primarily responsible for the ripening of fruits?","Auxin","Gibberellin","Ethylene","Cytokinin","C","Ethylene accelerates fruit ripening."
"bio_0646","Biology","Plant Morphology","Stem Modification","Which one of the following plants exhibits phylloclade as its stem modification for photosynthesis?","Opuntia","Potato","Pea","Onion","A","Opuntia stem is modified into phylloclade."
"bio_0647","Biology","Zoology - Endocrine System","Arthropods","Which hormone is primarily responsible for the molting process in arthropods?","Thyroxine","Ecdysone","Gibberellin","Insulin","B","Ecdysone controls molting in arthropods."
"bio_0648","Biology","Zoology - Classification","Mammals","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of mammals but not of birds?","Three-chambered heart","External ears (pinnae)","Warm-bloodedness","Lungs with air sacs","B","Mammals have external ears."
"bio_0649","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for promoting the elongation of stems?","Gibberellin","Abscisic acid","Ethylene","Cytokinin","A","Gibberellin promotes stem elongation."
"bio_0651","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which of the following cells in plants is responsible for the opening and closing of stomata?","Trichome cells","Guard cells","Companion cells","Sieve tube cells","B","Guard cells regulate stomatal movement."
"bio_0652","Biology","Human Physiology","Nervous System","In mammals, which part of the brain is primarily responsible for regulating body temperature?","Cerebellum","Hypothalamus","Medulla oblongata","Cerebrum","B","Hypothalamus controls temperature."
"bio_0653","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","In mammals, which organ is primarily responsible for the production of urea?","Liver","Kidney","Pancreas","Spleen","A","Liver converts ammonia to urea."
"bio_0654","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","In dicot stems, the cambium responsible for secondary growth originates from which tissue?","Pericycle","Endodermis","Medullary rays","Vascular bundles","D","Cambium arises between vascular bundles."
"bio_0655","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Amphibians","Which one of the following organisms exhibits external fertilization?","Frog","Hen","Rabbit","Dog","A","Frog performs external fertilization in water."
"bio_0656","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Aschelminthes","In which phylum does the body cavity (coelom) arise between the mesoderm and endoderm?","Annelida","Aschelminthes","Arthropoda","Echinodermata","B","Aschelminthes have a pseudocoelom."
"bio_0657","Biology","Zoology - Endocrine System","Amphibians","Which of the following hormones is primarily responsible for the metamorphosis of tadpoles into adult frogs?","Insulin","Thyroxine","Cortisol","Aldosterone","B","Thyroxine induces metamorphosis."
"bio_0658","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which of the following plant hormones is primarily responsible for promoting the elongation of stems?","Gibberellin","Abscisic acid","Ethylene","Cytokinin","A","Gibberellin stimulates elongation."
"bio_0659","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","In mammals, the renal corpuscle is composed of which two structures?","Loop of Henle and collecting duct","Bowman’s capsule and glomerulus","Proximal tubule and distal tubule","Ureter and urinary bladder","B","Renal corpuscle has glomerulus and Bowman’s capsule."
"bio_0661","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Arachnida","In which group of animals does respiration occur through book lungs?","Insects","Crustaceans","Arachnids","Annelids","C","Arachnids respire via book lungs."
"bio_0662","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot stem in T.S. (transverse section)?","Scattered vascular bundles","Closed vascular bundles","Vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Absence of cambium","C","Dicot stems show vascular bundles in a ring."
"bio_0663","Biology","Human Physiology","Digestive System","Which of the following is not a function of the liver in mammals?","Bile production","Urea synthesis","Detoxification","Insulin secretion","D","Insulin is secreted by the pancreas, not liver."
"bio_0664","Biology","Human Physiology","Endocrine System","Which hormone is primarily responsible for stimulating the development of secondary sexual characteristics in males?","Progesterone","Estrogen","Testosterone","Oxytocin","C","Testosterone controls male secondary traits."
"bio_0665","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","In a typical mammalian nephron, where does maximum reabsorption of glomerular filtrate occur?","Distal convoluted tubule","Collecting duct","Proximal convoluted tubule","Loop of Henle","C","Most reabsorption occurs in PCT."
"bio_0666","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Echinodermata","Which phylum is characterized by the presence of a water vascular system used for locomotion and feeding?","Cnidaria","Echinodermata","Annelida","Arthropoda","B","Echinoderms possess a water vascular system."
"bio_0667","Biology","Cell Biology","Mitosis","In which phase of mitosis do the sister chromatids separate and move towards opposite poles in a plant cell?","Prophase","Metaphase","Anaphase","Telophase","C","Sister chromatids separate in anaphase."
"bio_0668","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis","Which of the following is an example of a xerophyte that shows CAM (Crassulacean Acid Metabolism) photosynthesis?","Opuntia","Hydrilla","Pisum","Oryza","A","Opuntia shows CAM photosynthesis."
"bio_0670","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Root","Which one of the following is a characteristic feature of dicotyledonous roots, but not monocotyledonous roots?","Pith is large and well developed","Secondary growth is absent","Xylem is arranged in a ring","Vascular bundles are usually tetrarch or pentarch","D","Dicot roots are tetrarch or pentarch."
"bio_0672","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Platyhelminthes","In which animal is the flame cell a specialized excretory structure?","Earthworm","Cockroach","Planaria","Frog","C","Planaria excretes through flame cells."
"bio_0673","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem","Which one of the following is a characteristic feature of dicotyledonous stem but not monocotyledonous stem?","Vascular bundles are scattered","Vascular bundles are closed","Presence of cambium in vascular bundles","Absence of cortex","C","Dicot stems have cambium for secondary growth."
"bio_0675","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","In mammals, the portion of the nephron where maximum reabsorption of glucose occurs is the","Distal convoluted tubule","Proximal convoluted tubule","Loop of Henle","Collecting duct","B","Glucose reabsorbed in proximal convoluted tubule."
"bio_0676","Biology","Human Physiology","Immune System","Which of the following cells in human blood is responsible for antibody production?","Neutrophil","Basophil","B lymphocyte","Erythrocyte","C","B lymphocytes produce antibodies."
"bio_0677","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","In which part of the leaf does the maximum photosynthetic activity occur?","Upper epidermis","Palisade parenchyma","Spongy parenchyma","Lower epidermis","B","Palisade layer performs most photosynthesis."
"bio_0678","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Tissue","Which of the following is the primary function of companion cells in phloem tissue?","Transport of water","Providing mechanical support","Assisting sieve tube elements in translocation","Storing starch","C","Companion cells help sieve tubes in translocation."
"bio_0679","Biology","Plant Morphology","Inflorescence","Which type of inflorescence is characterized by the youngest flowers being at the base and older flowers towards the apex?","Racemose","Cymose","Capitulum","Spadix","A","Racemose inflorescence has youngest at base."
"bio_0681","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis","Which of the following is a C4 plant that exhibits Kranz anatomy?","Rice","Sugarcane","Wheat","Bean","B","Sugarcane is a C4 plant with Kranz anatomy."
"bio_0682","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Insects","The Malpighian tubules in insects are primarily responsible for which physiological process?","Digestion","Excretion","Respiration","Reproduction","B","Malpighian tubules excrete nitrogenous waste."
"bio_0683","Biology","Zoology - Circulation","Amphibians","Which structure in the frog’s heart prevents the mixing of oxygenated and deoxygenated blood?","Sinus venosus","Truncus arteriosus","Interatrial septum","Spiral valve","D","Spiral valve prevents blood mixing in frog heart."
"bio_0684","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Cnidaria","In which phylum do animals possess stinging cells called cnidocytes?","Porifera","Annelida","Cnidaria","Platyhelminthes","C","Cnidarians have stinging cnidocytes."
"bio_0685","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot stem in T.S.?","Scattered vascular bundles","Open vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Closed vascular bundles","Absence of cambium","B","Dicot stems have open bundles in a ring."
"bio_0687","Biology","Cell Biology","Photorespiration","Which of the following cell organelles is responsible for photorespiration in plants?","Peroxisome","Golgi apparatus","Mitochondria","Ribosome","A","Photorespiration occurs in peroxisomes."
"bio_0689","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which of the following is the main function of guard cells in plant leaves?","Absorption of water","Regulation of gas exchange","Transport of nutrients","Photosynthesis","B","Guard cells control gas exchange."
"bio_0690","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","Which part of the nephron is primarily responsible for the selective reabsorption of glucose from the filtrate?","Bowman’s capsule","Proximal convoluted tubule","Loop of Henle","Distal convoluted tubule","B","Glucose reabsorbed in proximal convoluted tubule."
"bio_0691","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Xylem Tissue","Which of the following cells in plants is mainly responsible for the transport of water and minerals?","Sieve tube elements","Tracheids","Companion cells","Phloem fibers","B","Tracheids conduct water and minerals."
"bio_0692","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","In mammals, which organ is primarily responsible for the filtration of nitrogenous wastes from the blood?","Liver","Kidney","Lungs","Spleen","B","Kidney filters nitrogenous wastes."
"bio_0693","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem","Which one of the following is a characteristic feature of dicot stems but not monocot stems?","Vascular bundles are arranged in a ring","Scattered vascular bundles","Presence of bulliform cells","Absence of cambium","A","Dicot stems have vascular bundles in a ring."
"bio_0694","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Insects","The malpighian tubules in insects primarily function in","Respiration","Excretion","Digestion","Circulation","B","Malpighian tubules excrete nitrogenous waste."
"bio_0695","Biology","Plant Classification","Gymnosperms","In which group of plants would you find seeds but no flowers?","Bryophytes","Gymnosperms","Pteridophytes","Angiosperms","B","Gymnosperms have naked seeds without flowers."
"bio_0696","Biology","Human Physiology","Muscular System","Which of the following is the functional unit of contractile tissue in mammals?","Sarcomere","Neuron","Osteon","Nephron","A","Sarcomere is the basic unit of muscle contraction."
"bio_0698","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis","Which one of the following is a C4 plant?","Wheat","Rice","Maize","Pea","C","Maize follows the C4 photosynthetic pathway."
"bio_0699","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Xylem Tissue","Which of the following is the main water-conducting tissue in gymnosperms?","Vessels","Tracheids","Sieve tubes","Companion cells","B","Gymnosperms conduct water mainly through tracheids."
"bio_0700","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of dicotyledonous stem in T.S.?","Scattered vascular bundles","Closed vascular bundles","Vascular bundles arranged in a ring","Absence of cambium","C","Dicot stems show vascular bundles in a ring."
"bio_0701","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Amphibians","Which of the following animals is correctly matched with its excretory organ?","Earthworm – Malpighian tubules","Cockroach – Nephridia","Frog – Kidneys","Planaria – Green glands","C","Frog excretes through kidneys."
"bio_0702","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip found in endodermal cells of roots is primarily composed of","Cellulose","Suberin","Lignin","Pectin","B","Casparian strip is made of suberin."
"bio_0704","Biology","Human Physiology","Muscular System","Which of the following is the correct sequence of events in the process of muscle contraction in vertebrates?","Release of calcium ions → ATP hydrolysis → Cross-bridge formation → Sliding of actin","ATP hydrolysis → Cross-bridge detachment → Calcium release → Sliding of actin","Release of calcium ions → Cross-bridge formation → Sliding of actin → ATP hydrolysis","ATP hydrolysis → Release of calcium ions → Sliding of actin → Cross-bridge formation","A","Muscle contraction starts with calcium release followed by ATP-driven cross-bridge movement."
"bio_0705","Biology","Plant Physiology","Plant Hormones","Which plant hormone is primarily responsible for the elongation of internodes in deepwater rice?","Ethylene","Gibberellin","Cytokinin","Abscisic acid","B","Gibberellin promotes internode elongation in deepwater rice."
"bio_0706","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Annelids","Which structure in earthworms serves as the site for sperm storage after copulation?","Seminal vesicle","Cocoon","Seminal receptacle","Clitellum","C","Sperms are stored in seminal receptacles after mating."
"bio_0707","Biology","Plant Ecology","Adaptations","Which one of the following is an example of a xerophytic adaptation in plants?","Presence of hydathodes","Thick cuticle on leaves","Aerenchyma tissue","Stomata on upper surface only","B","Thick cuticle reduces water loss in xerophytes."
"bio_0708","Biology","Zoology - Endocrine System","Insects","Which hormone primarily regulates molting in insects?","Ecdysone","Insulin","Gibberellin","Oxytocin","A","Ecdysone controls molting in insects."
"bio_0709","Biology","Human Physiology","Nervous System","In mammals, the corpus callosum connects which of the following structures?","The two cerebral hemispheres","Cerebellum and medulla oblongata","Pons and spinal cord","Thalamus and hypothalamus","A","Corpus callosum connects the cerebral hemispheres."
"bio_0710","Biology","Plant Reproduction","Fertilization","In which of the following plants would you most likely observe the phenomenon of double fertilization?","Pinus","Cycas","Mango","Marchantia","C","Double fertilization occurs only in angiosperms like mango."
"bio_0711","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","Which structure in a mammalian nephron is primarily responsible for the filtration of blood?","Loop of Henle","Bowman’s capsule","Collecting duct","Distal convoluted tubule","B","Bowman’s capsule filters blood in the nephron."
"bio_0713","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem","Which of the following is a feature of dicotyledonous stem but not of monocotyledonous stem?","Presence of scattered vascular bundles","Presence of cambium between xylem and phloem","Closed vascular bundles","Absence of cortex","B","Dicot stems have cambium for secondary growth."
"bio_0715","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Arthropoda","Which of the following is a characteristic feature of members belonging to Phylum Arthropoda?","Presence of flame cells","Unsegmented body","Jointed appendages","Cilia for locomotion","C","Arthropods have segmented bodies with jointed legs."
"bio_0716","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which tissue in dicot stems is responsible for the formation of annual rings?","Phloem","Cork cambium","Vascular cambium","Epidermis","C","Vascular cambium forms annual rings."
"bio_0719","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Tissue","Which of the following tissues in plants is responsible for the transport of organic solutes from leaves to other parts of the plant?","Xylem","Phloem","Collenchyma","Sclerenchyma","B","Phloem transports food materials."
"bio_0720","Biology","Human Physiology","Excretory System","In mammals, which part of the nephron is primarily responsible for selective reabsorption of glucose and amino acids?","Bowman’s capsule","Loop of Henle","Proximal convoluted tubule","Distal convoluted tubule","C","PCT reabsorbs glucose and amino acids."
"bio_0721","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Echinodermata","Which phylum exhibits a water vascular system used primarily for locomotion and food capture?","Arthropoda","Mollusca","Echinodermata","Annelida","C","Echinoderms have a water vascular system."
"bio_0722","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Root","Which of the following is a distinguishing feature of dicot roots when compared to monocot roots?","Presence of pith in the center","Polyarch xylem","Exarch xylem arrangement","Absence of endodermis","C","Dicot roots show exarch xylem."
"bio_0723","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip, found in the endodermis of roots, is mainly composed of","Lignin and suberin","Cellulose and hemicellulose","Pectin and chitin","Cutin and wax","A","Casparian strips contain lignin and suberin."
"bio_0724","Biology","Human Anatomy","Epithelial Tissue","Which type of animal tissue lines the inner surface of blood vessels?","Cuboidal epithelium","Ciliated epithelium","Squamous epithelium","Columnar epithelium","C","Endothelium of blood vessels is squamous."
"bio_0725","Biology","Plant Morphology","Placentation","Which type of placentation is characterized by ovules attached to the central axis of a multilocular ovary?","Axile","Parietal","Marginal","Basal","A","Axile placentation has ovules on a central axis."
"bio_0726","Biology","Human Physiology","Circulatory System","The bundle of His is primarily responsible for","Generating action potentials in the SA node","Transmitting impulses from atria to ventricles","Preventing backflow of blood into atria","Stimulating contraction of the papillary muscles","B","Bundle of His conducts cardiac impulses."
"bio_0727","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Dicot Stem","Which of the following is characteristic of dicot stem but not of monocot stem?","Open vascular bundles","Scattered vascular bundles","Absence of endodermis","Presence of pith","A","Dicot stems have open vascular bundles."
"bio_0728","Biology","Human Physiology","Reproductive System","In mammals, which structure is primarily responsible for production of mature functional spermatozoa?","Seminiferous tubules","Vas deferens","Prostate gland","Epididymis","A","Sperm cells develop in seminiferous tubules."
"bio_0729","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Tissue","Which of the following is the main function of companion cells in phloem tissue of angiosperms?","Transport of water and minerals","Providing mechanical support","Assisting sieve tube elements in translocation","Storage of starch","C","Companion cells help sieve tubes in translocation."
"bio_0730","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Tissue","In which plant tissue would you find sieve tubes and companion cells?","Xylem","Phloem","Cork","Collenchyma","B","Phloem contains sieve tubes and companion cells."
"bio_0731","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis","Which of the following is the primary function of bundle sheath cells in C4 plants?","Transport of water","Storage of starch","Decarboxylation of malate","Absorption of minerals","C","Bundle sheath cells decarboxylate malate in C4 pathway."
"bio_0732","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","Which structure is responsible for the absorption of water and minerals in the root of a plant?","Root cap","Root hair","Pericycle","Vascular bundle","B","Root hairs absorb water and minerals."
"bio_0734","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which of the following is the main photosynthetic tissue in leaves of most dicotyledonous plants?","Palisade parenchyma","Collenchyma","Xylem","Sclerenchyma","A","Palisade parenchyma carries out photosynthesis."
"bio_0736","Biology","Plant Reproduction","Fertilization","The process of double fertilization in flowering plants results in the formation of","Two embryos","Endosperm and embryo","Two endosperms","Two zygotes","B","Double fertilization forms embryo and endosperm."
"bio_0738","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Annelids","Which of the following is the main excretory organ in earthworms?","Malpighian tubules","Nephridia","Green glands","Flame cells","B","Earthworms excrete through nephridia."
"bio_0739","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Monocot Stem","Which of the following is a distinguishing feature of monocotyledonous stems?","Vascular bundles are arranged in a ring","Secondary growth is common","Vascular bundles are scattered","Presence of cambium","C","Monocot stems have scattered vascular bundles."
"bio_0740","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Annelids","The primary excretory organ in annelids is known as","Malpighian tubule","Nephron","Nephridia","Green gland","C","Annelids excrete through nephridia."
"bio_0741","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip, which helps regulate the flow of water and minerals, is present in which plant tissue?","Endodermis","Pericycle","Epidermis","Cortex","A","Casparian strip is found in endodermis."
"bio_0742","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","The Casparian strip found in the endodermal cells of roots is mainly composed of","Lignin","Suberin","Cutin","Pectin","B","Casparian strip contains suberin."
"bio_0743","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Annelida","Which one of the following animals exhibits metameric segmentation?","Cockroach","Earthworm","Octopus","Snail","B","Earthworm shows metameric segmentation."
"bio_0745","Biology","Animal Physiology","Respiration","In which animal is the respiratory pigment haemocyanin found dissolved in plasma?","Frog","Cockroach","Earthworm","Octopus","D","Octopus has copper-based haemocyanin."
"bio_0746","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Xylem Tissue","Which plant tissue is responsible for the movement of water and minerals from roots to leaves?","Phloem","Xylem","Collenchyma","Cork","B","Xylem conducts water and minerals upward."
"bio_0747","Biology","Plant Morphology","Stem Modification","Which of the following plants exhibits phylloclade as an adaptation to arid environments?","Opuntia","Pisum","Mangifera","Solanum","A","Opuntia stem is modified into phylloclade."
"bio_0748","Biology","Human Anatomy","Epithelial Tissue","Which type of epithelium lines the inner surface of the urinary bladder in mammals?","Ciliated epithelium","Transitional epithelium","Stratified squamous epithelium","Cuboidal epithelium","B","Urinary bladder is lined with transitional epithelium."
"bio_0750","Biology","Human Physiology","Sensory System","Which part of the human ear is responsible for maintaining balance and equilibrium?","Cochlea","Pinna","Semicircular canals","Tympanic membrane","C","Semicircular canals maintain body balance."
