"bio_0767","Biology","Animal Kingdom","Amphibians","Which of the following animals exhibits metamorphosis during its development?","Earthworm","Frog","Pigeon","Rabbit","B","Frog undergoes metamorphosis from tadpole to adult."
"bio_0768","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","Casparian strips are characteristic features of which plant tissue?","Phloem","Cortex","Endodermis","Pericycle","C","Casparian strips occur in endodermal cells."
"bio_0769","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Annelids","Which of the following is the excretory organ in earthworm?","Malpighian tubules","Nephridia","Green glands","Flame cells","B","Earthworms excrete through nephridia."
"bio_0770","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Leaf Structure","Which of the following is the primary photosynthetic tissue in the leaf of a dicot plant?","Collenchyma","Palisade parenchyma","Sclerenchyma","Xylem","B","Palisade parenchyma performs photosynthesis."
"bio_0772","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Root Structure","Casparian strip is characteristic of which plant tissue?","Cortex","Endodermis","Pericycle","Phloem","B","Casparian strips are present in the endodermis."
"bio_0773","Biology","Zoology - Reproduction","Amphibians","Which one of the following animals is correctly matched with its mode of fertilization?","Frog – External fertilization","Earthworm – External fertilization","Bird – External fertilization","Dogfish – External fertilization","A","Frogs reproduce by external fertilization."
"bio_0774","Biology","Plant Morphology","Stem Modification","Which one of the following plants exhibits phylloclade as a modification for photosynthesis?","Opuntia","Pisum","Solanum","Helianthus","A","Opuntia stem is modified into phylloclade for photosynthesis."
"bio_0775","Biology","Zoology - Excretion","Amphibians","Which of the following is the primary nitrogenous waste excreted by adult amphibians?","Ammonia","Urea","Uric acid","Creatinine","B","Amphibians excrete urea as their main waste."
"bio_0776","Biology","Plant Physiology","Photosynthesis","Which one of the following is a C4 plant that exhibits Kranz anatomy?","Wheat","Rice","Maize","Pea","C","Maize is a C4 plant with Kranz anatomy."
