"bio_0789","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Phloem Transport","Which of the following statements about phloem transport in plants is correct?","Sucrose moves from sink to source","Companion cells assist in loading sugars into sieve tubes","Phloem translocates only inorganic nutrients","Movement through phloem is always passive","B","Companion cells load sugars into sieve tubes for transport."
"bio_0790","Biology","Plant Anatomy","Secondary Growth","Which structure in dicot stems is responsible for the formation of secondary xylem and secondary phloem?","Endodermis","Vascular cambium","Pericycle","Epidermis","B","Vascular cambium produces secondary xylem and phloem."
"bio_0792","Biology","Plant Morphology","Inflorescence","Which of the following types of inflorescence is characterized by the youngest flower being present at the base and the oldest at the apex?","Cymose","Racemose","Umbel","Spikelet","B","Racemose inflorescence has youngest flowers at the base."
